{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","prNumber":170,"prUrl":"https://github.com/Squidys-Tools/inkling/pull/170","prRepository":"Squidys-Tools/inkling","timestamp":"2026-10-20T11:42:12.168Z"}
{"parentUuid":"7afe5144-f0a7-48fd-8730-ed0a6b67f653","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[{"name":"mcp__t3-code__html_render","description":"Show a finished HTML page (chart, table, diagram, collage, mockup) inline in this thread, above your final text reply; call it before writing that reply. The reader already sees the page, so the reply should not announce it, say where it is, or restate it: add only what the page doesn't say. Preview with html_preview first. T3 fits the frame to the page's height at each reader's width. On mobile, a height below the page's contentHeight caps the frame there, and the rest scrolls inside it; web and desktop fit the whole page, up to 20000px. Write one self-contained document with inline <style> and <script>. Local images written as absolute file paths (src=\"/abs/shot.png\", CSS url(/abs/bg.webp), or a JS string) are inlined automatically; remote http(s) URLs, such as a CDN chart library, load as-is. The frame is borderless on the thread's background, as wide as the reply column (728px on desktop by default, wider if the reader widens chat, about 360px on phones), and its left edge lines up with your reply text. The page sits on the thread's own background, so by default leave html, body, and the outermost element with no background color. This overrides general style preferences such as a fixed black page background. Use a fluid width with no horizontal padding on the outermost element, and no outer card, border, or banner title: the page is part of your reply. If a box needs its own background (a mock of a specific screen, a panel that must stand apart), give it at least 16px of padding on every side and var(--radius) corners, so content never touches its edge. Give charts fixed pixel heights rather than heights that scale with width. Let content set the page's height. The frame grows to fit the page, so a height that follows the viewport makes it grow again and again: html_preview and html_render reject vh, svh, lvh, and dvh units, and height:100% on html or body has the same problem. T3 injects its active theme as CSS custom properties on :root, and they follow the user's theme and light/dark mode live: --background (page background, identical to the thread around the frame), --foreground, --muted, --muted-foreground, --card, --card-foreground, --popover, --popover-foreground, --secondary, --secondary-foreground, --border, --input, --ring, --primary, --primary-foreground (solid buttons), --accent, --accent-foreground (brand accent), --accent-surface, --accent-surface-foreground, --destructive, --destructive-foreground, --destructive-surface, --warning, --warning-foreground, --warning-surface, --success, --success-foreground, --info, --info-foreground, --code-background, --code-foreground, --chart-1 ... --chart-6 (categorical series for charts), --radius, --font-sans, --font-mono. The base stylesheet sets html background/color/font from these, body margin to 0, and hides the page's scrollbar; your own CSS overrides it.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"html":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":512000,"description":"A complete, self-contained HTML document."},"title":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"description":"Short name for the page."},"height":{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"The frame height in CSS pixels, 80-2000. Use html_preview's contentHeight. A lower height makes long content scroll inside the frame on mobile only."}},"required":["html","title","height"],"additionalProperties":true},"eager_input_streaming":true,"defer_loading":true}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"31b55a91-1348-4c91-b767-70395171ff43","timestamp":"2026-10-20T11:42:44.306Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"31b55a91-1348-4c91-b767-70395171ff43","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDRoLDNC1UNgg2CqH52K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm worried that having many Haiku subagents work in parallel will cause conflicting edits to shared files like App.tsx and App.css. A safer approach is to have one agent establish the foundational tokens and fonts first, then split remaining work into disjoint areas so parallel agents don't collide.\n\nI'll instruct subagents never to commit, never overwrite files with Write when edits could conflict, and never run destructive git commands like checkout or stash — I'll handle commits myself at the end after merging everyone's work. Since the user wants the UI to match the Paper designs exactly, I'll have agents pull fonts and styling directly from those reference screens.\n\nFor gaps where the app lacks real data behind the Paper design (palette swatches, video duration, disk size, version numbers, avatars), I'll tell agents to hide those elements rather than build new backend logic, and I'll flag these omissions to the user afterward. I also need to bundle the fonts (DM Sans, DM Mono, Libre Baskerville) locally via package dependencies to keep things local-first rather than pulling from Google Fonts, and note that the sidebar's mascot/wordmark doesn't appear in the Paper reference. Now I'm sketching the phased plan, starting with a sequential foundation phase for fonts and design tokens before parallelizing further work.\n\nFor the parallel phase, I'm dividing work between a sidebar agent handling nav rows, counts, blob markers, and footer details (deciding to keep the Help entry point reachable via a shortcut key even if its row gets removed), and a toolbar/header agent handling the floating search pill, glass capsule controls, and card scroll behavior.\n\nFor the remaining agents: one covers grid and card layout (column width, gaps, insets, and the various card types like article, quote, note, video, file), another handles item view details like Info/Similar tabs, the inspector grid, stage navigation, and action bar, and I'm considering splitting off a separate agent for zoom/original-asset loading since that touches backend data paths more than pure styling.\n\nSettings and archive get their own agent with everything listed, and I'm debating whether mascot travel timing deserves a dedicated low-priority agent or just a mention in the report since it's unverified.\n\nI also need to resolve overlaps — scroll-under-toolbar behavior belongs to the layout/grid agent while grid sizing stays separate, and the sidebar collapse button position should be owned by the sidebar agent rather than duplicated elsewhere.\n\nFor the Similar tab versus the library-wide find-similar mode, I'm leaning toward replacing the old \"Find similar\" button with the new tab entirely, treating the library-wide code path as something cleanup can remove later rather than preserving both.\n\nI need each Haiku subagent to have access to the Paper MCP tools, and I'll start a single shared dev server myself rather than having every agent spin one up. Since multiple agents screenshotting concurrently through one preview browser could conflict, I'll have them verify mostly through code review and limit screenshots to a final QA pass.\n\nFor cleanup, given the user's cost concerns, I'll delegate it to a Haiku agent at xhigh effort followed by a separate QA comparison agent, rather than reviewing the diff myself, then commit once that's done.\n\nFirst I need to start the dev server and check the port, running phase 1 in the foreground since the other phases depend on it and this saves time overall.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":124606,"cache_read_input_tokens":15387,"output_tokens":2649,"output_tokens_details":{"