{"parentUuid":"d5664866-de0b-4b06-8648-e03f60e700b7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDRv84p8ujiWjjThmaCw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The non-design pieces here—palette swatches, video duration, disk size, version info, show-in-folder IPC, original-image-on-zoom IPC—should go to Luna rather than me. I'll note this briefly and wait for the foundation work to finish first.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1637,"cache_read_input_tokens":146084,"output_tokens":789,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":82},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1637,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":789,"cache_read_input_tokens":146084,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1637,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1637},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7906,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgDRv4tpXycj2eKdYE7Fs","requestRef":"f0a709bd-c842-4490-becf-e01038208850","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"22d184a3-9baa-479c-a623-cdff0c83f0a0","timestamp":"2026-10-20T11:43:53.679Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"22d184a3-9baa-479c-a623-cdff0c83f0a0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDRv84p8ujiWjjThmaCw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The plan, so you can stop me before wave 2 starts:\n\n**Wave 1 (running now):** one Haiku is bundling DM Sans and DM Mono locally and adding Paper's colour, radius and spacing values, including the 232px sidebar. All the screen work builds on this, so it goes first.\n\n**Wave 2 (Haiku, in parallel once wave 1 lands):** each agent owns one area so they don't edit each other's parts.\n1. **Sidebar:** the blot-only logo, Paper's icons and rows, formatted counts, a count on every Space, coloured blobs, the footer and the collapse tab.\n2. **Toolbar and search:** glass capsules top-left, cards scrolling under the toolbar, the floating search pill, the search drop-in and the pinned query chip, the Add pill, and the results count.\n3. **Grid and cards:** the 286px columns and spacing, plus the article, quote, note, PDF, video and file cards.\n4. **Item view:** the Info/Similar tabs with the similar grid inside the side panel, glass back/forward on the photo, the full action bar and the inspector type.\n5. **Settings and Archive:** both panels and the archive tiles with Restore.\n\n**Backend work for GPT-6 Luna in parallel, since it isn't design:**\n- disk size and app version for Settings;\n- a \"show in folder\" call and a \"last export\" date that survives restarts;\n- loading the original image when you zoom in;\n- storing colour swatches and video length.\n\nThe Haiku agents will hook into these as they land.\n\n**Wave 3:** one agent cleans up and optimises the combined changes, then another compares the running app against every Paper screen. I'll send the remaining gaps back out for fixes, and only commit once it matches.\n\nI'm making three calls myself, since you said \"exactly like Paper\":\n- **Paper's fonts:** these replace the all-mono look.\n- **Similar tab:** it replaces the \"Find similar\" button.\n- **Avatar:** I'm leaving it out. It implies an account, and the app has no accounts.\n\nIf you'd rather go the other way on any of these, say so before wave 2 starts."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1637,"cache_read_input_tokens":146084,"output_tokens":789,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":82},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1637,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":789,"cache_read_input_tokens":146084,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1637,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1637},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgDRv4tpXycj2eKdYE7Fs","requestRef":"f0a709bd-c842-4490-becf-e01038208850","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"15b7c4de-7296-4cf5-9291-d2901f313020","timestamp":"2026-10-20T11:43:53.738Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-20T11:46:08.781Z","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a85d13cff9b0bece2</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_015WcksPX1Ly4hj4tfWwXGz9</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-chris--t3-worktrees-inkling-t3-47ff5304\\fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7\\tasks\\a85d13cff9b0bece2.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Foundation: fonts + tokens\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Wave 1 foundation is in the working tree, uncommitted. The main deviation: the default UI font is system-ui, not DM Sans, because Paper's own labels use system-ui.\n\n**Packages added**\n- `@fontsource-variable/dm-sans@5.3.0` (variable, wght axis). The brief named `@fontsource/dm-sans`, but a variable build exists, so I used it. Its family name is \"DM Sans Variable\".\n- `@fontsource/dm-mono@5.3.0`, weight 400 only, which is the only DM Mono weight I found in Paper.\n- `knip.json`: `ignoreDependencies` now also matches `@fontsource-variable/.+`, otherwise knip would flag the CSS-imported package.\n\n**Imports** (top of `src/App.css`): `@fontsource-variable/dm-sans/wght.css` and `@fontsource/dm-mono/400.css`, next to the existing Libre Baskerville and Gloria imports.\n\n**Font variables** (`:root`, `src/App.css`)\n- `--font-sans: \"DM Sans Variable\", \"DM Sans\", system-ui, sans-serif`\n- `--font-mono: \"DM Mono\", ui-monospace, monospace`\n- `--font-body: system-ui, -apple-system, \"Segoe UI\", sans-serif`\n- `--font-quote: \"Libre Baskerville\", Georgia, serif`\n- `--font-ui: var(--font-body)`. This is now the default, and `font-family: var(--font-ui)` is unchanged. The old Paper Mono `@font-face` is still there but nothing uses it.\n\n**Tokens added or changed**\n- `--library-text-soft: #c9c1b6` (new)\n- `--nav-label-active: #f0e9df` (new)\n- `--row-radius: 9px` (new)\n- `--tile-radius: 12px` (new, also missing before)\n- `--card-radius: 20px` (new)\n- `--sidebar-width: 232px` (was 248px; the 220px narrow breakpoint is unchanged)\n- The other colour and radius tokens already matched Paper's values.\n\n**Paper typography, per role** (from computed styles)\n- system-ui: nav labels (14px 600), card titles (26px 600), Spaces header (12px 500), inspector note body (13px 400), Details labels (11px 500). This is most of the UI.\n- DM Sans: Settings title (15px 600), mascot heading (22px 600), quote body (18px 400), glass note body (14px 400).\n- DM Mono 400: counts (12px), quote attribution (10px), small meta (11px).\n- Georgia: the 110px quote mark.\n- Gloria Hallelujah: handwritten note titles, already imported.\n- Libre Baskerville is in Paper's font list but I did not find it on any node I checked.\n\nOn Windows, system-ui resolves to Segoe UI, so body text will not match Paper's rendering pixel for pixel.\n\n**Checks**\n- `bunx biome check knip.json package.json`: passed. `App.css` is not Biome-checked here.\n- `bun run typecheck`: passed.\n- I did not run a Vite build. The two new CSS import targets exist in `node_modules`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>108148</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>47</tool_uses><duration_ms>191116</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
