{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"5825a0d807895103efae15f1cd32475b5233ab4a3c4af2f48a4bb446159be7b2","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Gtwm19owEFjWGtXR7e5sCB","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"W2 sidebar","model":"haiku","effort":"xhigh","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"First read C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\resurf\\BRIEF.md and follow it exactly.\n\nYOUR AREA: the SIDEBAR (artboard 1.1 left column, and the collapsed edge tab). Match Paper exactly:\n- Brand: the 26px blot only. Remove the \"inkling\" wordmark. The mascot still has to live there (it roams; see src/components/mascot/), so keep the mascot's anchor working.\n- Nav: Everything uses the 3×3 dot-grid icon (accent colour), Top of mind an outline star, Serendipity shuffle (Hugeicons equivalents). Rows are 32px with --row-radius, system-ui 14px labels, and NO active fill. The active label is --nav-label-active with an accent icon; inactive labels are #C9C1B6.\n- Counts in DM Mono 12px, formatted with toLocaleString (\"1,601\"). Top of mind shows its count.\n- Spaces heading: sentence case \"Spaces\", 12px/500, 0.02em.\n- Space rows: Paper's blob marker shapes (export the SVG path with get_jsx). Colours #B0714F, #7F9A8C, #C98B8B, #C9B27A, #8E9BBF, #A88AB5. Every row shows its count. Fix the bug where only \"orange\" has a colour (App.css ~371-391): every Space colour must render.\n- Footer: Settings, 13px. NO avatar. Paper has no Help row. Remove the Help & shortcuts row from the sidebar, but keep the shortcuts dialog reachable through its keyboard shortcut. If no shortcut opens it, add \"?\" (skip it when typing in an input).\n- Collapse button: the 26×34 chevron on the sidebar edge, positioned as in Paper.\nHover, rename, delete and Space menus must keep working.\n\nYour files: the sidebar JSX in src/App.tsx (around 4600-4910) and the sidebar CSS in src/App.css. Leave the toolbar, grid and item view alone."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B49ewBfaBcaGCSKhgNokDW","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"W2 toolbar + search","model":"haiku","effort":"xhigh","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"First read C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\resurf\\BRIEF.md and follow it exactly.\n\nYOUR AREA: the TOOLBAR and SEARCH (artboards 1.1 top bar, 1.2 and 1.3). Match Paper exactly:\n- Top-left: two glass capsules. One holds back/forward, the other the grid/list view toggle. Move the view toggle out of its current solid box on the row below (App.tsx ~5331-5369, App.css ~3459-3485). Back/forward keep their existing history wiring and disabled states.\n- Floating toolbar: the toolbar floats over the grid, and cards scroll underneath the glass (Paper's masonry starts under it, marginTop -96px). The grid's own sizing belongs to another agent; you own only the toolbar overlay and the scroll container's top offset/padding so cards pass under it.\n- Resting search pill: centred, 34px tall, radius 17, 13px/600 label \"Everything\" (or the current view or Space name), with a glass recipe from Paper.\n- 1.2 drops in: on open, a 700×50 glass bar overlays the toolbar with Paper's deeper shadow (0 18px 40px …) and \"esc to close\" on the right. Keep the mascot eyes/anchor in the bar if they're already there.\n- 1.3 query pinned: after a query is committed, the pill returns to centre and the query shows as a glass chip (138×30, radius 999, 13px/500, with an × that clears it). \"N results\" sits right-aligned in DM Mono 12px. Remove the \"N items in library\" line in browse mode; Paper has no count there. Keep \"Save as Space\" reachable where Paper allows. If Paper has no spot for it, put it in the least intrusive place and report it.\n- Add button: a 34px pill, radius 999, padding 11/14, 14px icon, 13px/600. Keep its menu working.\nKeyboard focus, Esc and the search debounce/history behaviour must keep working.\n\nYour files: the header/toolbar JSX in src/App.tsx (~4920-5000 and ~5300-5370) and their CSS. Leave the sidebar, card internals and item view alone."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EriVAhhA9Y7UYKRvmM5HFE","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"W2 grid + cards","model":"haiku","effort":"xhigh","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"First read C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\resurf\\BRIEF.md and follow it exactly.\n\nYOUR AREA: the GRID and every CARD TYPE (artboard 1.1 masonry). Match Paper exactly:\n- Density: about 286px columns, 12px gap, 14px inset (App.tsx ~1213-1219 target width, App.css ~610 padding). Keep the virtualization intact. The column count should still adapt to the window width.\n- Cards: no border; radius from Paper (--tile-radius or --card-radius, whichever Paper uses).\n- Article card: cream #ECE6DC, a 120px image on top, the title in 16px/600 #1A1714, and a \"domain · N min\" line in DM Mono 11px #7A7268. Right now `.library-card .card-content {display:none}` hides grid text (App.css ~1641), so articles look like untitled images. Fix that for the card kinds that need text.\n- Quote card: a 110px Georgia quote mark #C4BA8C, the FULL quote in DM Sans 18px/128% #D0C68F (no 69-char cut, App.tsx ~936; clamp generously only if it's very long), a 120px divider, and the attribution in DM Mono 10px.\n- Note and PDF cards: the title in DM Sans 21px/600 uppercase, a 10px DM Mono label, a 22px ring, 10px dots (ItemMedia.tsx 85-135, App.css ~2295-2329).\n- Video card: 190px tall, with a bottom-left glass pill holding a play glyph and the duration (DM Mono 11px). Remove the centre play disc. If no duration exists, show the pill with just the play glyph.\n- File card (and Post without data): never a blank tile. Give it a designed typed card with the extension, name and size, in the same visual language as Note/PDF. There is no Paper artboard for it, so design it consistently and report that.\n- Image card: no border.\n- Hover and selected states: keep them subtle and consistent with Paper.\nThe list view (App.css ~1951) needs to keep working; restyle its type to the new fonts.\n\nYour files: src/components/ItemMedia.tsx, the card rendering in src/App.tsx (~900-1110, ~1200-1230), and the card and grid CSS. Leave the toolbar overlay, sidebar and item view alone."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JDRDVrcTrXN2fQuCZ524vq","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"W2 item view","model":"haiku","effort":"xhigh","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"First read C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\resurf\\BRIEF.md and follow it exactly.\n\nYOUR AREA: the opened ITEM VIEW (artboards 2.1, 2.2 and 2.3), in src/components/ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx plus its CSS (the item-view block in src/App.css). Match Paper exactly:\n- Inspector header: Info and Similar tabs (14px, the active one at 600) on the left, Close and esc on the right.\n- Similar tab (2.2): a two-column tile grid inside the inspector (139px columns, 8px gap, 12px radius; image, quote and note tiles). Clicking a tile opens that item, which makes it a history step. Fill it from the existing find-similar data source (find how App.tsx gets similar items, ~3170). This REPLACES the \"Find similar\" text button under Details, so remove that button. Leave the library-wide similar mode code in App.tsx alone; the cleanup wave will decide what happens to it. In the web preview similar data may be empty, so add an empty state.\n- Stage toolbar: a glass back/forward group (62×34) at the top-left of the stage, wired to the app's history. Pass the callbacks and canGoBack/canGoForward in as props. The toolbar back button is currently unclickable while an item is open, so this also fixes that. Do NOT add the title pill; the user removed it on purpose.\n- Title block: a 26/30 600 -0.025em system-ui title at 66px. Five 22px rounded colour swatches go under the title, rendered only when the item has a palette (add an optional `palette?: string[]` prop path; the backend agent is adding the data).\n- Action bar: favourite, move to Space, open original, show in folder, archive, with delete/trash at the far right. Show in folder and delete call optional callbacks. Hide them when no callback is passed. Wire delete to the existing archive/delete flow if there is one, otherwise leave it hidden and report.\n- Details: three rows (Saved, From, Size); drop Type. The note box has min-height 72px. The Space chip uses the blob marker icon instead of the 6px dot.\n- Stage image: 4px radius, box-shadow 0 24px 60px rgba(0,0,0,0.55).\n- Fonts: system-ui inspector text, and DM Mono for size, zoom and esc.\n- Zoom pill: keep the existing behaviour. Loading the original image on zoom is the backend agent's job.\nKeep the GSAP card flight, Esc/close, pixel zoom and note editing working.\n\nSmall, prop-only changes in App.tsx to pass data and callbacks in are allowed."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EGQ66bXBW2GW8WdKSsigrJ","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"W2 settings + archive","model":"haiku","effort":"xhigh","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"First read C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\resurf\\BRIEF.md and follow it exactly.\n\nYOUR AREA: SETTINGS and ARCHIVE (artboards 3.1 and 3.2). Match Paper exactly:\n- Sheet: scrim #080807 at 74%. Panel padding 28/40/32/48 with a 16px left radius. The panel title is DM Sans 28/34 at -0.02em; the note is 14/21 at 460px.\n- Rail: the \"Settings\" title in DM Sans 15px. The active row has NO fill, weight 500. The footer gets an \"inkling <version>\" line in DM Mono 11px, rendered only when a version is available (an optional value; a backend agent is adding it).\n- Library panel: the count line gets \"<size> on disk\" in DM Mono 12px, plus a 28px \"Show folder\" pill. Each renders only when its data or callback exists. The Export row shows a persistent \"last copy <date> · N items\" line (an optional value from the backend). Legend text #A8A096, Files swatch #4A443E. Close button 34×34. Don't auto-focus the close button on open; it causes the orange ring. Move initial focus to the panel or dialog container instead, so keyboard users still land inside.\n- Archive (3.2): uniform 179×174 tiles with 132px media, a 10px radius, no border, a 14px column gap and a 22px row gap. Each tile has a caption: the title plus a \"Kind · time\" line. On hover: a Restore pill and a 28px round delete at the bottom right, plus a 2px outline on the media. Select is 34px. Rename \"Recover\" to \"Restore\" everywhere in the archive UI. Selection mode and the empty state keep working; restyle them in the same language.\n- Browser extension tab: no artboard. Restyle it in the same language (replace the inline styles with classes), and replace the native window.confirm with an in-app confirm that matches the sheet.\n- Keep \"Show the welcome again\".\n\nYour files: the Settings and Archive JSX in src/App.tsx (~1283-1500, ~5550-5810) and their CSS (~5380-5520, archive ~2987-3000). Leave everything else alone."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
