folder\" that reveals that item's asset file, for the item view action bar.\n4. Persistent last export: store the last export's date and item count when an export succeeds, and read it back after a restart. Settings shows \"last copy Oct 12 · 1,588 items\".\n5. Original image on zoom: a way for the renderer to get the original full-resolution asset URL for an image item. Cards and the item view currently use the 512px thumbnail; the item view needs the original only once the user zooms past fit. Don't change thumbnail usage anywhere else.\n6. Colour palette: 5 dominant colours per image item. First check whether colours are already extracted (AGENTS.md lists colours as a search path). If so, expose them as `palette?: string[]` on the item summary. If not, compute them in the existing background job pipeline from the thumbnail (cheap), persist them, and backfill existing items lazily or with a job. Add a focused test.\n7. Video duration: if the existing video-link ingestion already gets a duration (from oEmbed or page metadata), persist it and expose `durationSeconds?`. If getting it would need new network calls beyond the capture fetch the user asked for, DON'T add them. Just report that.\n\nKeep IPC payloads small: summaries only, never full content (performance rule). Add focused bun tests for the job and persistence logic. Run `bun test <your test files>`, `bunx biome check <files you touched>` and `bun run typecheck`; ignore type errors in the frontend files other agents are editing, but report them.\n\nAt the end, report the exact renderer API for each item, so the frontend can wire it: the function/field names, their types, and how to call them from src/App.tsx. Also report what you skipped and why, and the test results.","target":{"providerInstanceId":"codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","options":{"reasoningEffort":"high"}},"mode":"async","role":"implementation","clientRequestId":"resurf-backend-data-r1","title":"Redesign backend data"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId