{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-20T11:59:07.287Z","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a71041f041c9ce200</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Gtwm19owEFjWGtXR7e5sCB</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-chris--t3-worktrees-inkling-t3-47ff5304\\fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7\\tasks\\a71041f041c9ce200.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"W2 sidebar\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>The sidebar rework is in and typechecks, but I could not verify it visually. The preview browser disconnected on every call (open, resize, evaluate, snapshot, including after status retries), so there is no screenshot at `C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\resurf-redesign\\w2-sidebar.png` and no measured comparison against Paper. This needs one real pass before it's called done.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- **`src/App.tsx`**\n  - Brand row: wordmark removed; the mascot slot and the mobile close button stay.\n  - Nav: dot grid (inline SVG copied from Paper, since Hugeicons has no 3×3 dot grid), `StarIcon` for Top of mind, `ShuffleIcon` for Serendipity. Counts use `toLocaleString`. Top of mind shows `pinsCount`, a memoised count of `matchesPinsView` items.\n  - Spaces: blob mark (`SpaceMark`, path from Paper's `get_jsx`), counts, heading in sentence case.\n  - Footer: Help &amp; shortcuts row removed. The update notice now sits above Settings so Settings stays anchored at the foot. No avatar.\n  - Helpers and `SPACE_MARK_PATH` sit just above `SidebarEdgeTab`. Icon imports updated.\n- **`src/lib/libraryApi.ts`**: added optional `itemCount?: number` to `StoredSpace`. This is the one shared-code change; the backend agent should fill that field. Until it does, only the open Space shows a count.\n- **`src/App.css`**: all changed sidebar rules are in one commented block at the old brand/nav position. Old rules are deleted. Three in-place edits: `.space-form` padding, `.sidebar-action-error` margin, and the mobile `.sidebar` padding. `.edge-tab` top moved 44px to 39px. Dead `.mobile-menu` removed.\n\n**Checks**\n\n- `bun run typecheck`: passes.\n- `bunx biome check` on my regions: clean. Remaining diagnostics are not mine: the App.tsx restore block at roughly 4292–4355 (formatting), App.tsx:1461 (settings role), App.css:5548 (format).\n\n**Decisions to confirm**\n\n- **Top padding:** kept at 39px to clear the Electron titlebar drag strip. Paper uses 18px, so the whole sidebar sits about 21px lower than Paper. The collapse chevron is aligned to the brand row at the same top.\n- **Mascot size:** `MASCOT_SIZE` stays at 44 because the roam code and its test expect one size everywhere. The brand row reserves only 26px through negative margins, and the centre the roam anchor measures does not move. The blot's ink is about 28px, close to Paper's 26px logo.\n- **Everything icon colour:** accent only when active, like the other two rows. The brief could also be read as always accent. Say if you want that.\n- **Space counts:** non-active rows show no count until `itemCount` exists. Preview seed Spaces show none except the open one.\n- **Yellow Space colour:** Paper's sixth colour (#C9B27A) is not wired. `electron/storage.mjs:475` normalises Space colours to five values, so this needs a backend change.\n- **Shortcut:** `?` already opens the shortcuts dialog (`src/lib/keyboardShortcuts.ts`, keydown handler in App.tsx), skipping inputs. No new binding was added.\n\n**Outside my area, not touched**\n\n- `src/components/mascot/RoamBoard.tsx` (dev-only `?mascot-roam`) still renders `&lt;strong&gt;inkling&lt;/strong&gt;`. The rule that styled it is gone, so it now renders unstyled. This belongs to the mascot owner.\n- `ExpandedItemOverlay` `.detail-space-dot` (`src/App.css` around 2615–2625) has the same orange-only colour bug.\n- The Gloria Hallelujah `@import` at the top of `src/App.css` is now unused by the sidebar. Paper lists Gloria among its fonts, so I left it for the foundation owner.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>251564</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>93</tool_uses><duration_ms>742700</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
