 settings and archive rules are deleted, including the duplicate `.settings-data-link` and the leftover block that ran to the \"Pixel zoom\" comment (now at line 5676).\n- `C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304\\src\\App.tsx`:\n  - 265: `formatLastCopy`.\n  - 1038-1180: archive tile markup (`isArchiveTile`, Restore pill, round delete, caption).\n  - 1366-1510: `ExtensionPairing`, with an in-panel Renew confirm replacing `window.confirm`. I changed the confirm group from `div role=\"group\"` to `section aria-label` to clear a Biome lint error.\n  - 1557-1645: `MAKEUP_GROUPS` recolored and `LibraryMakeup` with size and Show folder.\n  - 1646: `SidebarEdgeTab`, where the stale comment was moved.\n  - 1914: `settingsDialogRef`, so focus lands on the dialog, not the close button.\n  - 2157: `showLibraryFolderFromSettings`.\n  - 4329-4402: `restoreArchivedLibraryItems`, shared by single and selection restore. I re-indented it to Biome style.\n  - 5778 onward: settings sheet JSX (footer at 5825, restore button at 5861, last copy at 5969).\n\n**Checks**\n\n- `bun run typecheck`: exit 0.\n- `biome check src/App.tsx`: my two issues are fixed. Remaining items are outside my area: a format diff near line 1245 (card-source ternary, from the grid/card work) and a `noUselessFragments` at line 5278 (search result context).\n- `biome format src/App.css`: no hunks in the settings block. The 15 hunks elsewhere are quote and similar-item rules outside my area.\n- Removed identifiers (`settings-data-scroll`, `settings-archive-scroll`, `settings-panel-count`, `settings-batch-recover`, `settings-data-card`, `settings-data-heading`, `settingsCloseRef`, `recoverSelectedArchivedItems`) are gone. No `window.confirm` remains in App.tsx. \"Recover\" survives only in two code comments.\n\n**Visual check: not done**\n\n- Every `preview_snapshot` call timed out or lost the browser connection. Tabs were also closed out from under me, probably by parallel agents sharing this preview session.\n- `preview_evaluate` worked once. It showed the sheet rendering with Library, Archive, and Browser extension tabs. At the reported 1280x800 viewport the sheet measured 1058x627, so I did not get exact values for the scrim, padding, or type sizes.\n- I closed the two preview tabs I had opened. One other tab in the session belongs to someone else and I left it alone.\n\n**Known mismatches and open items**\n\n- Archive panel left padding is 46 in Paper; I used the brief's 48.\n- Paper's custom icons are replaced with the app's Hugeicons (RotateLeft01Icon for restore, Delete02Icon for delete).\n- Caption dates use the app's `item.date` format, not Paper's relative \"3 days ago\".\n- The archive grid maps every archived item and is not virtualized. That conflicts with the brief's virtualization rule and needs a decision.\n- The count line's \"on disk\" size, the Show folder pill, the last-copy line, and the version footer depend on helpers in `src/lib/libraryApi.ts` and the backend agent's main and preload handlers. They render only when data exists, so they are absent in web preview.\n- Shared-file note: the grid, toolbar, and item-view agents are still editing `App.tsx`, so line numbers may shift.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>109710</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>158</tool_uses><duration_ms>1280311</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
