{"parentUuid":"3ba60c09-0200-4226-a4c6-bbb898bb0c58","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDUfcXGFn7txtLVzMhnR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"For wave 3, I'm splitting wiring and cleanup into two tracks: backend fixes like the EBUSY test teardown, per-Space item counts, and adding a sixth yellow Space color across storage and the Paper palette, versus frontend wiring tasks like showItemInFolder, the palette, original-resolution zoom, and settings.\n\nI also need to decide on the dead code for library-wide similar items — since it's now unreachable, I should remove it along with its history snapshot handling. There's a pile of smaller leftovers too: unused RoamBoard library-toolbar styling, the LibraryEdgeFade top fade, a possibly unused Gloria import, an unused Paper Mono @font-face, an orange bug in detail-space-dot, overlapping capture error chips, unvirtualized archive view, and biome formatting cleanup for App.css/App.tsx.\n\nI'm thinking Luna should run backend-only changes in parallel with Haiku's wiring and cleanup work, making sure Haiku knows the itemCount and yellow color types are coming from Luna so they don't collide on libraryApi.ts. Afterward I want a proper visual QA pass — possibly running the verify-inkling skill against the Electron app with a scratch library for a more thorough comparison, treating that as design-side work for Haiku.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":266,"cache_read_input_tokens":192264,"output_tokens":3593,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":612},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":266,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3593,"cache_read_input_tokens":192264,"cache_creation_input_tokens":266,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":266},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":11081,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgDUfcEA6FWDJQLtxCUnD","requestRef":"451551b2-73b1-4fe0-a8d0-5b609470fd8e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ea79a9cf-4130-48cf-8f0e-9417753ff1a5","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:20:00.600Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"ea79a9cf-4130-48cf-8f0e-9417753ff1a5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDUfcXGFn7txtLVzMhnR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016cpkMEd9gBXtK3ZnyTZP8e","name":"mcp__t3-code__delegate_task","input":{"task":"Repo worktree: C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304 (branch feat/glass-surface; HEAD is 4a587e1). Read AGENTS.md and follow it strictly: no pattern kills, NEVER touch the live library, no hardcoded ports or paths, targeted checks only.\n\nA Haiku frontend agent is editing src/App.tsx, src/App.css and src/components/* in this same checkout right now. Do NOT edit those files. Your scope: electron/*, the preload bridge, src/lib/*, src/electron.d.ts and tests. Use targeted edits only. Never checkout/restore/stash/reset/commit; the orchestrator commits.\n\nTasks (backend only):\n1. Your earlier round added tests in electron/ai-jobs.test.ts and electron/storage.test.ts. They fail on Windows during temp-dir teardown with EBUSY. Fix them so `bun test <those files>` passes cleanly on Windows. Close DB handles and workers before rm, or use the cleanup pattern the other tests use. Don't add sleeps or retry loops that hide a leak. Also look at the pre-existing \"Windows path expectation\" failure you saw: if it's on main too, report it and leave it; if this branch caused it, fix it.\n2. Per-Space item counts. The sidebar shows a count on EVERY Space. Fill the optional `itemCount?: number` on `StoredSpace` (src/lib/libraryApi.ts) in the Spaces list the renderer loads. Regular Spaces: a COUNT of membership. Smart Spaces run a saved search, so skip theirs if counting would mean running every query on each load (performance rule); leave it undefined and say so. Keep it cheap: one grouped query.\n3. Sixth Space colour. Paper has six Space colours, #B0714F, #7F9A8C, #C98B8B, #C9B27A, #8E9BBF, #A88AB5, but electron/storage.mjs (~line 475) normalises to five. Add the yellow (#C9B27A) value using the existing naming scheme, so it can be stored and round-trips. Update the shared colour type in src/lib if there is one.\n4. Video duration. You found no existing extraction. Check whether the oEmbed/page metadata the capture ALREADY fetches carries a duration (e.g. YouTube's page meta `duration`, or og:video:duration). Only if it's already in the fetched data, persist it as metadata `durationSeconds` (the frontend reads `metadata.durationSeconds`), with a focused test. No new network requests.\n\nRun `bun test <files you touched>`, `bunx biome check <files you touched>` and `bun run typecheck`. Report the API/field changes, the test results, and anything you skipped.","target":{"providerInstanceId":"codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","options":{"reasoningEffort":"high"}},"mode":"async","role":"implementation","clientRequestId":"resurf-backend-data-r2","title":"Redesign backend round 2"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":266,"cache_read_input_tokens":192264,"output_tokens":3593,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":612},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":266,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3593,"cache_read_input_tokens":192264,"cache_creation_input_tokens":266,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":266},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_016cpkMEd9gBXtK3ZnyTZP8e":{"task":"Repo worktree: C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304 (branch feat/glass-surface; HEAD is 4a587e1). Read AGENTS.md and follow it strictly: no pattern kills, NEVER touch the live library, no hardcoded ports or paths, targeted checks only.\n\nA Haiku frontend agent is editing src/App.tsx, src/App.css and src/components/* in this same checkout right now. Do NOT edit those files. Your scope: electron/*, the preload bridge, src/lib/*, src/electron.d.ts and tests. Use targeted edits only. Never checkout/restore/stash/reset/commit; the orchestrator commits.\n\nTasks (backend only):\n1. Your earlier round added tests in electron/ai-jobs.test.ts and electron/storage.test.ts. They fail on Windows during temp-dir teardown with EBUSY. Fix them so `bun test <those files>` passes cleanly on Windows. Close DB handles and workers before rm, or use the cleanup pattern the other tests use. Don't add sleeps or retry loops that hide a leak. Also look at the pre-existing \"Windows path expectation\" failure you saw: if it's on main too, report it and leave it; if this branch caused it, fix it.\n2. Per-Space item counts. The sidebar shows a count on EVERY Space. Fill the optional `itemCount?: number` on `StoredSpace` (src/lib/libraryApi.ts) in the Spaces list the renderer loads. Regular Spaces: a COUNT of membership. Smart Spaces run a saved search, so skip theirs if counting would mean running every query on each load (performance rule); leave it undefined and say so. Keep it cheap: one grouped query.\n3. Sixth Space colour. Paper has six Space colours, #B0714F, #7F9A8C, #C98B8B, #C9B27A, #8E9BBF, #A88AB5, but electron/storage.mjs (~line 475) normalises to five. Add the yellow (#C9B27A) value using the existing naming scheme, so it can be stored and round-trips. Update the shared colour type in src/lib if there is one.\n4. Video duration. You found no existing extraction. Check whether the oEmbed/page metadata the capture ALREADY fetches carries a duration (e.g. YouTube's page meta `duration`, or og:video:duration). Only if it's already in the fetched data, persist it as metadata `durationSeconds` (the frontend reads `metadata.durationSeconds`), with a focused test. No new network requests.\n\nRun `bun test <files you touched>`, `bunx biome check <files you touched>` and `bun run typecheck`. Report the API/field changes, the test results, and anything you skipped.","target":{"providerInstanceId":"codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","options":{"reasoningEffort":"high"}},"mode":"async","role":"implementation","clientRequestId":"resurf-backend-data-r2","title":"Redesign backend round 2"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgDUfcEA6FWDJQLtxCUnD","requestRef":"451551b2-73b1-4fe0-a8d0-5b609470fd8e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3ea6be39-1ecb-429c-bbcc-4af56ffab076","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:20:07.385Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
