-data-heading) whose CSS was deleted. Restyle it in the new settings-data-row language the Library panel uses. Keep the welcome replay working, and keep the tab order Library, General, Archive, Browser extension.\n- The library-wide \"Find similar\" mode is no longer reachable now that the inspector has a Similar tab. Remove its dead code: onFindSimilar, findSimilarItems, the similar-mode state, its result-context UI and its history snapshot fields. Keep everything the inspector's Similar tab uses (loadSimilarLibraryItems, openSimilarItem). Make sure back/forward history still works for the remaining state.\n- Remove these leftovers: the unused `edge=\"top\"` path of LibraryEdgeFade (if nothing uses it); the `library-toolbar` class in src/components/mascot/RoamBoard.tsx (point it at the new capture-bar classes); the Paper Mono @font-face and the Gloria Hallelujah import if nothing uses them (grep first); any CSS rule whose class no longer appears in any .tsx (check every class in the redesign blocks); and duplicate rules that the parallel agents defined twice.\n- The capture error chip and the pinned-query filter row overlap when both show. Stack them.\n- Archive grid not virtualized: check `git show bc69b04:src/App.tsx`. If the archive was already unvirtualized before, leave it and say so. If wave 2 removed virtualization, restore it.\n- Replace hardcoded colours the agents added (e.g. `#ffffff14` in the view selection) with existing tokens where an equivalent token exists.\n- Run `bunx biome check --write src/App.tsx src/App.css src/components/` (formatting only), then fix the remaining lint by hand.\n\nC. OPTIMIZE: no new re-renders on the grid hot path, memoised derived counts (pinsCount, Space counts), no effects that refetch on every render (library size, version and last export load once when Settings opens), no continuously repainting animations.\n\nChecks: `bun run typecheck`, `bunx biome check src/App.tsx src/App.css src/components/`, and `bun test src/components/`. Don't commit.\n\nReport: what you wired, what you removed (with rough line counts), anything still missing, and the check results.","outputFile":"C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-chris--t3-worktrees-inkling-t3-47ff5304\\fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7\\tasks\\aadb798ad96493397.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"29cf392e-6667-4ea3-b4ca-0a9e27fd81da","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
