{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"cde4c1f506305ed78c5f468a5f463dcf3b8b6c6e8aec5d76ebf75f051b45f408","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"For wave 3, I'm splitting wiring and cleanup into two tracks: backend fixes like the EBUSY test teardown, per-Space item counts, and adding a sixth yellow Space color across storage and the Paper palette, versus frontend wiring tasks like showItemInFolder, the palette, original-resolution zoom, and settings.\n\nI also need to decide on the dead code for library-wide similar items — since it's now unreachable, I should remove it along with its history snapshot handling. There's a pile of smaller leftovers too: unused RoamBoard library-toolbar styling, the LibraryEdgeFade top fade, a possibly unused Gloria import, an unused Paper Mono @font-face, an orange bug in detail-space-dot, overlapping capture error chips, unvirtualized archive view, and biome formatting cleanup for App.css/App.tsx.\n\nI'm thinking Luna should run backend-only changes in parallel with Haiku's wiring and cleanup work, making sure Haiku knows the itemCount and yellow color types are coming from Luna so they don't collide on libraryApi.ts. Afterward I want a proper visual QA pass — possibly running the verify-inkling skill against the Electron app with a scratch library for a more thorough comparison, treating that as design-side work for Haiku.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016cpkMEd9gBXtK3ZnyTZP8e","name":"mcp__t3-code__delegate_task","input":{"task":"Repo worktree: C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304 (branch feat/glass-surface; HEAD is 4a587e1). Read AGENTS.md and follow it strictly: no pattern kills, NEVER touch the live library, no hardcoded ports or paths, targeted checks only.\n\nA Haiku frontend agent is editing src/App.tsx, src/App.css and src/components/* in this same checkout right now. Do NOT edit those files. Your scope: electron/*, the preload bridge, src/lib/*, src/electron.d.ts and tests. Use targeted edits only. Never checkout/restore/stash/reset/commit; the orchestrator commits.\n\nTasks (backend only):\n1. Your earlier round added tests in electron/ai-jobs.test.ts and electron/storage.test.ts. They fail on Windows during temp-dir teardown with EBUSY. Fix them so `bun test <those files>` passes cleanly on Windows. Close DB handles and workers before rm, or use the cleanup pattern the other tests use. Don't add sleeps or retry loops that hide a leak. Also look at the pre-existing \"Windows path expectation\" failure you saw: if it's on main too, report it and leave it; if this branch caused it, fix it.\n2. Per-Space item counts. The sidebar shows a count on EVERY Space. Fill the optional `itemCount?: number` on `StoredSpace` (src/lib/libraryApi.ts) in the Spaces list the renderer loads. Regular Spaces: a COUNT of membership. Smart Spaces run a saved search, so skip theirs if counting would mean running every query on each load (performance rule); leave it undefined and say so. Keep it cheap: one grouped query.\n3. Sixth Space colour. Paper has six Space colours, #B0714F, #7F9A8C, #C98B8B, #C9B27A, #8E9BBF, #A88AB5, but electron/storage.mjs (~line 475) normalises to five. Add the yellow (#C9B27A) value using the existing naming scheme, so it can be stored and round-trips. Update the shared colour type in src/lib if there is one.\n4. Video duration. You found no existing extraction. Check whether the oEmbed/page metadata the capture ALREADY fetches carries a duration (e.g. YouTube's page meta `duration`, or og:video:duration). Only if it's already in the fetched data, persist it as metadata `durationSeconds` (the frontend reads `metadata.durationSeconds`), with a focused test. No new network requests.\n\nRun `bun test <files you touched>`, `bunx biome check <files you touched>` and `bun run typecheck`. Report the API/field changes, the test results, and anything you skipped.","target":{"providerInstanceId":"codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","options":{"reasoningEffort":"high"}},"mode":"async","role":"implementation","clientRequestId":"resurf-backend-data-r2","title":"Redesign backend round 2"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SSm57b4vwni4dJKKqsLKba","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"W3 wiring + cleanup","model":"haiku","effort":"xhigh","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"First read C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\resurf\\BRIEF.md and follow it, with these exceptions: you are the only frontend agent now (a backend agent is editing electron/ and src/lib/ in parallel, so don't edit those), and do NOT use the preview browser tools. They're broken in this session; a later QA pass does the visual check.\n\nWave 2 built every redesign screen in parallel, and main is merged (HEAD 4a587e1). You are WAVE 3: WIRE the data, then CLEAN UP and OPTIMIZE the combined work. Read `git diff bc69b04 HEAD -- src/` to see everything that changed.\n\nA. WIRE the backend data. The renderer API is in src/lib/libraryApi.ts:\n- getAppVersion(): Promise<string|undefined> → Settings footer \"inkling <version>\".\n- getLibrarySize(refresh=true): Promise<{bytes}|undefined> → \"<size> on disk\".\n- getLastExport(): Promise<{exportedAt, items}|null|undefined> → \"last copy <date> · N items\". Refresh it after an export succeeds.\n- showLibraryFolder(): Promise<boolean> → the Show folder pill.\n- showItemInFolder(id): Promise<boolean> → the item view's \"show in folder\" action. ExpandedItemOverlay takes `onShowInFolder`, but App.tsx doesn't pass it yet.\n- Original image on zoom: once the user zooms past fit in ZoomableImage (ExpandedItemOverlay), swap the source to `await assetUrl(item.localAssetPath)`. Keep the thumbnail until then; keep the swap seamless (same layout, no flash) and only for images.\n- `palette?: string[]` on LibraryItem → the item view swatches. Make sure storedItemToLibraryItem maps it.\nSeveral of these may be partly wired by the Settings agent already. Verify each end to end in the code and finish what's missing. In the web preview these return undefined, so the UI must hide cleanly.\nComing from the backend agent (code against these; they may land while you work): `StoredSpace.itemCount?: number` (sidebar counts on every Space) and a sixth Space colour, yellow #C9B27A (wire it into the sidebar colour set and the Space colour cycle). Also fix the `.detail-space-dot` orange-only bug in the item view; it should use the Space's own colour, the same way the sidebar does.\n\nB. CLEAN UP:\n- Main's new Settings \"General\" tab (around App.tsx 5840, with the \"Show the welcome again\" button) still uses old markup and classes (settings-data-scroll, settings-data-card, settings-data-heading) whose CSS was deleted. Restyle it in the new settings-data-row language the Library panel uses. Keep the welcome replay working, and keep the tab order Library, General, Archive, Browser extension.\n- The library-wide \"Find similar\" mode is no longer reachable now that the inspector has a Similar tab. Remove its dead code: onFindSimilar, findSimilarItems, the similar-mode state, its result-context UI and its history snapshot fields. Keep everything the inspector's Similar tab uses (loadSimilarLibraryItems, openSimilarItem). Make sure back/forward history still works for the remaining state.\n- Remove these leftovers: the unused `edge=\"top\"` path of LibraryEdgeFade (if nothing uses it); the `library-toolbar` class in src/components/mascot/RoamBoard.tsx (point it at the new capture-bar classes); the Paper Mono @font-face and the Gloria Hallelujah import if nothing uses them (grep first); any CSS rule whose class no longer appears in any .tsx (check every class in the redesign blocks); and duplicate rules that the parallel agents defined twice.\n- The capture error chip and the pinned-query filter row overlap when both show. Stack them.\n- Archive grid not virtualized: check `git show bc69b04:src/App.tsx`. If the archive was already unvirtualized before, leave it and say so. If wave 2 removed virtualization, restore it.\n- Replace hardcoded colours the agents added (e.g. `#ffffff14` in the view selection) with existing tokens where an equivalent token exists.\n- Run `bunx biome check --write src/App.tsx src/App.css src/components/` (formatting only), then fix the remaining lint by hand.\n\nC. OPTIMIZE: no new re-renders on the grid hot path, memoised derived counts (pinsCount, Space counts), no effects that refetch on every render (library size, version and last export load once when Settings opens), no continuously repainting animations.\n\nChecks: `bun run typecheck`, `bunx biome check src/App.tsx src/App.css src/components/`, and `bun test src/components/`. Don't commit.\n\nReport: what you wired, what you removed (with rough line counts), anything still missing, and the check results."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
