{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:34:04.636Z","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","content":"Delegated task node:delegated-task:command%3Amcp%3Afe69a27e-d71d-499d-a1f1-f04b58072a79%3Adelegate-task%3Aresurf-backend-data-r2 (Redesign backend round 2) [completed]:\nImplemented the backend changes.\n\n- `list_spaces` now returns `itemCount` for Regular Spaces using one grouped membership query. Smart Spaces leave it undefined. The existing `StoredSpace.itemCount?` field carries the count.\n- Added `yellow` to the accepted Space colours and the shared `SpaceColor` type. Tests cover listing counts and yellow surviving export and restore.\n- Updated test teardown to stop workers, close processors and databases, and clean up temp roots. The restore staging read is isolated so Bun can finalize SQLite statement wrappers before removing its temp directory.\n- Skipped video duration: the current video capture reads oEmbed title, author, and thumbnail fields; it does not fetch or extract a duration. No new network request was added.\n\n**Checks:** Biome passed on all four changed files; `bun run typecheck` passed. The combined test run had 40 passes and one failure: the POSIX-path expectation in `data directory keeps portable precedence...` expects `/apps/inkling/data`, while Windows returns `\\apps\\inkling\\data`. That test and implementation are present on `main`, so I left them unchanged. No EBUSY teardown failures occurred in the final run.\n\nEarlier failed test runs left temporary test directories under `%TEMP%`. I attempted to remove those exact test directories after verifying their paths, but automatic review rejected the cleanup command. The latest test runs clean up their own temp directories. I did not edit the concurrent frontend files or access the live library."}
