{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:44:15.845Z","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a63fe3c33f59ab4ab</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01WgDdmR2kSsSd1B6XJzK3x7</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-chris--t3-worktrees-inkling-t3-47ff5304\\fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7\\tasks\\a63fe3c33f59ab4ab.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"QA: app vs Paper visual\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>QA is stopped at the first step. The preview screenshot tool times out on every attempt, so I have no app screenshots and only one of the nine Paper references.\n\n**Tooling status**\n- `preview_snapshot` timed out (15s) on the first tab, and again on a fresh visible tab, which was the retry you asked for.\n- `preview_evaluate` works, so the dev server at `http://localhost:5173/` is alive. The problem is the snapshot channel.\n- Both tabs are closed. I did not start, stop, or touch any server or the library.\n\n**Saved so far**\n- Paper, 1.1 Library: `C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\resurf-redesign\\qa-1.1-paper.png`\n- ![1.1 Library, Paper](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\resurf-redesign\\qa-1.1-paper.png)\n- The Paper export tool writes to Downloads. I moved the file out, so nothing is left there.\n\n**Not done**\n- All 9 app screenshots.\n- The other 8 Paper references.\n- The computed-style comparison against Paper.\n\n**Preliminary observations (from `preview_evaluate` only, not verified visually)**\n1. **Viewport mismatch.** The preview reports 1280x800 even after a freeform resize to 1440x900 on both tabs. The Paper artboards are 1440x900, so a layout comparison at matching width isn't possible with the preview as it stands. Treat this as a blocker for a fair comparison.\n2. **Sample data differs from the Paper mock.** The nav counts are \"Everything 28\" and \"Top of mind 3\" against Paper's 1,601 and 11. The Space list also differs: the app has Design references, Read later, Top picks and Weekend reading, while Paper has Japan trip, Type &amp; fonts, Quotes I keep and Kitchen in addition to two shared names. This is content, not design, but it means the references won't match exactly.\n3. **Font, unconfirmed.** The app's body font is `system-ui, -apple-system, \"Segoe UI\", sans-serif`. The Paper file uses DM Sans, DM Mono, Georgia and Libre Baskerville. I only checked the body element. Specific nav and card text may set their own fonts, so this needs a per-element check.\n\n**To resume:** the snapshot tool needs fixing first, or an alternative capture path with a 1440-wide viewport. Once that works, the remaining work is the app captures, the Paper exports, and the computed-style pass.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>89524</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>18</tool_uses><duration_ms>119836</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
