{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:04:38.773Z","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a4fd0ebb47aa00594</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Qm3w7qXYf9Gvj4v2EC1JZk</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-chris--t3-worktrees-inkling-t3-47ff5304\\fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7\\tasks\\a4fd0ebb47aa00594.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"QA via Electron CDP\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Visual QA: inkling app vs Paper \"resurf redesign\" (p-6-0), 1440x900\n\nMost type, radius, glass and spacing values match Paper. The real problems are a pinned query chip that covers the first card (1.3), a window-controls band that overlaps the inspector's Close button (2.x), and a top band that pushes the sidebar and toolbar down relative to Paper. Differences are listed biggest first.\n\nSeverity: high breaks layout or hides a control; medium is a visible offset or extra chrome; low is small measured drift or a content/structure difference.\n\n### 1.1 Library\n\nMATCHES: sidebar width 232, gap 22, inline padding 10. Nav rows 32px tall, 9px radius, active label 14px/600 #F0E9DF. Counts DM Mono 12px muted. Spaces heading 12px/500, 0.24px tracking. Main frame #0D0C0B, 16px radius, #262221 border. Add button 69x34 (#E5DDD2, 13px/600, 999px radius). Search pill 116x34, 17px radius, paddings 13/16, gap 8. Glass recipe (#0C0B0A9E, blur 18px saturate 140% brightness 70%, #FFFFFF29 top border, matching inset and drop shadows). Note card 20px radius, #161412 fill, note title 21px/600 uppercase.\n\nDifferences:\n- Toolbar and sidebar sit lower › Paper toolbar top 8px, sidebar padding-top 18px › app toolbar top 37px, sidebar padding-top 39px. The app reserves a top band for the frameless window controls. › medium\n- Brand mark › Paper logo 26x26 at (16,23) › app 44x44 at (7,35). Horizontal centre matches, vertical centre is 21px lower. › medium\n- Card grid top › Paper masonry starts above the toolbar (marginTop -96) and runs under it › app first card at y=37, leaving an empty band above the grid. › low\n- Sidebar bottom padding › Paper 6px › app 10px › low\n\nScreenshots: `C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\resurf-redesign\\qa-1-1-library-app.png` and `qa-1-1-library-paper.png`\n\n### 1.2 Search drops in\n\nMATCHES: expanded bar 700x50, 20px radius, 15px padding, gap 12, same glass and shadows as Paper. Input text 14px. \"esc to close\" DM Mono 10px/12px, 72x12 (matches Paper). Query field 548px wide.\n\nDifferences:\n- Copper focus ring on the expanded bar › Paper has no outline › app `.search-field:has(input:focus-visible)` draws 2px solid #B0714F with 3px offset (computed on `label.search-field`). Text inputs always match `:focus-visible`, so the ring also appears after a mouse click. This is an intentional accessibility rule, but it shows in the default state. › medium\n- Bar horizontal position › Paper left 482 absolute › app 487 (+5px) › low\n- Field mascot slot › Paper 24x20 › app 22x23 at (504,56) › low\n\nScreenshots: `qa-1-2-search-drops-in-app.png` and `qa-1-2-search-drops-in-paper.png` (same folder)\n\n### 1.3 Query pinned\n\nMATCHES: pinned chip 30px tall with 999px radius. Search pill returns to 116x34 (Paper 117x34). Chip text 13px/500.\n\nDifferences:\n- Pinned chip covers the first result card › Paper reserves a 44px filter row above the grid (marginTop 52) and cards start about 100px down › app's filter row sits at y 89, but the grid does not move. First card is at (247,37) 286x191, and the chip at (247,93) 90x30 sits on its top-left corner. › high\n- Chip width › Paper 138px › app 90px (content: Paper's chip holds more text) › low\n- \"6 results\" count › Paper DM Mono 12px/16px muted › app shows a result count and \"Save as Space\" on the same row › not measured\n\nScreenshots: `qa-1-3-query-pinned-app.png` and `qa-1-3-query-pinned-paper.png`\n\n### 2.1 Item inspector (image card)\n\nMATCHES: Info tab 14px/600 #E5DDD2, Similar 14px/400 muted, 18px tab gap. Title 26px/600, 30px line height, -0.025em tracking. Note card 72px min height, 10px radius, #161412 fill, #262221 border, 13px/20px text #C9C1B6, padding 11/12. Action bar 44px tall with #262221 top border, 32x32 buttons, 4px gap. Zoom pill 114x36 glass with 4/6 padding and 4px gap. \"Close details\" DM Sans 12px muted.\n\nDifferences:\n- Window controls cover the overlay's Close details button › Paper has no window chrome, Close sits at y≈19 › app's fixed `.electron-window-controls` (z 200) has Minimize at x 1302, Maximize at 1348 and Close window at 1394, each 46x32 from y 0. The overlay's \"Close details\" (1357,19, 67x16) sits under that band. The preload exposes `windowControls` unconditionally (`electron/preload.cjs:75`), so the packaged full app has this too. › high\n- Inspector and viewer sit flush to the overlay edges › Paper's library frame has 8px top and bottom padding › app has none. Tab text top is 18 vs Paper 25. Title is 67 vs 74. Action bar is 851–895 vs Paper 844–888. › medium\n- Centre title pill missing in the inspector toolbar › Paper shows it centred › app none. From screenshot review, not re-measured. › medium\n- Trash (\"Delete permanently\") absent › Paper shows it at the right end of the action bar on a live item › app renders it only when the item is archived (`ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx`, `actions.onDelete &amp;&amp; shownItem.archived`). Probably intentional; confirm with the designer. › low\n- Detail row step › Paper 25px (16px line + 9px gap) › app 26px › low\n- Zoom pill position › Paper about x 619–733, y 840–876 › app x 624–738, y 838–874 › low\n\nNot compared: swatches and Space chips, because the sample item has none.\n\nScreenshots: `qa-2-1-item-inspector-app.png` and `qa-2-1-item-inspector-paper.png`\n\n### 2.2 Similar tab\n\nMATCHES: active Similar tab 14px/600 #E5DDD2 with Info 14px/400 muted. Title switches to 20px/600, 26px line height, -0.015em tracking, the same as Paper. An earlier note that Similar was unstyled was a misread; the first tab in the probe is Info.\n\nDifferences:\n- Similar tile grid not comparable › Paper shows a 2-column tile grid (286x670) › app shows \"Nothing similar yet.\" because the preview sample has no similar results › content, not compared\n- Window controls and inspector edge inset › same as 2.1 › high and medium\n\nScreenshots: `qa-2-2-similar-tab-app.png` and `qa-2-2-similar-tab-paper.png`\n\n### 2.3 Zoomed in (past 800%)\n\nMATCHES: zoom pill 114x36 with glass recipe. Zoom label DM Mono 12px.\n\nDifferences:\n- Window controls over Close details › same as 2.1 › high\n- Inspector flush to overlay edges › same as 2.1 › medium\n- Pixel grid and centre title pill › not verified by computed style. The earlier screenshot review noted the title pill missing in this view. › medium (visual only)\n\nScreenshots: `qa-2-3-zoomed-in-app.png` and `qa-2-3-zoomed-in-paper.png`\n\n### 3.1 Settings, Library\n\nMATCHES: sheet 1080x640 with 24px radius (Paper's sheet is 1080x640; position is centred, not read from Paper). Rail 232x638 with padding 22/12/18/12. \"Settings\" title DM Sans 15px/600, 20px line height. Active row Library 208x32 at (193,195), 14px/500, 9px radius, gap 10, padding 10. Inactive rows 14px/400 in text-soft. Row pitch 34px (2px gap).\n\nDifferences:\n- General row › Paper has three rows (Library, Archive, Browser extension) and Archive is second at y 228 › app inserts General second (y 229), pushing Archive to third (y 263) and showing a count of 1 › low. Structure and content: the app keeps the General tab that the mock lacks (commit 4a587e1 kept main's General tab).\n- Right-hand panel › not measured in this pass; visual check only\n\nScreenshots: `qa-3-1-settings-library-app.png` and `qa-3-1-settings-library-paper.png`\n\n### 3.2 Settings, Archive\n\nMATCHES: archive grid column gap 14px and row gap 22px. Tile size 179x174. Restore is hover-only in the app and not visible at rest in `qa-3-2-settings-archive-app.png`, which matches Paper's hover-tile frame.\n\nDifferences:\n- Archive tile count › Paper 8 tiles › app 1 (content)\n- Archive row position › same General-row shift as 3.1 › low\n\nScreenshots: `qa-3-2-settings-archive-app.png` and `qa-3-2-settings-archive-paper.png`\n\n### 4.1 Mascot\n\nMATCHES: composite strip covers rest, transition frames t0–t3, listening, reading, no-match and back-home, built from live captures.\n\nDifferences:\n- Field mascot eye slot › Paper 24x20 › app 22x23 › low\n- Busy and capture-failed mascot states were not verified. Preview cannot trigger them.\n\nScreenshots: `qa-4-1-mascot-app.png` and `qa-4-1-mascot-paper.png`\n\n### Cross-cutting\n\n- Window controls appear in every Electron mode because the preload exposes them unconditionally. The inspector Close collision therefore also applies to the packaged app.\n- The sidebar (+21px) and toolbar (+29px) offsets come from the top band the app reserves for those controls (main padding-top 36, sidebar padding-top 39). Paper has no window chrome.\n- Preview-only limits: similar tiles are empty, Export and Restore are disabled, and mascot busy and capture-failed states cannot be triggered.\n\n### Cleanup\n\n- Stopped PID 40876 (electron.exe, preview, CDP 53602, profile `inkling-resurf-qa-TtTTN2`) after confirming its command line. Also stopped its three child processes (41884, 36320, 7584), found through the parent chain. Confirmed gone.\n- Deleted the temp profile and `run.json`.\n- Restored `HKCU\\Software\\Classes\\inkling` from the pre-launch backup. The dev launch had repointed it to this worktree's Electron. Heads-up: launching the dev Electron repoints the `inkling://` handler, so a deep-link test will need the same restore.\n- No source edits, no commits. `git status` is clean. The worktree `dist\\` was overwritten by the `vite build --mode electron-preview` run and is gitignored.\n- Never touched the desktop app or the live library.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>188400</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>104</tool_uses><duration_ms>1204325</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
