{"parentUuid":"bff314b2-90cf-4fb8-8c67-ecbe90ec0cf2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDY63YvtjwY37QgzFkrZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm identifying the high-priority fixes: the pinned chip overlapping the toolbar/search area, and the window controls colliding with the close button in item view, which likely needs the inspector header to reserve space for window chrome.\n\nFor medium issues, I'm tackling the stray copper focus ring on the search bar after mouse clicks by removing it in favor of the expanded bar itself acting as the focus indicator, plus the brand mark sizing mismatch and the card grid's top band alignment. I'll ignore the title pill removal since that was intentional, and leave the low-priority items for later.\n\nThe window-controls band is unavoidable since the toolbar's Add button would otherwise collide with the title bar controls in Electron, so I'm accepting that constraint. For deleting live items, I'm treating it as a judgment call tied to the archive flow rather than a true bug, just flagging it for awareness.\n\nI'm splitting the remaining fixes into three parallel tasks: one covering the toolbar and search chip overlap plus focus ring and mascot slot sizing, one for the item view's window-controls overlap and frame padding and zoom pill position, and one for the sidebar's brand mark and bottom padding — since they touch different parts of the stylesheet, they can run concurrently.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4586,"cache_read_input_tokens":210079,"output_tokens":3273,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":818},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4586,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iteratio