{"parentUuid":"57221f66-a8aa-4e11-a566-07304cac1ffc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDY63YvtjwY37QgzFkrZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The comparison is in. Most values match Paper; what's left is a few real layout bugs. I'm splitting them across three Haiku agents."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4586,"cache_read_input_tokens":210079,"output_tokens":3273,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":818},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4586,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":3273,"cache_read_input_tokens":210079,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4586,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4586},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgDY5yx8fDkwqM1GLvDKV","requestRef":"efd7c7e6-8937-4588-a154-4629a979f096","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8097d4a9-811e-4a5f-aff0-82e2febcea26","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:04:55.060Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"8097d4a9-811e-4a5f-aff0-82e2febcea26","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDY63YvtjwY37QgzFkrZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017YaWXaUQ7t1UxEjzipxQxH","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix: search/query pinned","model":"haiku","effort":"xhigh","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"Read C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\resurf\\BRIEF.md and follow it. Exception: DON'T use the T3 preview tools, which are broken. Two other agents are editing other areas of App.css/App.tsx at the same time, so use targeted Edits only. Don't commit.\n\nA visual QA of the app against Paper (p-6-0) found these TOOLBAR/SEARCH issues. Fix them using Paper's exact values (get_computed_styles on artboards 1.2 and 1.3):\n1. HIGH, 1.3 Query pinned: the pinned query chip (filter row at y≈89) sits ON TOP of the first result card. The grid doesn't move down when a query is pinned. Paper reserves a 44px filter row above the grid (masonry marginTop 52), so cards start about 100px down. Make the grid's top offset account for the filter row while a query is pinned, without re-measuring or re-virtualizing on every keystroke (only when the pinned state changes). Keep the \"N results\" count in DM Mono 12px/16px muted per Paper. \"Save as Space\" stays on that row, but must not collide with anything.\n2. MEDIUM, 1.2: the expanded search bar shows a 2px copper focus ring (`.search-field:has(input:focus-visible)`) even after a mouse click, because text inputs always match :focus-visible. Paper has no ring. The expanded glass bar is itself the focus indicator, so remove the ring for the expanded bar. Keep a visible focus style on the RESTING pill button for keyboard users.\n3. LOW: the expanded bar sits 5px right of Paper (app left 487, Paper 482 at 1440 wide), and the field's mascot slot is 22×23 where Paper has 24×20. Match them.\n\nVerify by reasoning plus targeted checks: `bunx biome check src/App.tsx src/App.css` and `bun run typecheck`. Report what changed (file:lines)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4586,"cache_read_input_tokens":210079,"output_tokens":3273,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":818},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4586,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":3273,"cache_read_input_tokens":210079,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4586,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4586},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_017YaWXaUQ7t1UxEjzipxQxH":{"description":"Fix: search/query pinned","model":"haiku","effort":"xhigh","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"Read C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\resurf\\BRIEF.md and follow it. Exception: DON'T use the T3 preview tools, which are broken. Two other agents are editing other areas of App.css/App.tsx at the same time, so use targeted Edits only. Don't commit.\n\nA visual QA of the app against Paper (p-6-0) found these TOOLBAR/SEARCH issues. Fix them using Paper's exact values (get_computed_styles on artboards 1.2 and 1.3):\n1. HIGH, 1.3 Query pinned: the pinned query chip (filter row at y≈89) sits ON TOP of the first result card. The grid doesn't move down when a query is pinned. Paper reserves a 44px filter row above the grid (masonry marginTop 52), so cards start about 100px down. Make the grid's top offset account for the filter row while a query is pinned, without re-measuring or re-virtualizing on every keystroke (only when the pinned state changes). Keep the \"N results\" count in DM Mono 12px/16px muted per Paper. \"Save as Space\" stays on that row, but must not collide with anything.\n2. MEDIUM, 1.2: the expanded search bar shows a 2px copper focus ring (`.search-field:has(input:focus-visible)`) even after a mouse click, because text inputs always match :focus-visible. Paper has no ring. The expanded glass bar is itself the focus indicator, so remove the ring for the expanded bar. Keep a visible focus style on the RESTING pill button for keyboard users.\n3. LOW: the expanded bar sits 5px right of Paper (app left 487, Paper 482 at 1440 wide), and the field's mascot slot is 22×23 where Paper has 24×20. Match them.\n\nVerify by reasoning plus targeted checks: `bunx biome check src/App.tsx src/App.css` and `bun run typecheck`. Report what changed (file:lines)."}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgDY5yx8fDkwqM1GLvDKV","requestRef":"efd7c7e6-8937-4588-a154-4629a979f096","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a831bc82-1f5d-411a-87b9-477879444e2a","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:04:58.300Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
