{"parentUuid":"d34fb2c5-b9af-4d2a-b8af-3ebfb6360d57","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDY63YvtjwY37QgzFkrZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ENFu8WPnd9vssfcNVqqTj4","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix: item view chrome","model":"haiku","effort":"xhigh","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"Read C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\resurf\\BRIEF.md and follow it. Exception: DON'T use the T3 preview tools, which are broken. Two other agents are editing other areas of App.css/App.tsx at the same time, so use targeted Edits only. Don't commit.\n\nA visual QA of the app against Paper (p-6-0, artboards 2.1, 2.2 and 2.3) found these ITEM VIEW issues (src/components/ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx and the item-view block in src/App.css):\n1. HIGH: in Electron, the fixed `.electron-window-controls` (z-index 200; Minimize/Maximize/Close at x 1302–1440, y 0–32, each 46×32) sit over the item inspector's \"Close details\" button (at ~1357,19), so the user can't reach the overlay's close button with the mouse. The library shell already reserves a top band for these controls (main padding-top 36, sidebar padding-top 39), but the item overlay ignores it. Make the overlay respect the same band, reusing the shell's existing variable or measurement rather than a new magic number, so nothing in the overlay sits under the window controls. In the web preview (no window controls) it should still look like Paper. Find how the shell decides whether the band applies (grep electron-window-controls / windowControls) and follow that.\n2. MEDIUM: Paper's library frame has 8px top and bottom padding around the stage and inspector, so the tab text sits at 25, the title at 74, and the action bar at 844–888. The app has the inspector and viewer flush to the overlay edges (tabs at 18, title at 67, action bar 851–895). Match Paper's insets: read get_computed_styles on 2.1's frame, stage and inspector.\n3. LOW: the Details row step is 26px where Paper has 25px (16px line + 9px gap). The zoom pill sits at x 624–738, y 838–874 where Paper has about x 619–733, y 840–876. Match both.\nDo NOT add the centred title pill; the user removed it on purpose. Do NOT show Delete on live (non-archived) items; that stays archive-only.\n\nChecks: `bunx biome check src/components/ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx src/App.css` and `bun run typecheck`. Report what changed (file:lines)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4586,"cache_read_input_tokens":210079,"output_tokens":3273,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":818},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4586,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":3273,"cache_read_input_tokens":210079,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4586,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4586},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01ENFu8WPnd9vssfcNVqqTj4":{"description":"Fix: item view chrome","model":"haiku","effort":"xhigh","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"Read C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\resurf\\BRIEF.md and follow it. Exception: DON'T use the T3 preview tools, which are broken. Two other agents are editing other areas of App.css/App.tsx at the same time, so use targeted Edits only. Don't commit.\n\nA visual QA of the app against Paper (p-6-0, artboards 2.1, 2.2 and 2.3) found these ITEM VIEW issues (src/components/ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx and the item-view block in src/App.css):\n1. HIGH: in Electron, the fixed `.electron-window-controls` (z-index 200; Minimize/Maximize/Close at x 1302–1440, y 0–32, each 46×32) sit over the item inspector's \"Close details\" button (at ~1357,19), so the user can't reach the overlay's close button with the mouse. The library shell already reserves a top band for these controls (main padding-top 36, sidebar padding-top 39), but the item overlay ignores it. Make the overlay respect the same band, reusing the shell's existing variable or measurement rather than a new magic number, so nothing in the overlay sits under the window controls. In the web preview (no window controls) it should still look like Paper. Find how the shell decides whether the band applies (grep electron-window-controls / windowControls) and follow that.\n2. MEDIUM: Paper's library frame has 8px top and bottom padding around the stage and inspector, so the tab text sits at 25, the title at 74, and the action bar at 844–888. The app has the inspector and viewer flush to the overlay edges (tabs at 18, title at 67, action bar 851–895). Match Paper's insets: read get_computed_styles on 2.1's frame, stage and inspector.\n3. LOW: the Details row step is 26px where Paper has 25px (16px line + 9px gap). The zoom pill sits at x 624–738, y 838–874 where Paper has about x 619–733, y 840–876. Match both.\nDo NOT add the centred title pill; the user removed it on purpose. Do NOT show Delete on live (non-archived) items; that stays archive-only.\n\nChecks: `bunx biome check src/components/ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx src/App.css` and `bun run typecheck`. Report what changed (file:lines)."}},"apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgDY5yx8fDkwqM1GLvDKV","requestRef":"efd7c7e6-8937-4588-a154-4629a979f096","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"0ad41c82-e831-4c02-94fe-30d6a51f9977","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:05:05.553Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktr