{"parentUuid":"b519ac99-f8bd-470b-b40c-d0d76bcc62d4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDY63YvtjwY37QgzFkrZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XHo43a56khmCucxJunZHfA","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix: sidebar brand mark","model":"haiku","effort":"xhigh","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"Read C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\resurf\\BRIEF.md and follow it. Exception: DON'T use the T3 preview tools, which are broken. Two other agents are editing other areas of App.css/App.tsx at the same time, so use targeted Edits only. Don't commit.\n\nA visual QA against Paper (p-6-0, artboard 1.1) found these SIDEBAR issues:\n1. MEDIUM: the brand mark renders 44×44 at (7,35). Paper's logo is 26×26 at (16,23). The sidebar keeps a 39px top padding to clear the Electron window-controls band; Paper has 18px. Keep the band (it's needed for the frameless window). Make the mascot RENDER at Paper's 26px visual size with its centre aligned to Paper's logo position relative to the first nav row, so the gap from logo to \"Everything\" matches Paper.\n   Constraint: the roam engine and src/components/mascot tests expect a single MASCOT_SIZE everywhere (it roams to the search bar and elsewhere). Prefer a CSS scale on the sidebar-docked state, or a per-anchor size the engine already supports. Don't break roaming. Read src/components/mascot/ first, and run `bun test src/components/mascot` after.\n2. LOW: the sidebar's bottom padding is 10px where Paper has 6px. Match it.\n\nChecks: `bunx biome check <files>`, `bun run typecheck`, and `bun test src/components/mascot`. Report what changed (file:lines)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4586,"cache_read_input_tokens":210079,"output_tokens":3273,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":818},"server_tool_use