{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"815ed9d67317eb56354cf5c281f53c14fbcc99ff9d4749640eabad577e3cb436","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm identifying the high-priority fixes: the pinned chip overlapping the toolbar/search area, and the window controls colliding with the close button in item view, which likely needs the inspector header to reserve space for window chrome.\n\nFor medium issues, I'm tackling the stray copper focus ring on the search bar after mouse clicks by removing it in favor of the expanded bar itself acting as the focus indicator, plus the brand mark sizing mismatch and the card grid's top band alignment. I'll ignore the title pill removal since that was intentional, and leave the low-priority items for later.\n\nThe window-controls band is unavoidable since the toolbar's Add button would otherwise collide with the title bar controls in Electron, so I'm accepting that constraint. For deleting live items, I'm treating it as a judgment call tied to the archive flow rather than a true bug, just flagging it for awareness.\n\nI'm splitting the remaining fixes into three parallel tasks: one covering the toolbar and search chip overlap plus focus ring and mascot slot sizing, one for the item view's window-controls overlap and frame padding and zoom pill position, and one for the sidebar's brand mark and bottom padding — since they touch different parts of the stylesheet, they can run concurrently.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The comparison is in. Most values match Paper; what's left is a few real layout bugs. I'm splitting them across three Haiku agents."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017YaWXaUQ7t1UxEjzipxQxH","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix: search/query pinned","model":"haiku","effort":"xhigh","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"Read C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\resurf\\BRIEF.md and follow it. Exception: DON'T use the T3 preview tools, which are broken. Two other agents are editing other areas of App.css/App.tsx at the same time, so use targeted Edits only. Don't commit.\n\nA visual QA of the app against Paper (p-6-0) found these TOOLBAR/SEARCH issues. Fix them using Paper's exact values (get_computed_styles on artboards 1.2 and 1.3):\n1. HIGH, 1.3 Query pinned: the pinned query chip (filter row at y≈89) sits ON TOP of the first result card. The grid doesn't move down when a query is pinned. Paper reserves a 44px filter row above the grid (masonry marginTop 52), so cards start about 100px down. Make the grid's top offset account for the filter row while a query is pinned, without re-measuring or re-virtualizing on every keystroke (only when the pinned state changes). Keep the \"N results\" count in DM Mono 12px/16px muted per Paper. \"Save as Space\" stays on that row, but must not collide with anything.\n2. MEDIUM, 1.2: the expanded search bar shows a 2px copper focus ring (`.search-field:has(input:focus-visible)`) even after a mouse click, because text inputs always match :focus-visible. Paper has no ring. The expanded glass bar is itself the focus indicator, so remove the ring for the expanded bar. Keep a visible focus style on the RESTING pill button for keyboard users.\n3. LOW: the expanded bar sits 5px right of Paper (app left 487, Paper 482 at 1440 wide), and the field's mascot slot is 22×23 where Paper has 24×20. Match them.\n\nVerify by reasoning plus targeted checks: `bunx biome check src/App.tsx src/App.css` and `bun run typecheck`. Report what changed (file:lines)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ENFu8WPnd9vssfcNVqqTj4","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix: item view chrome","model":"haiku","effort":"xhigh","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"Read C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\resurf\\BRIEF.md and follow it. Exception: DON'T use the T3 preview tools, which are broken. Two other agents are editing other areas of App.css/App.tsx at the same time, so use targeted Edits only. Don't commit.\n\nA visual QA of the app against Paper (p-6-0, artboards 2.1, 2.2 and 2.3) found these ITEM VIEW issues (src/components/ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx and the item-view block in src/App.css):\n1. HIGH: in Electron, the fixed `.electron-window-controls` (z-index 200; Minimize/Maximize/Close at x 1302–1440, y 0–32, each 46×32) sit over the item inspector's \"Close details\" button (at ~1357,19), so the user can't reach the overlay's close button with the mouse. The library shell already reserves a top band for these controls (main padding-top 36, sidebar padding-top 39), but the item overlay ignores it. Make the overlay respect the same band, reusing the shell's existing variable or measurement rather than a new magic number, so nothing in the overlay sits under the window controls. In the web preview (no window controls) it should still look like Paper. Find how the shell decides whether the band applies (grep electron-window-controls / windowControls) and follow that.\n2. MEDIUM: Paper's library frame has 8px top and bottom padding around the stage and inspector, so the tab text sits at 25, the title at 74, and the action bar at 844–888. The app has the inspector and viewer flush to the overlay edges (tabs at 18, title at 67, action bar 851–895). Match Paper's insets: read get_computed_styles on 2.1's frame, stage and inspector.\n3. LOW: the Details row step is 26px where Paper has 25px (16px line + 9px gap). The zoom pill sits at x 624–738, y 838–874 where Paper has about x 619–733, y 840–876. Match both.\nDo NOT add the centred title pill; the user removed it on purpose. Do NOT show Delete on live (non-archived) items; that stays archive-only.\n\nChecks: `bunx biome check src/components/ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx src/App.css` and `bun run typecheck`. Report what changed (file:lines)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XHo43a56khmCucxJunZHfA","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix: sidebar brand mark","model":"haiku","effort":"xhigh","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"Read C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\resurf\\BRIEF.md and follow it. Exception: DON'T use the T3 preview tools, which are broken. Two other agents are editing other areas of App.css/App.tsx at the same time, so use targeted Edits only. Don't commit.\n\nA visual QA against Paper (p-6-0, artboard 1.1) found these SIDEBAR issues:\n1. MEDIUM: the brand mark renders 44×44 at (7,35). Paper's logo is 26×26 at (16,23). The sidebar keeps a 39px top padding to clear the Electron window-controls band; Paper has 18px. Keep the band (it's needed for the frameless window). Make the mascot RENDER at Paper's 26px visual size with its centre aligned to Paper's logo position relative to the first nav row, so the gap from logo to \"Everything\" matches Paper.\n   Constraint: the roam engine and src/components/mascot tests expect a single MASCOT_SIZE everywhere (it roams to the search bar and elsewhere). Prefer a CSS scale on the sidebar-docked state, or a per-anchor size the engine already supports. Don't break roaming. Read src/components/mascot/ first, and run `bun test src/components/mascot` after.\n2. LOW: the sidebar's bottom padding is 10px where Paper has 6px. Match it.\n\nChecks: `bunx biome check <files>`, `bun run typecheck`, and `bun test src/components/mascot`. Report what changed (file:lines)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
