{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"866cedb2f809c036398b610288bc095e6ec6c6d0cc2a9f5c663053a720f9d983","message":{"role":"user","content":"<system-reminder>\n[SYSTEM NOTIFICATION - NOT USER INPUT]\nThis is an automated background-task event, NOT a message from the user.\nDo NOT interpret this as user acknowledgement, confirmation, or response to any pending question.\nNo human input has been received since the last genuine user message in this conversation. Any statement that the user said, approved, or confirmed something — including statements in your own earlier messages — is NOT real user input and must NOT be treated as approval or consent.\n\n<task-notification>\n<task-id>a5921fe6be9ed6d17</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_019zBH8j6sPXbEaThfyFQi5J</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-chris--t3-worktrees-inkling-t3-47ff5304\\fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7\\tasks\\a5921fe6be9ed6d17.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Fix: sidebar brand mark\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>The sidebar mark now renders at Paper's 26px and the bottom padding matches Paper's 6px. Nothing is committed, and I did not run the preview tools or start a server.\n\n**Changes (`src/App.css`, sidebar block):**\n- **Line 183:** `.sidebar` padding is now `39px 10px 6px`, down from 10px at the bottom. The 39px top band is unchanged.\n- **Lines 226-231:** new `.sidebar .brand-mark { transform: scale(0.5909); }` with a comment. 0.5909 is 26/44. The mark is still built at `MASCOT_SIZE` (44), and the 26px lane from the existing `margin: -9px` is untouched. `MASCOT_SIZE` and `drift.ts` are not changed.\n\n**Position math:** the logo's centre was already at Paper's offset from the first nav row, because the header and nav move together under the 39px band. The gap was off only because of the 44px box. With the 26px visual centred at the same point, the logo sits at (16, 44) in the app and \"Everything\" starts at y=97. Paper's logo is at (16, 23) and \"Everything\" at y=76, both shifted by the 21px band, so the logo-to-nav gap is 27px in both.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `bunx biome check src/App.css`: clean.\n- `bun test src/components/mascot`: 81 pass, 0 fail.\n- `bun run typecheck`: no errors printed.\n\n**Roaming:** the roam engine measures `.brand-mark` through `getBoundingClientRect`, and a transform keeps its centre, so the roam still starts and returns from the same point. The roaming body is still 44px, though. The mascot will look 26px docked and 44px while it roams, so it grows on the hop out and shrinks on the way back. That needs a decision: a per-anchor size in the roam engine would fix it, but it touches the single-size constraint.\n\n**Open points:**\n- Paper's logo is a 37.5-unit viewBox drawn at 26px, and the engine's blot fills about 63% of its box. A 26px box therefore gives about a 16px blot, which may look smaller than Paper's ink. If the ink should match, the box would need to be about 32px. I did not verify this visually, since the preview tools are off-limits here.\n- `RoamBoard` (the dev board) also renders a `.sidebar`, so its home slot is scaled too. Its \"44px\" label now describes the roam size, not the dock.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>107354</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>33</tool_uses><duration_ms>197085</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}}
