{"parentUuid":"83025dce-47b4-4e6c-a8e9-80d697575b05","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"stop_hook_summary","hookCount":1,"hookInfos":[{"command":"sh -c 'if ! command -v entire >/dev/null 2>&1; then exit 0; fi; exec entire hooks claude-code stop'","durationMs":4641}],"hookErrors":[],"hookAdditionalContext":[],"preventedContinuation":false,"stopReason":"","hasOutput":false,"level":"suggestion","timestamp":"2026-10-20T20:36:11.022Z","uuid":"bf33e710-0059-41e3-a203-a08a827b12cd","toolUseID":"d0d553d0-0c07-40d2-b818-9cbce0cadff5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-20T20:36:15.951Z","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>acf24f7195dd9971b</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01RGmuZcfrzWtT2BTQjJYxPa</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-chris--t3-worktrees-inkling-t3-47ff5304\\fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7\\tasks\\acf24f7195dd9971b.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Fix: item view chrome\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All three item-view issues are fixed in the code, but I have not checked them in the running app. The checks are static only. Biome passes and the typecheck printed no errors. I did not commit.\n\n**1. Window controls over \"Close details\" (HIGH)**\n- `src/components/ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx:726-735`: `frameRect()` starts the overlay at the frame's top plus its computed `padding-top`. That is the same band the shell reserves for the window controls (`calc(4px + var(--titlebar-height))`, App.css:625). The offset applies only when `isElectronRuntime()` is true, the same helper that sets the `electron-shell` class. In the web preview the overlay stays flush at y=0, as in Paper.\n- `src/App.css:3792-3796`: focus mode is full-window and its Exit button sat at top 22, under the controls too. In the desktop app only, it now uses `calc(4px + var(--titlebar-height))`.\n\n**2. Paper insets (MEDIUM)**\nPaper 2.1 values, read with get_computed_styles:\n- Frame: `paddingBlock: 8px`, no border.\n- Viewer well: x=0, y=8, width 888.\n- Inspector: x=888 (320 wide), y=8, padding 6/16/4/18, gap 20.\n- Zoom pill: bottom 16, centred in the viewer.\n\nChanges:\n- `src/App.css:5327-5331`: removed the overlay's own 1px border. It shifted the stage and inspector by a pixel, which is why the pill sat at 838. Paper's frame has no border.\n- `src/App.css:5343`: stage inset `8px 320px 8px 0` (was `8px 320px 8px 8px`).\n- `src/App.css:5433` and `:5435`: inspector `top: 8px` and `bottom: 8px` (were 0).\n- `src/App.css:3800-3802`: the note-editing inspector stays flush (`top: 0; bottom: 0`), so the editor and focus mode don't shift.\n\nWith these, the computed positions are: tabs at about 25, title at 74, action bar at 844–888.\n\n**3. Details row step (LOW)**\n- `src/App.css:5612`: `line-height: 16px` on `.item-details dl`. With the existing 9px gap, the step is 25px.\n- Zoom pill: Paper's computed position is x 619–733, y 839–875. The app's pill should match after the border and inset changes. I did not re-measure it.\n\n**Not changed (outside the three items, or not verified)**\n- **Toolbar:** Paper's back/forward is a flush 52px row at the viewer's top-left. The app keeps a floating glass pill at top 10 and left 10.\n- **Stage padding:** Paper is 12px top, 70px bottom, 40px sides. The app is 72/72/40, so the image centre is about 3px off.\n- **Narrow windows:** at 780px and below, the shell drops `.main-content` padding-top to 12px. The overlay follows that measurement, so the window controls still overlap the shell's own header there. This is a shell-wide issue. Electron's minimum width is 320px, so the range is reachable.\n- **Not run:** I did not use the preview tools and did not launch the full app, so there is no screenshot and the Paper comparison is numbers only. The overlay-band change is the one to check first in the packaged app.\n- **Untouched:** no centred title pill, and Delete still appears only for archived items.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>164764</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>48</tool_uses><duration_ms>352086</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
