{"parentUuid":"377475da-3163-4995-91d4-fcc67305acbd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEBRiudoJU6wberH1sWJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VCqaumbafmSJttHwZEmSe4","name":"mcp__t3-code__delegate_task","input":{"task":"READ-ONLY VERIFICATION. Don't edit files, commit, or run servers. Repo worktree: C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304 (branch feat/glass-surface, HEAD fb487dd; `origin/main` is the base). Read AGENTS.md first, especially the performance section and the \"no continuously repainting animations (mascot excepted)\" rule.\n\nAnother agent produced the performance audit below. For EACH finding, verify it against the actual code and give one verdict:\n- TRUE-FIX: real and worth fixing;\n- TRUE-INTENTIONAL: real but a deliberate design or product choice, e.g. the liquid glass is the redesign's look and the mascot is explicitly allowed to animate;\n- PARTLY TRUE: say which part;\n- FALSE: the code doesn't do that.\n\nFor each finding, give:\n(a) file:line evidence (quote the key lines briefly);\n(b) whether the issue already exists on origin/main or was introduced by this branch (`git diff origin/main...HEAD -- <file>`, `git show origin/main:<file>`);\n(c) the realistic impact for a library of about 2,000 items on Windows;\n(d) for TRUE-FIX, the smallest fix that keeps behaviour and design intact, with a rough size (S/M/L).\nBe skeptical. Measure where you can cheaply: count the backdrop-filter layers that are actually over the scrolling grid; check whether the 30s reload diffs or replaces; check whether file capture really sends a number array over IPC (Array.from on a Uint8Array); check whether the embedding search is brute force on the main thread; check whether the job-status query uses an IN list with every id, and SQLite's variable limit; check whether the asset protocol handler supports range requests and cache headers; and check whether getLibrarySize is called with refresh=true every time Settings opens.\n\nTHE AUDIT (verbatim):\n---\nThe big ones\n- Glass over moving content. The top toolbar, history/view pills, search field, and a 120px full-width bottom fade all blur what's behind them. Cards scroll directly underneath, so the blur is recomputed continuously. The top bar combines 18px blur with saturation and brightness, and the bottom fade adds two more blur layers. This is the main cost while scrolling.\n- The whole library reloads on a timer. Every 30 seconds — and again after background-job updates settle (400ms trailing pause) — the app re-fetches every item and every item's job status, rebuilds every card object, and re-renders the visible grid.\n- File capture handles the entire file up front. Picking or dropping a file reads it completely into the UI, expands it into an array of individual numbers, sends that across, then writes it and, for images, builds the thumbnail before the card appears.\nWhile browsing\n- Opening an item animates its position and size. The overlay and everything inside it — image, inspector, toolbar — recalculates layout on every frame of the open/close flight. Animating a scaled/translated snapshot would be much cheaper.\n- Switching grid/list clones every visible card. Each clone includes its image, and each clone is measured repeatedly.\n- Opening or closing the sidebar animates width and padding, so the whole grid reflows for the full 300ms.\n- Panning a zoomed image re-renders the viewer on every pointer move instead of just moving the image.\n- Every new search result remounts the entire masonry grid. That recreates all visible cards and images and resets video/embed state.\nSearch and data\n- Semantic search reads and compares every stored embedding in one pass, on the same part of the app that serves files and handles storage.\n- Every refresh asks for job statuses for every item in one query. Large libraries create a very large query and can hit the database's limit.\n- The Archive tab loads, converts, and draws every archived item at once, and requests job summaries for all of them.\nFiles, media, and settings\n- The local asset handler reads each requested file fully into memory, with no cache headers and no range support.\n- Locally saved video cards load the real video file just to show a frame.\n- Opening Settings walks every asset file one at a time to compute library size, every time. The backend has a cache, but the UI always asks for a fresh scan.\nBackground\n- The mascot redraws a detailed SVG through React on every animation frame, in two places, all the time, even when idle or the sidebar is collapsed.\n---\n\nOutput: a table (finding | verdict | from main or branch | impact | fix and size), then a short ranked list of what you'd actually fix, in the order you'd fix it. Keep prose tight.","target":{"providerInstanceId":"codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","options":{"reasoningEffort":"high"}},"mode":"async","role":"research","clientRequestId":"perf-audit-verify-r1","title":"Verify performance audit"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2670,"cache_read_input_tokens":250921,"output_tokens":1911,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":169},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2670,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1911,"cache_read_input_tokens":250921,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2670,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2670},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VCqaumbaf