{"parentUuid":"65340897-67d7-44ed-8809-bd65d4b3a788","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"dd67321c-7887-433f-ba1a-4fdb0f76fc50","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Delegated task node:delegated-task:command%3Amcp%3A2dd0b88d-eaff-4e1a-b29c-2ffb930c8d61%3Adelegate-task%3Aperf-audit-verify-r1 (Verify performance audit) [completed]:\nRead-only verification complete. I made no edits, commits, or server runs. At 2,000 items, the main library grid is virtualized; several costs in the audit affect only visible cards or brief transitions, not 2,000 mounted cards.\n\n| Finding | Verdict | From main or branch | Impact at ~2,000 items on Windows | Fix and size |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Glass over scrolling content | **TRUE-INTENTIONAL** | **Branch:** three glass controls; the two-layer bottom fade already exists on `origin/main`. | In the usual grid view, three controls plus two fade layers put **five backdrop-filter layers** over scrolling cards. This can make scrolling more GPU-intensive, but the glass look is intentional. | — |\n| 30-second and job-event reloads | **PARTLY TRUE** | **Main.** | A refresh fetches all listed items, queries their job summaries, converts every item, and passes a new array to the grid. Visible cards can rerender. But the ID-based grid key stays stable when results are unchanged, so it does **not** remount the whole grid every time. The grid is virtualized. | Keep the fallback refresh, but reconcile unchanged items by stable identity and update job summaries incrementally. **M** |\n| File capture reads and sends the whole file | **TRUE-FIX** | **Main.** | `Array.from(Uint8Array)` expands each byte into a JS number before IPC; a 50 MB file can create substantial memory and copy overhead. Image thumbnail generation is awaited before the item is returned and shown. | Send an `ArrayBuffer`/`Uint8Array` over IPC and make thumbnail work a background job after the item is saved. **M** |\n| Opening an item animates its position and size | **PARTLY TRUE** | **Main:** the rectangle flight already existed; this branch changes the overlay presentation. | GSAP animates the dialog’s `left/top/width/height` for one brief flight. That can trigger layout, but the inspector is hidden during the flight, so “everything inside recalculates” overstates it. The cost is limited to opening or closing one item. | — |\n| Grid/list switch clones and measures visible cards | **TRUE-INTENTIONAL** | **Main.** | It clones mounted cards, including media, and reads layout several times during the transition. Virtualization limits this to the visible set; cost is transient and only on a view switch. | — |\n| Sidebar animation reflows the grid | **TRUE-INTENTIONAL** | **Main.** | The 300 ms width/padding transitions change the main content geometry and cause grid layout work, but only during an occasional sidebar toggle. | — |\n| Panning a zoomed image rerenders on pointer move | **PARTLY TRUE** | **Main.** | Each pointer move updates React state, but the state belongs to the image-stage component; it does not rerender the whole overlay. The image transform changes during the drag. | — |\n| Search results remount the masonry grid | **TRUE-INTENTIONAL** | **Main.** | A changed result-ID list changes `libraryGridKey`, remounting the virtualized grid and resetting mounted card state. This avoids position-keyed cards showing the wrong item after filtering. Only mounted cards and their media are recreated. | — |\n| Semantic search brute-forces embeddings on the main process | **TRUE-INTENTIONAL** | **Main.** | The main process loads matching vectors and scores them in a loop. At 2,000 items this is a few million vector operations, likely modest; it can briefly occupy the process that also handles storage and asset requests. A vector index is not justified at this scale without evidence of a delay. | — |\n| Job statuses use one `IN` list of every item ID | **PARTLY TRUE** | **Main.** | The query binds one parameter per item. The local Node SQLite build reports `MAX_VARIABLE_NUMBER=32766`, so 2,000 IDs are below that limit; the Electron package’s embedded build was not queried separately. The query is still linear in library size and could exceed a lower-limit build or a much larger library. | Batch IDs if libraries approach the runtime limit. **S**, but not urgent at 2,000. |\n| Archive loads and renders all archived items | **TRUE-FIX** | **Main.** | Opening Settings fetches all archived items and summaries, converts them, then renders every archived card in a regular grid. A large archive can make Settings open slowly and create many DOM nodes; this path is not virtualized. | Load when the Archive tab opens and virtualize its cards. **M** |\n| Asset handler reads full files; no range or cache headers | **TRUE-FIX** | **Main.** | Each GET reads the entire requested asset into memory and returns no range or cache headers. Thumbnails are usually small, but videos and PDFs can be large; concurrent visible media can increase memory use. | Stream files and support byte ranges; add suitable local asset cache headers. **M** |\n| Local video cards load the video file to show a frame | **TRUE-FIX** | **Main.** | Cards render a `<video>` using `item.fileUrl` with `preload=\"metadata\"` and seek to 0.01s. Only visible cards do this, but the current asset handler turns that request into a full-file read. | Generate a small poster in background and use it in the card; load the original in the detail view. **M** |\n| Settings recomputes library size on every open | **TRUE-FIX** | **Branch:** the size API/cache and Settings call are new here. | `getLibrarySize()` defaults to `refresh=true`; the backend recursively stats files sequentially, bypassing its cached result. With thousands of assets, Settings opening can wait on thousands of filesystem operations. | Use a short-lived cached value on open and refresh it asynchronously or after library writes. **S/M** |\n| Mascot continuously redraws in two places | **TRUE-INTENTIONAL** | **Main.** | The shared mascot loop samples a frame each animation frame and updates subscribed figures, including the sidebar and search mascot. It pauses for hidden tabs and reduced motion, but can keep running while the sidebar is collapsed. This is explicitly allowed by AGENTS.md. | — |\n\n**What I’d fix first:**\n\n1. Remove the file-capture byte-array expansion and stop waiting for image thumbnails before showing the saved item.\n2. Add streaming and range support to the local asset handler; it currently magnifies video loading costs.\n3. Avoid rebuilding unchanged library items on every periodic or job-event refresh.\n4. Virtualize the Archive view and defer loading it until that tab is selected.\n5. Stop forcing a sequential asset scan whenever Settings opens; refresh the size in the background or after writes.\n\nI’d leave the glass and one-shot transition costs alone for now; they are deliberate visual choices with bounded impact. The job-status parameter limit is not a practical issue at 2,000 items, though batching is a small future-proofing option."},"uuid":"4b3fe90d-4352-4de0-9445-8b946c971c36","timestamp":"2026-10-20T21:20:46.037Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","promptSource":"sdk","turnOrigin":"sdk","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":0,"turnIndex":115},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
