{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"fa04983df1fade167a38ee5ba9f4b932e229cdbc894f992b8066d8fa84ad9b74","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to lay out the plan: fix the settings size issue on this branch first, then push feat/glass-surface since stacking requires it, and then create the perf branch from it in a separate worktree so the agents working on it don't collide with the UI branch work.\n\nFor the worktree setup, I'll create it manually with a new branch off feat/glass-surface and run bun install inside it before handing it to the agents. I'm assigning backend-heavy tasks like the capture fix, asset handler streaming, and video poster generation to Sonnet since they touch electron/main.mjs, while the archive virtualization work goes to Haiku since it's frontend-centered -- though I need to watch for conflicts since multiple backend tasks touch the same main.mjs file.\n\nI'm thinking the video poster could use nativeImage.createThumbnailFromPath, which supports video thumbnails on Windows/macOS via the shell, avoiding the need for ffmpeg. To reduce conflicts, I'll split Sonnet's work into two sequential pieces -- one handling capture (App.tsx, preload, main ipc, storage) and another handling the asset handler streaming/range plus the video poster -- while Haiku works in parallel on archive lazy loading and virtualization.\n\nFor commits, since all agents share one worktree, I'm worried about `git add -A` sweeping up other agents' uncommitted work, especially where App.tsx is touched by multiple agents. I think the simplest fix is to have agents not commit at all, and instead I'll commit everything myself at the end, grouping by file where separable and combining otherwise, since interactive per-hunk staging isn't something the agents can do themselves.\n\nI'll keep bypassing the hanging commit hook via core.hooksPath since the user already approved skipping it. For the small settings size fix on the UI branch, it makes more sense to just do that myself since it's small and the delegation rule only restricts the heavier parallel work to Sonnet/Haiku — I'll look at the code and handle it directly before stacking the perf branch on top.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Bw2xnrYyoKfDrvjJ5jHpCR","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && sed -n 3920,3960p src/App.tsx && sed -n 250,270p src/lib/libraryApi.ts && grep -n \"refresh\\|cache\" electron/library-size.mjs | head -20","description":"Read the Settings size loading code"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
