{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"2c148e99aaa187ccc76d5196b8c769ee3c7e70a1faae031209de04d89a479e5b","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm tracing through the get/refresh logic to confirm it returns the right promise when there's no cached value, then planning the fix: load the version and last export immediately, and show the cached library size (or trigger a first scan) before refreshing further.\n\nThen the plan is to show the cached value right away and kick off a non-blocking background refresh deduped by the `refreshing` guard, which is good enough for now. I also want to flip the `refresh` parameter's default to false for safety, since Settings is the only caller.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The Settings size fix is small and on this branch, so I'll make it myself first. Then I'll push and stack the performance branch on top."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Lve3g5reoGjMAWdaEZTpKk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && python - <<'EOF'\np=\"src/App.tsx\"; s=open(p,encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\nold='''  // Version, size and last copy are optional: each stays hidden when the\n  // desktop backend cannot supply it (preview, or a failed call).\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (!isSettingsOpen || !isDesktopRuntime()) return;\n    let cancelled = false;\n    void Promise.all([\n      getAppVersion().catch(() => undefined),\n      getLibrarySize().catch(() => undefined),\n      getLastExport().catch(() => undefined),\n    ]).then(([version, size, copy]) => {\n      if (cancelled) return;\n      setAppVersion(version ?? null);\n      setLibrarySizeBytes(size?.bytes ?? null);\n      setLastCopy(copy ?? null);\n    });\n    return () => {\n      cancelled = true;\n    };\n  }, [isSettingsOpen]);'''\nnew='''  // Version, size and last copy are optional: each stays hidden when the\n  // desktop backend cannot supply it (preview, or a failed call). The size\n  // walks every asset file, so Settings shows the last measured value at once\n  // and replaces it when a fresh walk finishes, without holding up the rest.\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (!isSettingsOpen || !isDesktopRuntime()) return;\n    let cancelled = false;\n    void Promise.all([\n      getAppVersion().catch(() => undefined),\n      getLastExport().catch(() => undefined),\n    ]).then(([version, copy]) => {\n      if (cancelled) return;\n      setAppVersion(version ?? null);\n      setLastCopy(copy ?? null);\n    });\n    const showSize = (size: LibrarySize | undefined) => {\n      if (!cancelled && size) setLibrarySizeBytes(size.bytes);\n    };\n    void getLibrarySize()\n      .then(showSize)\n      .then(() => getLibrarySize(true))\n      .then(showSize)\n      .catch(() => undefined);\n    return () => {\n      cancelled = true;\n    };\n  }, [isSettingsOpen]);'''\nassert s.count(old)==1\ns=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\",newline=\"\").write(s)\np=\"src/lib/libraryApi.ts\"; s=open(p,encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\ns=s.replace(\"export async function getLibrarySize(refresh = true) {\",\"export async function getLibrarySize(refresh = false) {\",1)\nopen(p,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\",newline=\"\").write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"LibrarySize\" src/App.tsx | head -5","description":"Show cached library size first, refresh in background"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
