{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"42f37d8d7451eb4e48ca81c799927cd92af9086e2859645ee2b404891c86bd2c","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to import the LibrarySize type into that import block, and I'm noticing a bug where calling getLibrarySize twice on first open triggers two separate directory walks since the refreshing flag resets after the first completes. I should fix the backend logic so the second call reuses the in-flight walk instead of starting a new one.\n\nActually, if I fire both calls concurrently instead of sequentially, the refresh call reuses the in-flight walk when there's no cache, so it collapses into a single walk; when cache exists, the cached call resolves immediately while the fresh walk proceeds separately. That resolves the duplicate-walk concern cleanly without extra backend complexity.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KzVDtrFNzhESdBtbpaLYqe","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && python - <<'EOF'\np=\"src/App.tsx\"; s=open(p,encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\nold='''    void getLibrarySize()\n      .then(showSize)\n      .then(() => getLibrarySize(true))\n      .then(showSize)\n      .catch(() => undefined);'''\nnew='''    // Fired together so a first open, with nothing cached yet, shares one walk.\n    void getLibrarySize().then(showSize, () => undefined);\n    void getLibrarySize(true).then(showSize, () => undefined);'''\nassert s.count(old)==1\ns=s.replace(old,new)\ns=s.replace(\"  getLibrarySize,\\n\",\"  getLibrarySize,\\n  type LibrarySize,\\n\",1)\nopen(p,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\",newline=\"\").write(s)\nEOF\nsed -n 80,95p src/App.tsx; bunx biome check src/App.tsx src/lib/libraryApi.ts 2>&1 | tail -3; bun run typecheck >/tmp/tc.log 2>&1; echo tc=$?; tail -3 /tmp/tc.log","description":"Fire size calls together, add type import, check"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
