{"parentUuid":"2942c70d-45ec-4fea-ace9-cf72d86a6dda","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgECQB34vCGNqK4CjsG8o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to set up a separate perf worktree outside the current one and install dependencies there, then dispatch agents to work in parallel. I should think through potential conflicts since several agents will likely touch App.tsx, the capture and archive logic, video posters, and the electron asset handler.\n\nSince they're sharing a worktree, I'll instruct agents to use Edit (exact string replacement) rather than Write on shared files, avoid committing or running state-changing git commands, and skip repo-wide formatting — I'll handle the commit myself at the end. A separate worktree per agent would avoid conflicts but adds merge overhead, so shared worktree with edit discipline is faster.\n\nI'll assign Sonnet to the more backend-heavy work (capture, asset handler, video posters) and Haiku to the frontend archive task, then write self-contained briefs for each agent so they don't need to dig through context themselves. First step is just creating the worktree.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":506,"cache_read_input_tokens":57272,"output_tokens":678,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":443},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":506,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":678,"cache_read_input_tokens":57272,"cache_creation_input_tokens":506,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":506},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.con