{"parentUuid":"b3dd5284-2241-4319-addc-673a7031d18e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgECTEFcqqvjeVmM9Xu48","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01W5BJdWdC7FXNtWgzpoypER","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Stream asset protocol with ranges","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"You are fixing one performance problem in inkling, an Electron + React + TypeScript + Vite app with node:sqlite in the main process (Bun 1.4.2). Read AGENTS.md at the worktree root first. Its rules apply.\n\nWORKSPACE: C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\perf-library-io (branch perf/library-io). Work ONLY there. Never touch any other worktree or the live library. Three other agents are editing this same worktree right now:\n- one on capture IPC and background thumbnails;\n- one on video posters;\n- one on the Settings Archive tab.\nMake targeted edits with the Edit tool only. Never rewrite a shared file with Write, especially electron/main.mjs, which others are also editing. If an edit fails because the text moved, re-read and retry. Run NO git commands that change state (no add, commit, checkout, stash, reset or restore). The maintainer commits. Do not launch dev servers or Electron.\n\nTASK: the custom asset protocol handler in electron/main.mjs (around line 325, `const body = request.method === \"HEAD\" ? null : await readFile(realFile);`) reads the whole file into memory for every request. It also has no Range support, so a large local video or PDF is read fully before a byte is served, and video seeking can't work properly.\n- Stream the file instead (fs.createReadStream turned into a web stream via Readable.toWeb, or whatever works with Electron's protocol.handle Response).\n- Support single byte-range requests: 206 with Content-Range, and 416 with `Content-Range: bytes */size` for unsatisfiable ranges. Send Accept-Ranges: bytes and Content-Length. Keep HEAD working.\n- Keep every existing security check exactly as strict: realpath containment inside the assets directory, method checks and content types.\n- Caching: find out whether asset paths are immutable. Thumbnails may be regenerated at the same path. Only add cache headers that are correct and actually help for a custom protocol in Electron (ETag/Last-Modified from stat, for example). Don't add headers that do nothing, and say what you chose and why.\n- Move the request-to-response logic into a small module (e.g. electron/asset-response.mjs) so it can be tested without Electron, and keep main.mjs wiring thin.\n\nTESTS: add focused bun tests covering:\n- a full GET with the streamed body;\n- HEAD;\n- valid ranges, including open-ended `bytes=100-` and suffix `bytes=-100`;\n- an unsatisfiable range giving 416;\n- a malformed range giving a full 200;\n- path escape and symlink containment still rejected.\nRun `bun test <your test file>`, `bunx biome check <changed files>`, and `bun run typecheck`. Check the exit code with `echo $?`, not through a pipe. If typecheck errors are only in files another agent is editing, say so instead of fixing them.\n\nCode style: match the surrounding code. Comments only say why. No new dependencies.\n\nREPORT (under 200 words): files changed, the response behavior, the caching decision and why, tests run with results, and anything left unfinished."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":594,"cache_read_input_tokens":58621,"output_tokens":6896,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1859},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":594,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6896,"cache_read_input_tokens":58621,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5