en-ended `bytes=100-` and suffix `bytes=-100`;\n- an unsatisfiable range giving 416;\n- a malformed range giving a full 200;\n- path escape and symlink containment still rejected.\nRun `bun test <your test file>`, `bunx biome check <changed files>`, and `bun run typecheck`. Check the exit code with `echo $?`, not through a pipe. If typecheck errors are only in files another agent is editing, say so instead of fixing them.\n\nCode style: match the surrounding code. Comments only say why. No new dependencies.\n\nREPORT (under 200 words): files changed, the response behavior, the caching decision and why, tests run with results, and anything left unfinished.","outputFile":"C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-chris--t3-worktrees-inkling-t3-47ff5304\\fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7\\tasks\\a7fa55df09eb18dc9.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8cc8ddcf-cd36-4a0f-a2df-d7067a9a3bfd","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"1efb5573-523b-47e3-9132-6cdb616239e8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgECTEFcqqvjeVmM9Xu48","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0139YeE4p2jvqX4a9NqDXvm6","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Background video posters for cards","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"You are fixing one performance problem in inkling, an Electron + React + TypeScript + Vite app with node:sqlite in the main process (Bun 1.4.2). Read AGENTS.md at the worktree root first. Its rules apply, especially \"capture is instant\" and \"visual by type\".\n\nWORKSPACE: C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\perf-library-io (branch perf/library-io). Work ONLY there. Never touch any other worktree or the live library. Three other agents are editing this same worktree right now:\n- one on capture IPC plus moving IMAGE thumbnails to a background job (it touches electron/storage.mjs, ai-jobs.mjs, thumbnail.mjs, main.mjs and the capture code in App.tsx);\n- one on the asset protocol handler in main.mjs;\n- one on the Settings Archive tab in App.tsx.\nMake targeted edits with the Edit tool only. Never rewrite a shared file with Write. If an edit fails because the text moved, re-read and retry. If the image-thumbnail agent has added a background thumbnail job by the time you get there, reuse it for posters instead of building a parallel mechanism. Otherwise keep your additions self-contained so the two can be merged. Run NO git commands that change state (no add, commit, checkout, stash, reset or restore). The maintainer commits. Do not launch dev servers or Electron.\n\nTASK: local video file cards in the grid load the real video file just to show a frame. Look in src/components/ItemMedia.tsx and the card code in src/App.tsx for a <video> with preload or similar. Each card pulls a large file through the asset protocol.\n- Generate a poster image in the background for local video items and store it as the item's thumbnail asset, the way image thumbnails are stored.\n- Run it at capture, never blocking it. Also backfill existing local video items that have no poster, lazily or via the job queue, without a startup stall.\n- Electron's nativeImage.createThumbnailFromPath uses the Windows/macOS shell thumbnailer and needs no new dependency, so prefer it. On Linux, where it's unavailable, or on failure, leave the item without a poster. Do not add ffmpeg or any dependency.\n- The card should show the poster image. The video file loads only in the detail view or on play.\n- Without a poster, the card currently shows an empty dark tile with a tiny pill. It should show the shared video type artwork instead (see TypedArtwork in ItemMedia.tsx). Keep shared thumbnail logic in one place.\n- Video embed links (YouTube etc.) already have remote thumbnails. Leave them alone and do not add network calls.\n- Preview mode (`bun run dev`, sample data, no backend) must still render video cards sensibly.\n\nTESTS: add focused bun tests for the poster job logic:\n- a poster gets written and recorded;\n- failure keeps the item and doesn't retry forever;\n- backfill picks only local videos without posters.\nStub nativeImage. Run `bun test <files you touched>`, `bunx biome check <changed files>`, and `bun run typecheck`. Check the exit code with `echo $?`, not through a pipe. If typecheck errors are only in files another agent is editing, say so instead of fixing them.\n\nCode style: match the surrounding code. Comments only say why. No new dependencies.\n\nREPORT (under 200 words): files changed, how and when posters are generated and backfilled, what cards show with and without a poster, tests run with results, and anything left unfinished."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":594,"cache_read_input_tokens":58621,"