{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-20T21:43:33.120Z","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a0034157f14c1d64c</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01DmbtxzHXdwcbWr3U8JrTBf</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-chris--t3-worktrees-inkling-t3-47ff5304\\fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7\\tasks\\a0034157f14c1d64c.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Lazy load and virtualize Archive tab\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Archive tab work is done in `perf/library-io`. Nothing was committed.\n\n**Changed:** `src/App.tsx` (targeted edits), `src/App.css` (removed the `auto-fill` line, since columns are now set inline), new `src/components/ArchiveGrid.tsx`, new `src/components/archiveGridWindow.ts` and its test.\n\n**When it loads:** only while the Archive tab is shown, and again each time that tab opens. Restore and delete still update the list locally, as they did before. Nothing re-reads the backend there.\n\n**Virtualization:** the grid mounts only the rows near the scroll position, plus 3 overscan rows, and uses spacers for the rest. It stays a CSS grid, so tile size, spacing, and row-major tab order are unchanged. I did not use VirtuosoMasonry. It would stretch tiles and put tab order column-major.\n\n**Processing summaries:** no longer fetched on archive load. Archive tiles hide their processing text, and an opened item fetches its own summary. Restore still fetches them for the main grid.\n\n**Checks:** `bun test` on the new test (6 pass), Biome on the four files (exit 0), `bun run typecheck` (exit 0).\n\n**Left open:** no UI pass, because I did not launch the app. The tab count shows only after the Archive tab has loaded. Keyboard Tab stops at the overscan edge.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>175982</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>31</tool_uses><duration_ms>179482</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
