{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","prNumber":170,"prUrl":"https://github.com/Squidys-Tools/inkling/pull/170","prRepository":"Squidys-Tools/inkling","timestamp":"2026-10-20T21:43:43.192Z"}
{"parentUuid":"e49a1892-2304-4a1f-bb3e-356f9f958142","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEDfgHkDNXsVCMkW9ZKo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm weighing some minor tradeoffs: the hardcoded pixel constants mirroring CSS are a bit fragile but documented well enough to leave alone, and the tab count still requires reading the full item list each time, which is a small inefficiency worth flagging to the user but not critical to fix now.\n\nI'm also noting the archive list resets to unloaded each time Settings opens, causing a brief empty flash, and I can't fully verify the scroll wrapper structure without a UI pass in preview with seed data. I'll plan to do that verification at the end, but for now there's nothing else to act on while waiting for the other pieces to come in.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3656,"cache_read_input_tokens":80686,"output_tokens":802,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":463},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3656,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":802,"cache_read_input_tokens":80686,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3656,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3656},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7613,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEDfg1dF4p1cA6DVD1zK","requestRef":"9e978f03-05e6-4d57-89c8-f6fd3bbe2717","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"21dcc29b-1ba0-469e-b52f-35f848c11173","timestamp":"2026-10-20T21:43:52.503Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"21dcc29b-1ba0-469e-b52f-35f848c11173","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEDfgHkDNXsVCMkW9ZKo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Archive tab change is done and I've reviewed it:\n- **When it loads:** only while the Archive tab is open, and again each time you open it. It no longer loads with Settings or fetches processing details for every item.\n- **Rendering:** only the rows near the scroll position are drawn, so the grid's tile size, spacing and tab order stay the same.\n- **Checks:** its 6 tests pass, and Biome and typecheck are clean. It hasn't been looked at in the app yet; I'll do that in the UI pass.\n\nTwo side effects are worth knowing about:\n- **Tab count:** the number next to \"Archive\" now only shows after you open that tab, because nothing reads the archive before then. Showing it earlier would need a cheap count query in the backend.\n- **Row sizes:** `src/components/ArchiveGrid.tsx` hard-codes the tile and row sizes from `App.css`. If those styles change without it, rows will drift while scrolling. A comment there says so.\n\nI'm still waiting on the video poster and capture agents."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3656,"cache_read_input_tokens":80686,"output_tokens":802,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":463},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3656,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":802,"cache_read_input_tokens":80686,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3656,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3656},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgEDfg1dF4p1cA6DVD1zK","requestRef":"9e978f03-05e6-4d57-89c8-f6fd3bbe2717","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"44204c0f-798f-4e0f-a717-affa43f1b39d","timestamp":"2026-10-20T21:43:52.515Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
