{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-20T21:44:07.212Z","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a326fa48b5bd9febf</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01NJsA5vxuKRGpkL92Czyxj9</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-chris--t3-worktrees-inkling-t3-47ff5304\\fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7\\tasks\\a326fa48b5bd9febf.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Background video posters for cards\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Local video cards now show a background-generated poster in the grid instead of loading the video file.\n\n**Correction to the handoff:** I never edited `electron/thumbnail.mjs`. The `inspectImage` changes there are the image-thumbnail agent's, and I left them alone.\n\n**Files changed**\n- `electron/video-poster.mjs` (new)\n- `electron/storage.mjs`\n- `electron/ai-jobs.mjs`\n- `src/App.tsx`\n- `src/App.css`\n- `src/components/ItemMedia.tsx`\n- `electron/video-poster.test.ts` (new)\n\n**Generation**\n- `saveFile` queues a silent `video_poster` job ahead of the embedding job, so capture never waits on it. Imported videos with no thumbnail get one too.\n- The job calls `nativeImage.createThumbnailFromPath` at 512px and stores the result as `thumbnail.webp`. I generalised `storePdfThumbnail` into one shared function; the PDF path still works.\n- If the shell returns nothing or throws (including Linux), the job retries 3 times, then fails for good. The item stays and the card keeps the typed artwork.\n\n**Backfill:** `onIdle` enqueues one candidate at a time. It picks only videos with a local file, no thumbnail and no earlier failed poster job.\n\n**Cards**\n- With a poster: the image and pill, as before. No `&lt;video&gt;` is loaded in the grid any more.\n- Without one: the typed `FileArtwork` (\"VIDEO\", title) using the `file-card` layout. This also covers embeds with no poster, and preview mode (the sample clip now shows typed artwork).\n- Layout: the card is 300px tall without a poster and 190px with one, so it shrinks when the poster arrives.\n- The detail `&lt;video&gt;` now has `poster`.\n- I removed the dead `.video-art` CSS.\n\n**Tests:** `bun test electron/video-poster.test.ts` gives 6 pass. They cover the poster being written and recorded, three failure modes that stop retrying, and backfill picking only the right videos. `bunx biome check` on the changed files and `bun run typecheck` both exit 0.\n\n**Not verified**\n- 12 tests in `ai-jobs.test.ts` and `storage.test.ts` fail. Eleven fail because `saveFile` now rejects `number[]` bytes, which is the capture agent's change, so those tests need `Uint8Array`. One is a Windows path-separator assertion in `storage.test.ts`. A scratch run confirmed the refactored PDF thumbnail path still works.\n- Nothing was run in the real app or on a real video.\n- I skipped the changelog line because AGENTS.md says to ask first.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>176622</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>38</tool_uses><duration_ms>217363</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
