{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-20T21:47:07.425Z","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a8023c2e81f48683f</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01W4W8sRGFQTm1ozWUyuSbyE</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-chris--t3-worktrees-inkling-t3-47ff5304\\fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7\\tasks\\a8023c2e81f48683f.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Capture bytes and background thumbnails\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Image capture now returns right after the original is written, and the thumbnail comes from a background job. Tests, Biome and `bun run typecheck` pass, except one `storage.test.ts` test that fails on Windows (below).\n\n**Files changed**\n- `electron/thumbnail.mjs`, `storage.mjs`, `ai-jobs.mjs`, `main.mjs`\n- `src/lib/libraryApi.ts`, `src/App.tsx`, `src/components/ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx`\n- `docs/changelog.md`\n- Tests: `thumbnail.test.ts`, `storage.test.ts`, `ai-jobs.test.ts`\n- `preload.cjs` and `electron.d.ts` needed no change; they pass args straight through.\n\n**Bytes**\n- `persistFile` in `App.tsx` sends a `Uint8Array`, and `SaveFileInput.bytes` is `Uint8Array`.\n- Storage takes a view or `ArrayBuffer` without copying and rejects a number array.\n- `persistFile` is the only path that sends file bytes: file picker, paste, drag and drop, screenshot, and deep-link image. The extension capture server only sends URLs.\n\n**Thumbnails**\n- Capture reads only the image header (new `inspectImage`). Non-images and oversized images are still refused, and the card gets its shape right away. BMP/ICO only get header checks; their size is recorded when the thumbnail lands.\n- A silent `image_thumbnail` job writes the thumbnail through the video agent's `storeDerivedThumbnail`. It then queues the palette job, which no longer runs at capture.\n- The job runs on a second worker, kicked from the `save_file` handler, so OCR or PDF work can't hold it up. Recovery is the existing job-queue lease and restart handling. Library import queues it for imported images that have no thumbnail.\n- A failed job leaves the item in place with no error card.\n- Until the thumbnail lands the card shows the typed placeholder, not the original. The detail view still shows the full original.\n\n**Tests**\n- 86 pass.\n- 1 fail: the \"portable precedence\" test in `storage.test.ts`. It expects `/apps/inkling/data`, gets `\\apps\\inkling\\data`, and the code under test is untouched. I didn't confirm it fails on a clean checkout.\n\n**Left unfinished**\n- No backfill for old image items that lack a thumbnail.\n- `video_poster` stays on the main worker; the video agent can move it onto the thumbnail worker if it wants.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>253254</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>73</tool_uses><duration_ms>395169</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
