{"parentUuid":"056d77b5-5342-425a-9bdf-55b831ef4398","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEDzFq6t7SeGg5BTwsmj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm realizing BMP/ICO images might break under sharp since it doesn't support those formats for thumbnail generation, meaning those cards would get stuck showing the placeholder forever instead of falling back to the original asset path like before.\n\nLegacy images without thumbnails would also face this regression — previously main would show the original image, but now there's no backfill, so they'd permanently show a placeholder too. I think the better approach is restoring fallback-to-original: it preserves main's behavior for failures/legacy items, and gives instant visuals when a new capture happens since the card can show the original immediately before swapping to the thumbnail with no visible change. For bulk imports, virtualization should keep the cost manageable since only visible cards load originals.\n\nI want to check thumbnail.mjs to confirm how BMP is actually handled.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3812,"cache_read_input_tokens":98441,"output_tokens":738,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":609},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3812,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":738,"cache_read_input_tokens":98441,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3812,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3812},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":9294,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,