{"parentUuid":"9efc5280-8fd1-4375-b2c5-7ab9fe128dc5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEE6B5XAWUA3m5XZ4r9k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'll create the PR as a draft, consistent with the redesign PR and stacked PR both being drafts. For the body I'll cover the problem, the fix, and a footer, and since I don't have before/after UI images yet for the video card and archive changes, I'll note that's pending per the AGENTS requirement rather than block on it.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1038,"cache_read_input_tokens":108421,"output_tokens":1029,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":95},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1038,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1029,"cache_read_input_tokens":108421,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1038,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1038},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":3533,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEE6AMs9rgpnQNuXw3qK","requestRef":"32993e63-014c-479b-8735-217477ae9f08","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"39ed8c33-ab0f-4ae7-8813-b281d4f7a534","timestamp":"2026-10-20T21:49:25.804Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"39ed8c33-ab0f-4ae7-8813-b281d4f7a534","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEE6B5XAWUA3m5XZ4r9k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KZPiJEu78tEnzGKbuETmaw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/perf-library-io && timeout 60 gh pr create --draft --base feat/glass-surface --head perf/library-io --title \"perf(library): background thumbnails and posters, streamed assets, lazy archive\" --body-file - <<'EOF'\nStacked on #170.\n\nFour slow paths:\n- Capture sent file bytes over IPC as a number array, and the card waited for the thumbnail resize before it appeared.\n- Local video cards loaded the whole video file just to show a frame.\n- The asset protocol read every file fully into memory before sending a byte.\n- The Settings Archive tab read every archived item, with its processing state, whenever Settings opened, and then rendered every card.\n\n**Capture.** Bytes now travel as a `Uint8Array`. Capture reads only the image header to check the image and get its size, then saves and returns. The thumbnail comes from a queued `image_thumbnail` job on a second worker, so OCR and model loading can't delay it. The existing queue handles leases and recovery after a restart. Until the thumbnail lands, the card shows the original image.\n\n**Video posters.** A `video_poster` job on the same worker makes a poster with Electron's `nativeImage.createThumbnailFromPath`, which uses the shell thumbnailer and adds no dependency. Existing videos get theirs from an idle backfill. Grid cards no longer contain a `<video>` element. A video without a poster shows the typed video card instead of an empty dark tile.\n\n**Assets.** The asset handler moved to `electron/asset-response.mjs`. It streams files and supports single byte-range requests (206 and 416), with `ETag` and `Last-Modified` but no `Cache-Control`, because thumbnails are rewritten in place. The `app` scheme now has the `stream` privilege so media can seek. The path containment checks are unchanged.\n\n**Archive.** The archive is read only while its tab is shown. Its grid mounts only the rows near the scroll position and keeps the CSS grid layout and tab order.\n\n**Tests.** There are focused tests for each part. The one failing test in `storage.test.ts` (\"portable precedence\", a Windows path separator) already fails on main.\n\n**Not done:**\n- No run in the real app yet. Before/after screenshots of the video card and the Archive tab still need to be added.\n- A video card gets shorter when its poster arrives.\n- The Archive tab count shows only after the tab has been opened.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF","description":"Open the stacked perf PR as a draft"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1038,"cache_read_input_tokens":108421,"output_tokens":1029,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":95},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1038,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1029,"cache_read_input_tokens":108421,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1038,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1038},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01KZPiJEu78tEnzGKbuETmaw":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/perf-library-io && timeout 60 gh pr create --draft --base feat/glass-surface --head perf/library-io --title \"perf(library): background thumbnails and posters, streamed assets, lazy archive\" --body-file - <<'EOF'\nStacked on #170.\n\nFour slow paths:\n- Capture sent file bytes over IPC as a number array, and the card waited for the thumbnail resize before it appeared.\n- Local video cards loaded the whole video file just to show a frame.\n- The asset protocol read every file fully into memory before sending a byte.\n- The Settings Archive tab read every archived item, with its processing state, whenever Settings opened, and then rendered every card.\n\n**Capture.** Bytes now travel as a `Uint8Array`. Capture reads only the image header to check the image and get its size, then saves and returns. The thumbnail comes from a queued `image_thumbnail` job on a second worker, so OCR and model loading can't delay it. The existing queue handles leases and recovery after a restart. Until the thumbnail lands, the card shows the original image.\n\n**Video posters.** A `video_poster` job on the same worker makes a poster with Electron's `nativeImage.createThumbnailFromPath`, which uses the shell thumbnailer and adds no dependency. Existing videos get theirs from an idle backfill. Grid cards no longer contain a `<video>` element. A video without a poster shows the typed video card instead of an empty dark tile.\n\n**Assets.** The asset handler moved to `electron/asset-response.mjs`. It streams files and supports single byte-range requests (206 and 416), with `ETag` and `Last-Modified` but no `Cache-Control`, because thumbnails are rewritten in place. The `app` scheme now has the `stream` privilege so media can seek. The path containment checks are unchanged.\n\n**Archive.** The archive is read only while its tab is shown. Its grid mounts only the rows near the scroll position and keeps the CSS grid layout and tab order.\n\n**Tests.** There are focused tests for each part. The one failing test in `storage.test.ts` (\"portable precedence\", a Windows path separator) already fails on main.\n\n**Not done:**\n- No run in the real app yet. Before/after screenshots of the video card and the Archive tab still need to be added.\n- A video card gets shorter when its poster arrives.\n- The Archive tab count shows only after the tab has been opened.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF","description":"Open the stacked perf PR as a draft"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgEE6AMs9rgpnQNuXw3qK","requestRef":"32993e63-014c-479b-8735-217477ae9f08","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"f6f1ccd7-0cef-44db-bd56-eb8d7f046e9d","timestamp":"2026-10-20T21:49:31.068Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
