{"parentUuid":"e9f2ae76-6d2c-4cb6-9f67-07a7a80c499c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEEiyJ8QG1BL4uPqXzMh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CtveyjARAyJvySpyzskDvw","name":"mcp__t3-code__delegate_task","input":{"title":"E2E test perf + redesign","role":"test","clientRequestId":"perf-e2e-luna-1","mode":"async","target":{"providerInstanceId":"codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","options":{"reasoningEffort":"high"}},"task":"End-to-end test the inkling desktop app (Electron + React + Vite, Bun 1.4.2) on Windows. Use the real packaged/desktop app where native behavior matters and the browser preview where it is enough. This is TEST ONLY: do not edit source, and run no git commands that change state.\n\nWORKSPACE: C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\perf-library-io, branch perf/library-io (draft PR #174). It is stacked on feat/glass-surface (PR #170, the UI redesign). Read AGENTS.md there first and follow it strictly:\n- Never write to the live library. Use an isolated scratch userData/library. Copying a few real items with SQLite backup semantics is fine, and so is the committed demo seed.\n- Kill only PIDs you captured at spawn. Never kill by name, path or pattern.\n- Launching a dev Electron repoints the HKCU\\Software\\Classes\\inkling protocol handler. Back it up first with PowerShell `reg export HKCU\\Software\\Classes\\inkling <tempfile> /y`, and restore it with `reg import` when done.\n- Don't hardcode ports. Read them from the output.\n- If the repo has a verify-inkling skill or scripts (CDP against an isolated scratch library), use them. Existing CDP helpers live in C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\resurf\\qa\\ (launch.mjs, cdp.mjs, probe.mjs). Their selectors may be stale.\n- Build the renderer with `node node_modules/vite/bin/vite.js build --mode electron-preview` if you use those scripts. Use `bun run build:dir` if you need the full packaged backend.\n\nWHAT TO VERIFY (perf PR):\n1. Image capture via file picker/drag/paste:\n   - the card appears immediately, showing the original;\n   - it then switches to the thumbnail (thumbnail.webp appears under assets/items/<id>/);\n   - capture is not blocked;\n   - an interrupted thumbnail job recovers on restart if you can arrange it.\n   Check that bytes go over IPC as a Uint8Array, not a number array.\n2. Local video capture (an .mp4):\n   - the grid card shows a poster after a short background delay, with no <video> element in the grid;\n   - before the poster lands, it shows the typed video card, not an empty dark tile;\n   - the detail view plays the video, and seeking works (Range requests to the app:// asset handler return 206).\n   - Note the card height change when the poster lands.\n3. Asset handler:\n   - large files stream;\n   - Range gives 206, an unsatisfiable range gives 416;\n   - path escapes are rejected.\n4. Settings → Archive tab:\n   - the archive loads only when the tab opens;\n   - with many archived items, only nearby rows are mounted while scrolling;\n   - restore and permanent delete still work;\n   - the empty state shows;\n   - the tab count behavior.\n5. Settings → Library: the size shows quickly and then refreshes.\n6. Smoke-test the redesign broadly:\n   - library grid, search, pinned query;\n   - item inspector Info/Similar tabs, zoom;\n   - back/forward history;\n   - Settings tabs.\n   Look for console errors or broken states.\n\nEVIDENCE: save screenshots to C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\perf-e2e\\. Create the folder if missing, and only wipe that subfolder. Clean up every process you launched and restore the registry key.\n\nREPORT (concise): a pass/fail per item above with evidence (screenshot paths, log lines, timings), each bug found with exact repro and suspected file, and anything you could not test and why."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_det