{"parentUuid":"88a2c692-c73a-4b82-8fff-d5b9c3cef1e8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEEmfYsGVn1tLRGuwhph","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"That's probably fine in practice since SQLite's modern variable limit is around 32,766, so this would only break with very large item counts — but it also returns the entire job history per item including completed ones, so the dataset could grow unexpectedly over time.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1250,"cache_read_input_tokens":123165,"output_tokens":887,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":76},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1250,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":887,"cache_read_input_tokens":123165,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1250,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1250},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7887,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEEmfFX7cjiuhPm4oX2n","requestRef":"a8408a54-3ebf-4608-9de3-d8d5e5047bb6","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"29139c66-d460-4cbb-a2e2-ae1aee5d3826","timestamp":"2026-10-20T21:58:21.381Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"29139c66-d460-4cbb-a2e2-ae1aee5d3826","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEEmfYsGVn1tLRGuwhph","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've started GPT-6 Luna (high) on an end-to-end test of the perf branch and the redesign. It will use the desktop app for anything native and the browser preview where that's enough, with a scratch library rather than your real one. It's test-only, so it won't change any code. Screenshots go to `C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\perf-e2e\\`. I'll pass its results on when it finishes.\n\n## The two optional items\n\n### 1. Incremental library refresh (medium)\nWhen the library reloads, for example after you capture something or a background job finishes, the renderer rebuilds everything from scratch (`src/App.tsx:3805–3823`):\n1. It asks the backend for the whole list of items.\n2. It asks for the processing status of every one of them.\n3. It rebuilds every card's data, including working out each one's image URL.\n4. It replaces the grid's whole list.\n\nWith a few hundred items that's fine. With thousands, every finished OCR or embedding job means an IPC round trip carrying the full list, then rebuilding every card's data. The cards on screen also re-render, even though usually only one item changed.\n\nThe fix would be for the backend to report which item ids changed, so the renderer updates just those and leaves the rest alone. It's on the optional list because the cost only shows in large libraries, and it touches the most delicate code in `App.tsx`. That refresh code already re-applies note edits and pins you made in this session so a reload can't overwrite them, and an incremental path has to keep that working.\n\n### 2. Batching the job-status lookup (small)\nThe processing status comes from `getForItems` in `electron/storage.mjs:811`. It builds one SQL query with one `?` per item, so `item_id IN (?, ?, ?, …)` can end up with thousands of placeholders. Two smaller problems:\n- **Size limit:** SQLite caps how many `?` one query can have (32,766 in current builds). A library past that size would make this query fail and break the reload.\n- **Wasted work:** it returns every job the item has ever had, finished ones included, and the renderer then discards all but the latest of each kind. That history keeps growing.\n\nThe fix would be to run the query in chunks of a few hundred ids, and to ask SQL only for the latest job of each kind per item. It's small and independent of everything else, so it could go into #174 now if you want it.\n\nI'd do #2 now and leave #1 until the library is big enough to feel it, or until after the redesign lands."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1250,"cache_read_input_tokens":123165,"output_tokens":887,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":76},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1250,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":887,"cache_read_input_tokens":123165,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1250,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1250},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgEEmfFX7cjiuhPm4oX2n","requestRef":"a8408a54-3ebf-4608-9de3-d8d5e5047bb6","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e17f87ea-2326-48c7-9d4a-b9df9018b967","timestamp":"2026-10-20T21:58:23.010Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
