{"parentUuid":"90246816-278e-4436-b684-4436e18bc7cc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEGnTR8FRfu3WDKYdvsz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SZM1yidQdASGQcDjqA2Nay","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Incremental library refresh","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"You are making one performance change in inkling, an Electron + React + TypeScript + Vite app with node:sqlite in the main process (Bun 1.4.2). Read AGENTS.md at the worktree root first and follow it. Pay particular attention to \"A note on taste\": the maintainer wants the smallest model that makes the behavior unsurprising, not clever machinery.\n\nWORKSPACE: C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\perf-library-io (branch perf/library-io). Work ONLY there.\n- Another agent is running a test-only end-to-end pass in this worktree. Do not build, launch Electron or dev servers, or touch .artifacts.\n- Use the Edit tool for targeted edits. Do not rewrite src/App.tsx with Write.\n- Run NO git commands that change state. The maintainer commits.\n\nPROBLEM: in src/App.tsx, the library load effect (around line 3800, the one using listActiveItems / searchItems, countActiveJobs and getProcessingSummaries) rebuilds the entire library whenever it refreshes. It does so after a capture, and when a background job finishes and the backend announces an item/job update:\n1. It fetches every item over IPC.\n2. It fetches processing summaries for all of them.\n3. It runs storedItemToLibraryItem, with its assetUrl lookups, on every item.\n4. It replaces the whole items array, so every visible card re-renders.\n\nWith thousands of items this happens after every finished OCR or embedding job.\n\nGOAL: when the backend reports that specific items changed (a job finished, a thumbnail or poster landed, etc.), update just those items in place. Fetch them with the existing getItem, or batch them if a call already exists, plus getProcessingSummaries for those ids. Keep unchanged items referentially identical so memoized cards don't re-render. Full reloads stay where they're genuinely needed: the initial load, query/view changes, imports, and anything without an item id.\n\nSTEPS:\n- First find how updates reach the renderer. Look for an onItemUpdated/job lifecycle event in electron/preload.cjs, src/electron.d.ts, src/lib/libraryApi.ts, and the job queue's onUpdated/announce in electron/storage.mjs and electron/main.mjs. Find out what it carries and what currently triggers the full refresh. If the event already carries item ids, use them. If not, add the id with the smallest change.\n- Coalesce bursts: a short batch of changed ids applied together is fine. Don't reintroduce per-keystroke work.\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- An item may have been archived, deleted or filtered out by the current query/view since. Make sure a patched item doesn't appear where it doesn't belong. When in doubt for that item, falling back to the full reload is acceptable.\n- The full-refresh code re-applies session state: the note body cache and unconfirmed pins (\"A refresh can resolve with data older than two writes this session already made...\"). Your patch path must keep those guarantees for patched items.\n- Keep the active job count (countActiveJobs) updating, since the mascot depends on it.\n- Preview mode (shouldUseSeedLibrary / no desktop backend) must be unaffected.\n\nTESTS: if you extract a pure helper (e.g. merging patched items into the list while preserving the identity of untouched ones), add a focused bun test for it. Don't add render-to-markup tests. Run:\n- `bun test <files you touched>`;\n- `bunx biome check <changed files>`;\n- `bun run typecheck`, checking the exit code with `echo $?` and not through a pipe.\n\nREPORT (under 200 words):\n- files changed;\n- which events now patch and which still fully reload;\n- how the session-state guarantees are kept;\n- tests run with results;\n- any risk you see."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":764,"cache_read_input_tokens":149949,"output_tokens":1660,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":210},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":764,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1660,"cache_read_input_tokens":149949,"cache_creation_input_tokens":764,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":764},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01SZM1yidQdASGQcDjqA2Nay":{"description":"Incremental library refresh","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"You are making one performance change in inkling, an Electron + React + TypeScript + Vite app with node:sqlite in the main process (Bun 1.4.2). Read AGENTS.md at the worktree root first and follow it. Pay particular attention to \"A note on taste\": the maintainer wants the smallest model that makes the behavior unsurprising, not clever machinery.\n\nWORKSPACE: C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\perf-library-io (branch perf/library-io). Work ONLY there.\n- Another agent is running a test-only end-to-end pass in this worktree. Do not build, launch Electron or dev servers, or touch .artifacts.\n- Use the Edit tool for targeted edits. Do not rewrite src/App.tsx with Write.\n- Run NO git commands that change state. The maintainer commits.\n\nPROBLEM: in src/App.tsx, the library load effect (around line 3800, the one using listActiveItems / searchItems, countActiveJobs and getProcessingSummaries) rebuilds the entire library whenever it refreshes. It does so after a capture, and when a background job finishes and the backend announces an item/job update:\n1. It fetches every item over IPC.\n2. It fetches processing summaries for all of them.\n3. It runs storedItemToLibraryItem, with its assetUrl lookups, on every item.\n4. It replaces the whole items array, so every visible card re-renders.\n\nWith thousands of items this happens after every finished OCR or embedding job.\n\nGOAL: when the backend reports that specific items changed (a job finished, a thumbnail or poster landed, etc.), update just those items in place. Fetch them with the existing getItem, or batch them if a call already exists, plus getProcessingSummaries for those ids. Keep unchanged items referentially identical so memoized cards don't re-render. Full reloads stay where they're genuinely needed: the initial load, query/view changes, imports, and anything without an item id.\n\nSTEPS:\n- First find how updates reach the renderer. Look for an onItemUpdated/job lifecycle event in electron/preload.cjs, src/electron.d.ts, src/lib/libraryApi.ts, and the job queue's onUpdated/announce in electron/storage.mjs and electron/main.mjs. Find out what it carries and what currently triggers the full refresh. If the event already carries item ids, use them. If not, add the id with the smallest change.\n- Coalesce bursts: a short batch of changed ids applied together is fine. Don't reintroduce per-keystroke work.\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- An item may have been archived, deleted or filtered out by the current query/view since. Make sure a patched item doesn't appear where it doesn't belong. When in doubt for that item, falling back to the full reload is acceptable.\n- The full-refresh code re-applies session state: the note body cache and unconfirmed pins (\"A refresh can resolve with data older than two writes this session already made...\"). Your patch path must keep those guarantees for patched items.\n- Keep the active job count (countActiveJobs) updating, since the mascot depends on it.\n- Preview mode (shouldUseSeedLibrary / no desktop backend) must be unaffected.\n\nTESTS: if you extract a pure helper (e.g. merging patched items into the list while preserving the identity of untouched ones), add a focused bun test for it. Don't add render-to-markup tests. Run:\n- `bun test <files you touched>`;\n- `bunx biome check <changed files>`;\n- `bun run typecheck`, checking the exit code with `echo $?` and not through a pipe.\n\nREPORT (under 200 words):\n- files changed;\n- which events now patch and which still fully reload;\n- how the session-state guarantees are kept;\n- tests run with results;\n- any risk you see."}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgEGnT6n1pWUV4RrDNBks","requestRef":"181d1745-1ab6-460e-8b45-4bf545a7e47d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"757fb9c9-2e07-4881-99f9-0f80e27d35a9","timestamp":"2026-10-20T22:24:51.675Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
