{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-20T22:26:16.072Z","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","content":"Delegated task node:delegated-task:command%3Amcp%3A2dd0b88d-eaff-4e1a-b29c-2ffb930c8d61%3Adelegate-task%3Aperf-e2e-luna-1 (E2E test perf + redesign) [completed]:\n## Results\n\nThe packaged Windows app passed the tested capture, asset, archive, and redesign flows. I made no source edits and ran no Git commands that change state.\n\n1. **PASS — image capture.** File capture displayed the original first, then switched to `thumbnail.webp`; the observed transition took about **570 ms**, with the thumbnail visible about **1.0 s** after Save. Clipboard paste and drag/drop also persisted images through their renderer handlers. The capture code constructs a `Uint8Array`; the backend accepts typed bytes and rejects number arrays. **The OS file-picker dialog and real system clipboard/drag gestures were not automated**—the file input used CDP file injection, and paste/drop used synthetic events. Interrupted-job recovery was not tested; thumbnail work completed too quickly to leave a job pending.\n\n2. **PASS — local video.** The card first showed the typed video treatment, with no `<video>` element in the grid. Its height changed from **300 px to 190 px** when the poster arrived. The detail video played and advanced to about 0.29 s; seeking to 2 s succeeded. The app asset URL returned **206** for a byte range.\n\n3. **PASS — asset handler.** A 64 MiB file returned **200** and streamed a 64 KiB first chunk before completion. A valid range returned **206**; an unsatisfiable range returned **416**. An encoded path escape returned **404** with an empty body.\n\n4. **PASS — Archive.** The count was absent before opening the tab and appeared afterward. With 120 archived items, **18 cards** were mounted; scrolling moved the rendered window while retaining 18 mounted cards. Restore changed the active/archive counts, and permanent delete completed after its undo window. The empty state also appeared.\n\n5. **PASS — Settings → Library.** The size appeared as **69 MB on disk**. Cached and refreshed size calls returned the same 72,594,146 bytes in about **0.6 ms** and **8.6 ms**, respectively.\n\n6. **PASS — redesign smoke test.** Search returned the video result; pinning put the image in Top of mind; Info/Similar tabs and zoom worked; Back/Forward traversed search history; General, Archive, Browser extension, and Library settings opened. No renderer console errors were recorded. The Similar tab correctly showed “Nothing similar yet” for this test library.\n\n## Findings and limits\n\nThe packaged `build:dir` launch logged a non-blocking updater error: `ENOENT ... resources/app-update.yml` during `inkling:check_for_updates`. The UI continued working. This reproduces when launching the directory build made with `bun run build:dir`; likely areas are `electron/updater.mjs` and the builder’s update-config output.\n\nThe browser-preview snapshot timed out twice with `Preview automation snapshot timed out after 15000ms`, so broad UI coverage used the packaged app instead. The interruption-recovery case and native OS picker/clipboard interactions remain unverified.\n\nThe protocol registry export was restored and its hash matched the original. The packaged app and Vite server are stopped; no source files were edited.\n\nEvidence is in `C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\perf-e2e\\`.\n\n![Image displayed before thumbnail](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\perf-e2e\\image-original-first.png)\n\n![Video card before poster](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\perf-e2e\\video-pending.png)\n\n![Video playback at 2 seconds](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\perf-e2e\\video-play-attempt.png)\n\n![Archive with 120 items](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\perf-e2e\\archive-top-120.png)"}
