t.ts` (new)\n- `electron/storage.mjs` (new `getItemCards`, active items only, so archived or deleted ids drop out)\n- `electron/main.mjs`, `electron/preload.cjs`, `src/electron.d.ts` (new `get_item_cards` command)\n\n**What patches and what reloads**\n- The `job-updated` event already carried `itemId`, so I changed nothing there.\n- In the plain library view, bursts of ids are coalesced for 400ms. I fetch light cards, not `getItem`, which would send the full article HTML over IPC.\n- Each patch also fetches processing summaries and refreshes `countActiveJobs`.\n- It falls back to a full reload for a query or Space view, an id-less event, an active item not yet in the list, a full load already in flight, or any error.\n\n**Session-state guarantees**\n- The note body cache, unconfirmed pins and selected-item sync moved into helpers shared by both paths. They are read at apply time, not fetch time.\n- An epoch counter drops a patch that a newer full load has overtaken.\n\n**Risks**\n- A patched item keeps its grid position, whereas a full reload moved it to the top (the backend orders by `updated_at DESC`).\n- The 30s visible-tab fallback still does a full reload.\n- I added no changelog entry.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>80980</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>19</tool_uses><duration_ms>147268</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
