{"parentUuid":"013c5beb-8061-42ae-9a8d-fe94988f5bb1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEH3HiQMmG9ZeKvTUYxi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Committed and pushed. Starting Luna's re-test against a fresh build that includes the OCR fix and the new refresh."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1166,"cache_read_input_tokens":164145,"output_tokens":1422,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1166,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1422,"cache_read_input_tokens":164145,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1166,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1166},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEH3HPZ53aspPYMxjz7f","requestRef":"3f3051d2-c3aa-4a90-92ef-813057398c4f","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"0e16bfb1-7f5f-4513-9d4f-b84b16e4901c","timestamp":"2026-10-20T22:27:57.821Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"0e16bfb1-7f5f-4513-9d4f-b84b16e4901c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEH3HiQMmG9ZeKvTUYxi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BTfgMjhE13WvPA7FRzfFNg","name":"mcp__t3-code__delegate_task","input":{"title":"E2E retest round 2","role":"test","clientRequestId":"perf-e2e-luna-2","mode":"async","target":{"providerInstanceId":"codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","options":{"reasoningEffort":"high"}},"task":"Round 2 end-to-end test of the inkling Windows desktop app. This is TEST ONLY: edit no source, and run no git commands that change state.\n\nWORKSPACE: C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\perf-library-io, branch perf/library-io (draft PR #174, stacked on #170). Read AGENTS.md and follow it strictly:\n- Use an isolated scratch library, never the live one.\n- Kill only PIDs you captured at spawn.\n- Back up HKCU\\Software\\Classes\\inkling with PowerShell `reg export` before launching, and restore it with `reg import` afterwards.\n- Hardcode no ports.\n\nBuild a fresh packaged directory build with `bun run build:dir`. The previous build is stale.\n\nROUND 1 RESULTS:\n- Image capture, local video posters with 206 seeking, asset streaming (206/416/404), Archive virtualization (18 of 120 mounted), the Settings size and a redesign smoke test all passed.\n- Round 1 missed a real bug: the packaged app showed a main-process error dialog, \"Cannot find module 'regenerator-runtime/runtime'\", when OCR started. The cause was tesseract's worker running from app.asar.unpacked while its deps were inside app.asar. The fix adds those deps to asarUnpack in package.json.\n- Untested in round 1: recovery of an interrupted thumbnail job, and real OS file picker, clipboard and drag gestures.\n- A known non-issue: in --dir builds, the updater logs ENOENT for app-update.yml.\n\nVERIFY NOW:\n1. OCR in the packaged app. Capture an image with clear text (a screenshot of text works) and a scanned-style PDF if you can. Then confirm:\n   - no error dialog appears. Watch for native dialogs: take full-screen screenshots, don't rely only on CDP;\n   - the OCR job completes;\n   - searching for a word from the image finds it.\n2. New change, incremental refresh. When background jobs finish (thumbnail, OCR, embeddings), the plain library view now patches only the touched cards instead of reloading the whole list. Verify:\n   - finished jobs update the right card (thumbnail appears, processing state clears);\n   - other cards are not re-rendered or reordered. A quick check is to tag a DOM node of an untouched card and confirm it survives;\n   - archiving or deleting an item while its jobs run removes it cleanly;\n   - in a search query or a Space view, job events still refresh correctly via full reload;\n   - the mascot/active job count still settles to idle.\n3. Item processing status (getForItems now returns only the latest job per kind). A failed then retried job shows the right state on the card and in the inspector.\n4. The window opens at 1280x720 by default.\n5. Thumbnail-job restart recovery, if you can arrange it. For example, capture several large images and quit immediately, then relaunch and confirm the thumbnails complete.\n6. A quick regression pass on the round 1 items.\n\nSave screenshots to C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\perf-e2e-2\\. Create the folder if missing, and only wipe that subfolder. Clean up all processes you launched and restore the registry key.\n\nREPORT (concise):\n- pass/fail per item with evidence (screenshot paths, logs, timings);\n- each bug with exact repro and suspected file;\n- what you could not test and why."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1166,"cache_read_input_tokens":164145,"output_tokens":1422,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"w