{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-20T22:32:36.075Z","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","content":"Delegated task node:delegated-task:command%3Amcp%3A2dd0b88d-eaff-4e1a-b29c-2ffb930c8d61%3Adelegate-task%3Aperf-e2e-luna-2 (E2E retest round 2) [completed]:\n## Round 2 result\n\nThe fresh `bun run build:dir` completed successfully. The packaged app launched with a separate scratch library at `C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\inkling-perf-e2e-2`; its main window title was `inkling`. I made no source edits and ran no git commands.\n\n| Check | Result | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| OCR, search, and native error dialogs | **Not tested** — desktop controls were unavailable, so I couldn’t capture an image or inspect the screen. | CUA reported no apps; connecting `sky` returned `Trusted RPC service is not configured: sky`. |\n| Incremental refresh, card identity/order, archive/delete during jobs, search/Space refresh, mascot idle | **Not tested** — requires UI interaction and DOM inspection. | Same desktop automation blocker. |\n| Failed-then-retried job status on card and inspector | **Not tested** — requires creating and retrying a job in the UI. | Same blocker. |\n| Default window size | **Not verified** — the app opened, but I couldn’t capture a full-screen view or inspect the window dimensions through the UI harness. | Main window title observed as `inkling`. |\n| Thumbnail restart recovery | **Not tested** — requires capturing images and quitting during processing. | Same blocker. |\n| Round 1 regressions | **Not tested** — image capture, seeking, asset responses, virtualization, settings, and redesign need UI flows. | Same blocker. |\n\nNo app bug was confirmed, including the Round 1 OCR module error; OCR never ran, so that fix remains unverified. I saved no screenshots because the desktop capture/control APIs were unavailable. The requested evidence folder exists at `C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\perf-e2e-2\\`.\n\nI closed the app process I launched and restored `HKCU\\Software\\Classes\\inkling` from [the registry backup](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\perf-e2e-2\\inkling-registry-backup.reg). The launched process was no longer running afterward."}
