{"parentUuid":"da778fdb-6fc6-4288-8890-22dc93b901df","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEHQMqnDhJXKx1PDMqAf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EtSSrzjo2sRGEhFypopKsR","name":"mcp__t3-code__delegate_task","input":{"title":"E2E retest round 3 (CDP)","role":"test","clientRequestId":"perf-e2e-luna-3","mode":"async","target":{"providerInstanceId":"codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","options":{"reasoningEffort":"high"}},"task":"Round 3 end-to-end test of the inkling Windows desktop app. This is TEST ONLY: edit no source, and run no git commands that change state.\n\nWORKSPACE: C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\perf-library-io, branch perf/library-io (draft PR #174). Read AGENTS.md and follow it strictly:\n- Use a scratch library only.\n- Kill only PIDs you captured at spawn.\n- Back up HKCU\\Software\\Classes\\inkling with PowerShell `reg export` before launching, and restore it with `reg import` afterwards.\n- Hardcode no ports.\n\nA fresh packaged build already exists at .artifacts\\electron\\win-unpacked (built 18:30, includes the OCR fix). Don't rebuild unless it's missing.\n\nHOW TO DRIVE IT. Round 2 failed because it tried desktop/computer-use controls, which are NOT available. Use Chrome DevTools Protocol instead, the way round 1 did successfully:\n- Launch win-unpacked\\inkling.exe yourself with `--remote-debugging-port=0` and a scratch user data dir (`--user-data-dir=<temp dir>`, or whatever the app's data-dir override is; check electron/main.mjs and the verify-inkling skill or scripts if present).\n- Read the DevToolsActivePort file in that user data dir to get the port, then drive the renderer over CDP with Runtime.evaluate, Input.dispatch*, DOM.setFileInputFiles and Page.captureScreenshot.\n- Helpers from earlier runs are in C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\resurf\\qa\\ (cdp.mjs, launch.mjs, probe.mjs). Round 1's own scripts are probably under C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\ too, so reuse them.\n- To catch NATIVE main-process error dialogs, which CDP can't see:\n  - capture the app process's stdout/stderr to a log file and search it for \"Uncaught Exception\" / \"Cannot find module\";\n  - take full-screen screenshots with PowerShell (System.Windows.Forms + System.Drawing Graphics.CopyFromScreen) after OCR runs;\n  - list top-level windows of your PID (e.g. Get-Process -Id <pid> | MainWindowTitle, or EnumWindows via Add-Type) and look for a window titled \"Error\".\n- Window size: in the renderer, evaluate `window.outerWidth/outerHeight` (or use Browser.getWindowForTarget) on first launch with a fresh user data dir.\n\nROUND 1: all perf flows passed, but a native \"Cannot find module 'regenerator-runtime/runtime'\" dialog appeared when OCR started. The fix unpacks tesseract's worker deps; app.asar.unpacked/node_modules now contains regenerator-runtime, is-url, node-fetch, etc. Round 2 tested nothing.\n\nVERIFY:\n1. OCR. Capture an image containing clear text: render text to a PNG with PowerShell System.Drawing or sharp, then inject it via the file input. Then:\n   - wait for the OCR job to complete;\n   - confirm there's no error dialog or log line;\n   - search a word from the image and confirm the item is found.\n2. Incremental refresh. When jobs finish in the plain library view, only touched cards update. Check:\n   - the thumbnail lands and processing clears on the right card;\n   - mark an untouched card's DOM node (e.g. set a data attribute) and confirm it survives with the same order;\n   - archive or delete an item while its jobs run, and confirm it disappears cleanly;\n   - in a search query view, job completion still refreshes results;\n   - the active job count / mascot returns to idle.\n3. Failed then retried job status shows correctly on the card and in the inspector, if you can force a failure (e.g. a corrupt image or PDF).\n4. The default window size is 1280x720.\n5. Thumbnail restart recovery: capture several large images, quit immediately, relaunch with the same scratch dir, and confirm the thumbnails complete.\n6. Quick regressions: video poster plus seeking, Archive tab, Settings size.\n\nSave screenshots to C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\perf-e2e-3\\ (create it if missing). Clean up all processes you launched and restore the registry key.\n\nREPORT (concise):\n- pass/fail per item with evidence;\n- each bug with exact repro and suspected file;\n- what you couldn't test and why."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":534,"cache_read_input_tokens":168667,"output_tokens":2005,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":224},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":534,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2005,"cache_read_input_tokens":168667,"cache_creation_input_tokens":534,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":534},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01EtSSrzjo2sRGEhFypopKsR":{"title":"E2E retest round 3 (CDP)","role":"test","clientRequestId":"perf-e2e-luna-3","mode":"async","target":{"providerInstanceId":"codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","options":{"reasoningEffort":"high"}},"task":"Round 3 end-to-end test of the inkling Windows desktop app. This is TEST ONLY: edit no source, and run no git commands that change state.\n\nWORKSPACE: C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\perf-library-io, branch perf/library-io (draft PR #174). Read AGENTS.md and follow it strictly:\n- Use a scratch library only.\n- Kill only PIDs you captured at spawn.\n- Back up HKCU\\Software\\Classes\\