{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","prNumber":174,"prUrl":"https://github.com/Squidys-Tools/inkling/pull/174","prRepository":"Squidys-Tools/inkling","timestamp":"2026-10-20T22:40:26.187Z"}
{"parentUuid":"69eb5c3f-31d0-4fef-b851-af43981c3ebf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEHzXwBwaBxvnBx5YWfC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm considering adding a visibilitychange listener to trigger a full reload whenever the user returns to the tab, as a fallback for any missed events. I'm also tracing whether other sources like the browser extension capture server, deep links, or imports properly emit job events that the patch logic would catch, concluding URL captures do via the itemId path, and the fallback should only need to run sparingly as a safety net.\n\nA cheaper option is polling a lightweight library \"stamp\" — item count plus max updated_at — and only triggering a reload when it changes, rather than reloading on every focus regain. I'm also checking whether updated_at actually bumps when background jobs complete (thumbnails, OCR text), since if it doesn't, the stamp would miss those changes and I'd need to fold in job completion timestamps too.\n\nActually, SQLite's `total_changes()` on the main connection might be an even cleaner stamp — it increments on every insert/update/delete made through that connection, so comparing it to the last known value tells me if anything changed at all. The catch is that job heartbeat/progress updates would also bump this counter, potentially causing unnecessary reloads even when nothing visible changed.\n\nBut that's acceptable: during idle periods nothing reloads, and during active jobs the behavior matches today's 30-second refresh. I should double check whether worker_threads open separate database connections, since total_changes only counts writes made through the specific connection it's called on.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1050,"cache_read_input_tokens":172705,"output_tokens":1245,"output_tok