{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","id":"947fcce6-96a8-48fb-852b-ebef0bdb6dba","timestamp":"2026-10-20T22:43:08.024Z","version":"2.1.304","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"dfe7814906254ff001873d6255b116bdda00b295ee662266b96d56b73b9013f8","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"summarized"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"492c3dd6-de01-41a0-96bb-afee6dfabd32","keep":268,"tail":["201361100d87847172eac23c21b89f5eb24853dcc1886f5e4bfaa216c47e2767","2ecf653785d601e46786fb3f076d846d7f255ee3d71ac6cb376fddee1ba4ee14","4b8bd9022e1f1d78333fcd370681ee79d1655b97a52c14e0e30360c64fe2dca4"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",270,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"f1f961639766b5e363db0339852b29773804bc94de2db91c6dc8ecd0ab1d5c4c"}
{"parentUuid":"818f2548-d78b-4c59-b37b-9138bf8037cf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEJCVJH8NKhoJtxLD3cb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Saving a new PNG triggers the full-load path since new items always get inserted at the top, which naturally reflows the masonry order — that's expected behavior, not a bug. The real question is whether cards are keyed by id during re-render, since if virtualization re-mounts nodes on full load, that could explain unwanted DOM detachment.\n\nSo I think the test scenario itself is flawed — capturing a new item legitimately causes a full reload and reordering, which isn't the real bug signal. The better test would be an existing item's job completing (like retrying OCR), which shouldn't detach unrelated cards. I want to check how the grid keys items and whether capture inserts locally before concluding anything, rather than guessing at a root cause I haven't verified.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1383,"cache_read_input_tokens":182078,"output_tokens":699,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":521},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1383,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":699,"cache_read_input_tokens":182078,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1383,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1383},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":8955,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEJCTuRsFGsrV9ufrTbo","requestRef":"947fcce6-96a8-48fb-852b-ebef0bdb6dba","requestedModel":"claude-