{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","id":"097d0ba8-1e83-42a0-b8d4-c2fb4387be7a","timestamp":"2026-10-20T22:43:18.240Z","version":"2.1.304","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"dfe7814906254ff001873d6255b116bdda00b295ee662266b96d56b73b9013f8","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"summarized"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"947fcce6-96a8-48fb-852b-ebef0bdb6dba","keep":271,"tail":["9185dfd12585117c7620e7e0346f5c04efd4893976983350f16cbad97e1ccf59","996a083dc78c1c255d204cadd6831e5d3ef3463912646604360efe94a3472a4c","72dc4d350c5a6db5955b98ece155909ad79b62ce2286e2140e1b961c09ba1ca8"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",273,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"29737ec7b4bd7c02b5527a36c26d8c92e18392f050222792815324028c202f61"}
{"parentUuid":"956736d8-71b8-4b55-a0b3-b47398e6afe2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEJDDw5s8qpHWMk5ECCf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"VirtuosoMasonry keys items by position, so prepending an item shifts every index and remounts every card for new data — that's pre-existing capture behavior, not something my patch introduces, since the patch doesn't alter positions. I'll just report this plainly rather than running another verification round unless asked.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":961,"cache_read_input_tokens":183461,"output_tokens":792,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":141},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":961,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":792,"cache_read_input_tokens":183461,"cache_creation_input_tokens":961,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":961},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":8255,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEJDDbFNDFSKuDZQmRpN","requestRef":"097d0ba8-1e83-42a0-b8d4-c2fb4387be7a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"13ea2c22-73f4-46e9-a656-b2dfb6089541","timestamp":"2026-10-20T22:43:27.062Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"13ea2c22-73f4-46e9-a656-b2dfb6089541","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEJDDw5s8qpHWMk5ECCf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Round 3 got through most of the list. The one \"fail\" it reported doesn't hold up, but it also means the incremental refresh still hasn't actually been tested.\n\n**Passed**\n- **OCR in the installed app:** text in a captured image was found by search (\"quasar meadow\"). There was no error dialog and no \"Cannot find module\" in the logs, so the crash fix holds.\n- **Window size:** it opens at 1280×720. The 1296×728 Luna measured includes the window frame.\n- **Archive tab and Settings:** both still work.\n\n**The incremental refresh \"fail\" is a flaw in the test.** Luna marked a card, then captured a new image, and saw the marked card's element get replaced and the cards reorder. That's expected:\n- Capturing adds the new card at the top of the grid.\n- The masonry grid component identifies cards by position, not by item (`App.tsx:4154`). Adding a card at the top moves every card down one position, so every card's element gets replaced.\n- That has always happened on capture and isn't from this PR.\n\nThe real check is different: leave the list alone, let a job finish on an existing item (for example, retry its OCR), and confirm the other cards' elements survive. Luna didn't run that.\n\n**Not tested**\n- Failed then retried job status.\n- Recovering an interrupted thumbnail job: the jobs finished before the app quit.\n- Video posters and seeking: there was no video in its test library.\n- Job updates during a search, and archiving or deleting an item while its jobs run.\n- The mascot settling back to idle.\n- The skip-reload-when-nothing-changed change, which I made after this build.\n\n**Harmless noise**\n- Tesseract logs \"Image too small to scale\" for small test images.\n- The `app-update.yml` error happens because `build:dir` builds don't include update metadata; it's unrelated to these changes.\n\nIf you want, I can send Luna one more short round on a fresh build covering just the gaps above. Otherwise #174 is ready for you to review."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":961,"cache_read_input_tokens":183461,"output_tokens":792,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":141},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":961,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":792,"cache_read_input_tokens":183461,"cache_creation_input_tokens":961,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":961},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgEJDDbFNDFSKuDZQmRpN","requestRef":"097d0ba8-1e83-42a0-b8d4-c2fb4387be7a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"65758038-8564-4041-95c4-06c55bc3bb1a","timestamp":"2026-10-20T22:43:27.075Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
