{"parentUuid":"0adc461c-ae50-4ea5-b9d8-a42a432a4b31","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEN2iWhdZcasY7jKXp8d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017oaSHGzSRmapwVKSKtTqgk","name":"mcp__t3-code__delegate_task","input":{"title":"E2E retest round 4 (gaps)","role":"test","clientRequestId":"perf-e2e-luna-4","mode":"async","target":{"providerInstanceId":"codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","options":{"reasoningEffort":"high"}},"task":"Round 4 end-to-end test of the inkling Windows desktop app. This is TEST ONLY: edit no source and run no git commands that change state.\n\nWORKSPACE: C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\perf-library-io, branch perf/library-io (draft PR #174). Follow AGENTS.md strictly:\n- Use a scratch library only, never the live one.\n- Kill only PIDs you captured at spawn.\n- Back up HKCU\\Software\\Classes\\inkling with PowerShell `reg export` and restore it with `reg import` afterwards.\n- Hardcode no ports.\n\nFIRST: rebuild with `bun run build:dir`. The existing build is stale.\n\nDrive the app over Chrome DevTools Protocol, as in round 3. Launch .artifacts\\electron\\win-unpacked\\inkling.exe with `--remote-debugging-port=0` and a scratch data dir, then read DevToolsActivePort. Desktop/computer-use controls are NOT available. To watch for native error dialogs, log stdout/stderr and take PowerShell CopyFromScreen screenshots. Reuse your round 3 scripts under C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\.\n\nSeed the scratch library with at least 10 items, including:\n- a local .mp4 video;\n- an image with text, for OCR;\n- a corrupt image or PDF that will fail processing.\n\nVERIFY ONLY THESE GAPS:\n1. Incremental refresh, measured correctly. Do NOT capture a new item during this check. Capture prepends to the grid and the masonry grid keys by position, so every node remounts by design.\n   - With the list settled, mark several visible card DOM nodes.\n   - Trigger a job on an EXISTING item, e.g. retry OCR or a failed job from the inspector, or call the retry command.\n   - When the job finishes, confirm the marked nodes are still connected and in the same order, and that the target card's state updated.\n2. Job completion while a search query is active still refreshes the results.\n3. Archive, then delete, an item while its jobs are still running. It disappears cleanly with no ghost card and no console errors.\n4. The active job count/mascot settles to idle after work finishes.\n5. Failed-then-retried job status shows correctly on the card and in the inspector. Use the corrupt file.\n6. Idle refresh skip. With the library idle and visible, record the getItemCards / list IPC traffic or count renders across 60+ seconds and one window blur/focus. The full reload should NOT run when nothing changed, and should run once after a change.\n7. Video: the poster lands, there is no <video> element in the grid, and the detail view plays and seeks.\n8. The updater: confirm no `app-update.yml` ENOENT error is logged at launch now.\n\nSave screenshots to C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\perf-e2e-4\\ (create it if missing). Clean up all processes you launched and restore the registry key.\n\nREPORT (concise):\n- pass/fail per item with evidence;\n- each bug with exact repro and suspected file;\n- what you couldn't test and why."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1072,"cache_read_input_tokens":188132,"output_tokens":1291,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1072,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1291,"cache_read_input_tokens":188132,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1072,"cache_