{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:58:09.382Z","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","content":"Delegated task node:delegated-task:command%3Amcp%3A4bb97746-8cea-4b70-a5b2-26b784b7216d%3Adelegate-task%3Aperf-e2e-luna-4 (E2E retest round 4 (gaps)) [completed]:\n`bun run build:dir` succeeded. No source files or Git state were changed. I used a scratch library and restored `HKCU\\Software\\Classes\\inkling` from the saved export; the app process I launched is stopped.\n\n| # | Result | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1. Incremental refresh | **Fail.** After an existing OCR job completed, all three marked card nodes were disconnected and the order changed. The target card showed the completed state. No item was captured during this check. | [After refresh](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\perf-e2e-4\\incremental-after2.png) |\n| 2. Search refresh | **Pass.** With a unique query active and its item as the sole result, an OCR job completed and the result disappeared; the empty state appeared. No console errors. | [Before job](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\perf-e2e-4\\search-before-job.png), [after job](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\perf-e2e-4\\search-after-job.png) |\n| 3. Archive then delete during work | **Pass.** Archived an item while the background queue had 21 active jobs; its card disappeared. Deleted it from Archive; the archive became empty, with no ghost card or renderer console errors. | [Archived](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\perf-e2e-4\\archived-running-job.png), [deleted](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\perf-e2e-4\\deleted-running-job.png) |\n| 4. Jobs and mascot return to idle | **Pass.** Active job count reached 0 and stayed there through the idle observation. The screenshot shows the mascot back in its resting view. | [Idle after 65 seconds](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\perf-e2e-4\\idle-after-65s.png) |\n| 5. Failed then retried status | **Fail / retry UI untested.** The corrupt JPEG’s thumbnail job failed after three retries with `VipsJpeg: premature end of JPEG image`. Its OCR attempt then opened a native main-process error dialog (“Error attempting to read image”), interrupting the card and inspector retry check. | [Native error dialog](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\perf-e2e-4\\screen-stuck.png) |\n| 6. Idle refresh skip | **Partial.** Across 65 seconds, the grid had 0 mutations and its marked nodes stayed connected in order. An app storage update caused a refresh; a second unchanged visibility event caused no further grid mutations. I counted DOM mutations, not IPC calls. The blur/focus was simulated because this CDP build lacks the visibility/window controls needed for a real native focus transition. | [After idle change](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\perf-e2e-4\\idle-after-change.png) |\n| 7. Video | **Pass.** The grid showed a poster and contained no `<video>` element. Detail playback advanced and sought to 1.5 seconds; no console errors. | [Video detail](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\perf-e2e-4\\video-detail-playing.png) |\n| 8. Updater launch log | **Pass.** The rebuilt app’s launch logs had no `app-update.yml ENOENT`. | Logs: `Temp\\agents\\perf-e2e-4\\stdout2.log` and `stderr2.log` |\n\n**Bugs and suspected files**\n\n- **Card remount/order change after job completion:** Repro: mark visible cards, reprocess OCR for an existing image, then compare nodes after completion. All marked nodes disconnected and the updated item moved to the top. Suspect [App.tsx](C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\perf-library-io\\src\\App.tsx): job patching versus the change-count fallback reload and position-based grid keys.\n- **Corrupt-image OCR opens a native error dialog:** Repro: capture a JPEG with a valid header and truncated/corrupted image data, then let OCR process it. Suspect the Tesseract worker error boundary in [ocr.mjs](C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\perf-library-io\\electron\\ocr.mjs), called by [ai-jobs.mjs](C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\perf-library-io\\electron\\ai-jobs.mjs).\n\nThe generated text image’s OCR job completed with empty text, so the search-refresh check used a unique sentinel in the **scratch** OCR field, then verified that re-OCR removed the result. The failed-job card and inspector retry flow remains unverified because the native error dialog interrupted the app. Actual native window blur/focus also remains unverified; only synthetic events were available under the CDP-only constraint."}
