{"parentUuid":"6a678fcb-a1d6-45f6-9847-57fd1c527088","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEPwe97UzCBuVKcrMBMw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the reorder comes from a full reload path—likely a retry handler or change-count fallback—while OCR bumping updated_at pushes the card to the top once that reload happens. The real issue is that background jobs bumping updated_at causes cards to jump unexpectedly, which breaks the \"quiet intelligence\" feel; maybe background work shouldn't touch updated_at at all since that field drives the \"recently changed\" sort.\n\nBut updated_at doesn't seem to feed FTS or sync, since FTS runs off triggers, so removing it from job writes should be safe. Other job writers—thumbnail, palette, embeddings, poster—might also be bumping it, so this is a slightly broader product decision, though I think stripping updated_at bumps from background job writes is the right fix while leaving user-driven edits (title, notes) to still bump the order, since that's intended behavior. I want to check which job storage writes actually set updated_at.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":619,"cache_read_input_tokens":196212,"output_tokens":518,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":358},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":619,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":518,"cache_read_input_tokens":196212,"cache_creation_input_tokens":619,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":619},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":6750,"thinkingD