{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","id":"1b5725ee-58ed-4264-babd-13db01fc02a7","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:59:49.801Z","version":"2.1.304","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"dfe7814906254ff001873d6255b116bdda00b295ee662266b96d56b73b9013f8","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"summarized"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"low"}},"base":"6c89be32-b273-437d-80b9-920e4e0911b7","keep":334,"tail":["0306cb9ee25aeb1459af8c122829513deba84ea10f8a60781072d3b326ae4c00","e39bc69a3cc0d3abb2c480f9b403e7a2f3d9c35a95a41057bc8d372a6fc930e6","716290aa3211dd94641430f94b9a6b639cd467e9a5ee9afb9bc7c9b6e90229dc"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",336,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"9a687a072d04fb940792d95229d3884a6692a3d0e54a7b3d74cd55f8e7c11c1b"}
{"parentUuid":"56e898e5-e956-4800-a256-159a29833159","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEQ3hF5BhFYmsGmpt6q9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Luna's round 4 confirmed the `app-update.yml` fix: the error no longer appears at launch. It also found two real bugs, both now fixed and pushed to #174. Their tests pass, but neither fix has been run in the app yet; round 5 is checking them now.\n\n**Passed in round 4:**\n- A job finishing during a search refreshes the results.\n- Archiving and then deleting an item while its jobs run leaves no leftover card.\n- The mascot and active job count settle back to idle.\n- Video: the grid shows the poster without loading the video, and the detail view plays and seeks.\n- The idle check is only partly confirmed. Nothing in the grid changed over 65 seconds, but Luna counted page updates rather than reload calls, and it could only simulate switching back to the window.\n\n**Bugs found and fixed:**\n1. **A card jumped to the top when OCR finished.** The library is sorted by last-updated time, and saving OCR text was bumping that time. So any full reload moved the image to the top and redrew the grid. This is older than the perf work. OCR no longer changes the last-updated time, so the grid order stays put.\n2. **A corrupt image opened a native error dialog.** The bad JPEG went straight into tesseract, whose worker throws in a way that crashes into the main process. Images are now decoded first, so a corrupt one just fails its OCR job quietly. A new test covers it.\n\n**Round 5** is checking:\n- an existing item's OCR finishing leaves every other card in place;\n- the corrupt image fails with no dialog;\n- the failed-then-retried status on the card and in the item view, which round 4 couldn't reach because the dialog got in the way;\n- OCR search, video posters and the Archive tab still work."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1696,"cache_read_input_tokens":203573,"output_tokens":570,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1696,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":570,"cache_read_input_tokens":203573,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1696,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1696},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEQ3gwhfQ84q46SHoA96","requestRef":"1b5725ee-58ed-4264-babd-13db01fc02a7","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"t3-code","attributionMcpTool":"delegate_task","type":"assistant","uuid":"ed0cb6df-7523-474a-a93c-87cc30271dcc","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:59:55.779Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","perTurnEffort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
