{"parentUuid":"55943668-76fa-4472-b150-5939c4955a66","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6fbfdc56-1f69-40e6-8ddc-6bc558efee7d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Delegated task node:delegated-task:command%3Amcp%3A4bb97746-8cea-4b70-a5b2-26b784b7216d%3Adelegate-task%3Aperf-e2e-luna-5 (E2E retest round 5) [completed]:\n## Round 5\n\n- **1. Existing image OCR — PASS.** Reprocessed the existing image without capturing anything. All three marked nodes stayed connected and were the same DOM nodes; order was unchanged. OCR and its follow-up embedding completed, the card settled, and `updatedAt` did not change. [Settled result](C:/Users/chris/AppData/Local/Temp/agents/chat-images/perf-e2e-5/check1-settled.png)\n\n- **2. Corrupt JPEG — PASS, with a retry caveat.** No native error dialog appeared in 24 full-screen PowerShell captures; stdout/stderr contained no image-read dialog text. OCR, thumbnail, and embedding jobs failed with JPEG decode errors, while the item remained an image card showing its filename and failure state. The inspector’s **Try again** action showed processing and then failure again. That retry requeued the embedding job; OCR remained failed, so an OCR-specific retry through the UI was not verified. [Full-screen captures](C:/Users/chris/AppData/Local/Temp/agents/chat-images/perf-e2e-5/corrupt-watch-contact-sheet.png) · [Failed inspector](C:/Users/chris/AppData/Local/Temp/agents/chat-images/perf-e2e-5/corrupt-inspector-failed.png)\n\n- **3. Sanity checks — PASS.** The good text image’s OCR completed and searching `7429` returned that image alone. The video card showed its poster; playback and seeking worked. Archive displayed the video in its tab, and Restore returned it to the library. [OCR search](C:/Users/chris/AppData/Local/Temp/agents/chat-images/perf-e2e-5/good-ocr-search-settled.png) · [Video playback](C:/Users/chris/AppData/Local/Temp/agents/chat-images/perf-e2e-5/video-detail-playing.png) · [Archive](C:/Users/chris/AppData/Local/Temp/agents/chat-images/perf-e2e-5/archive-video.png)\n\nThe reused round 4 check script had a polling bug: it used the job ID where the item ID was required. I reran the check with corrected polling. No product bug was confirmed. The OCR-specific UI retry remains untested because the visible retry action requeued the embedding job.\n\n`bun run build:dir` completed. No source files were edited. The app and sampler processes were stopped, and the registry key was restored; its post-run export matched the pre-run export."},"uuid":"456cb563-c6ad-4c28-bd33-4674331a36ef","timestamp":"2026-10-21T00:14:03.982Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","promptSource":"sdk","turnOrigin":"sdk","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":0,"turnIndex":132},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
