{"parentUuid":"eda44978-f64d-4fbb-92ed-d793f37b3853","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e64edfd1-8e8e-4d2c-9a35-dc55661b290e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Avr1YWZEKEJDiZ3zA9Xm8V","type":"tool_result","content":"  .first-run-keys,\n  .first-run-keys kbd,\n  .first-run-crumb .breadcrumb-list > *,\n  .memory-card,\n  .memory-slot {\n    animation: none;\n  }\n  .reads-card,\n  .reads-search,\n  .reads-receipt,\n  .reads-receipt-mark {\n    animation: none;\n    transition: none;\n  }\n  .reads-beam {\n    display: none;\n  }\n  .kept-card,\n  .memory-found {\n    animation: none;\n  }\n  .memory-dot {\n    animation: none !important;\n    opacity: 0.5;\n  }\n  .memory-dot.is-last {\n    opacity: 1;\n  }\n}\n/* Toolbar and search, floating over the grid (Paper artboards 1.1 to 1.3).\n   Back/forward and the view toggle sit left, the search pill is centred, Add\n   is right. The grid starts at the toolbar's top edge so cards scroll under\n   the glass, except while a query is pinned: then it starts below the filter\n   row (`.library-scroll.has-pinned-query`). The toolbar passes pointer events\n   through its empty space. Glass comes from `.glass`. */\n.capture-bar {\n  position: relative;\n  z-index: 2;\n  display: flex;\n  flex: 0 0 auto;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 8px;\n  height: 52px;\n  pointer-events: none;\n}\n.capture-bar > * {\n  pointer-events: auto;\n}\n.capture-bar > .capture-status {\n  pointer-events: none;\n}\n.library-scroll {\n  flex: 1 1 auto;\n  min-height: 0;\n  overflow: hidden;\n  position: relative;\n  scrollbar-width: none;\n  -ms-overflow-style: none;\n  margin-top: -52px;\n}\n/* Paper 1.3: the 44px filter row and the grid's 4px top padding put the first\n   card 100px below the toolbar's top. The -52px pull-up above cancels the\n   52px toolbar, so the pinned offset is 100 - 52. */\n.library-scroll.has-pinned-query {\n  margin-top: 48px;\n}\n.history-nav,\n.view-controls {\n  position: relative;\n  display: flex;\n  flex: 0 0 auto;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 2px;\n  height: 34px;\n  min-width: 0;\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 3px;\n  border-radius: 999px;\n}\n.history-button,\n.view-button {\n  display: grid;\n  place-items: center;\n  width: 26px;\n  height: 26px;\n  padding: 0;\n  border: 0;\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  background: transparent;\n  cursor: pointer;\n}\n.history-button {\n  color: var(--library-text-soft);\n  transition: color 0.18s ease;\n}\n.history-button:hover:not(:disabled) {\n  color: var(--ink);\n}\n.history-button:disabled {\n  opacity: 0.35;\n  cursor: default;\n----\n/* Library grid and cards (Paper artboard 1.1). Masonry columns are 286px with a\n   12px gap; App.tsx mirrors both (GRID_GAP, TARGET_CARD_WIDTH). Virtuoso lays the\n   columns out in a flex row, so `.library-grid` gap is the real column gap.\n   Images take their media ratio. Typed cards (article, quote, note, PDF, file,\n   video) use fixed Paper heights, with no border. The list view reuses this\n   markup with 155px artwork; its overrides sit at the end of this block. */\n.library-grid {\n  min-width: 0;\n  min-height: 100%;\n  gap: 12px;\n  scrollbar-width: none;\n  -ms-overflow-style: none;\n}\n.library-grid::-webkit-scrollbar {\n  display: none;\n  width: 0;\n---\n}\n.detail-attribution:empty {\n  display: none;\n}\n.serendipity-stage {\n  height: 100%;\n  overflow-y: auto;\n  padding: 18px 0 44px;\n  scrollbar-width: none;\n}\n.serendipity-stage::-webkit-scrollbar {\n  display: none;\n  width: 0;\n  height: 0;\n}\n.serendipity-intro {\n  width: min(820px, 100%);\n  margin: 0 auto;\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: flex-end;\n  justify-content: space-between;\n  gap: 24px;\n}\n.serendipity-intro-copy {\n  min-width: 0;\n}\n.serendipity-eyebrow {\n  margin: 0 0 10px;\n  color: var(--orange);\n  font: 10px var(--font-ui);\n  letter-spacing: 0.12em;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n}\n.serendipity-intro h1 {\n  margin: 0;\n  color: var(--ink);\n  font:\n    400 clamp(28px, 4vw, 42px) / 1.08 \"Libre Baskerville\",\n    Georgia,\n    serif;\n  letter-spacing: -0.04em;\n}\n.serendipity-intro-copy > p:last-child {\n  max-width: 48ch;\n  margin: 12px 0 0;\n  color: var(--muted);\n  font-size: 13px;\n  line-height: 1.55;\n}\n.serendipity-progress {\n  flex: 0 0 auto;\n  margin: 0 0 5px;\n  color: var(--muted);\n  font: 10px var(--font-ui);\n  white-space: nowrap;\n}\n.serendipity-browse {\n  width: min(820px, 100%);\n  margin: 30px auto 0;\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: minmax(240px, 350px) minmax(0, 1fr);\n  gap: 34px;\n  align-items: center;\n}\n.serendipity-art {\n  min-width: 0;\n}\n.serendipity-art .library-card-slot {\n  padding-bottom: 0;\n}\n.serendipity-art .library-card {\n  width: 100%;\n}\n.serendipity-copy {\n  min-width: 0;\n}\n.serendipity-kicker {\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: space-between;\n  gap: 12px;\n---\n  color: var(--muted);\n  font-size: 13px;\n  line-height: 1.55;\n}\n.empty-state {\n  padding: 80px 20px;\n  text-align: center;\n  border: 1px dashed var(--rule);\n  border-radius: var(--sidebar-radius);\n}\n.empty-icon {\n  width: 42px;\n  height: 42px;\n  margin: 0 auto var(--small-component);\n  display: grid;\n  place-items: center;\n  border-radius: 50%;\n  color: var(--muted);\n  background: var(--surface);\n}\n.empty-state h2 {\n  margin: 0;\n  font:\n    400 24px \"Libre Baskerville\",\n    Georgia,\n    serif;\n  letter-spacing: -0.04em;\n}\n.empty-state p {\n  margin: 9px 0 17px;\n  color: var(--muted);\n  font-size: 13px;\n}\n.text-button {\n  border: 0;\n  background: none;\n  color: var(--orange);\n  cursor: pointer;\n  font-size: 13px;\n  text-decoration: underline;\n  text-underline-offset: 3px;","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"085a3f6a-273b-45c6-b847-c03d0de657a7","timestamp":"2026-10-21T02:00:26.275Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"  .first-run-keys,\n  .first-run-keys kbd,\n  .first-run-crumb .breadcrumb-list > *,\n  .memory-card,\n  .memory-slot {\n    ani