{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"1d9f62291e71c31413f6a21737c4dba2f9a5b5cb6746a8a682e0c96de77af587","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm reconsidering the coordinates — the outer rounded box at x=33 is actually the inkling window itself, while the frame I thought was the main app is really the inner content area starting around x=265.\n\nComparing with the browser version, stage boundaries seem shifted in the Electron window — top inset around 45px, bottom only 5px, so the overlay isn't symmetric like it is in the browser. That makes me think the overlay's height may be fixed to the full window while its top offset gets pushed down by the titlebar, so I should check wherever the JS sets the overlay's position to find why it's misaligned.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TvXYhJLVE3pToK39YBDwU5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && grep -n \"frameRect\\|getBoundingClientRect\\|libraryFrameRef\\|is-placed\\|titlebar\" src/components/ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx | head -40","description":"Find overlay placement logic"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
