{"parentUuid":"2d4de4d2-0d88-46c3-8371-33a862eaca64","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_012SwH3UfCzx95zL3g9kXgcQ","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d06e3fd4-16f0-47c0-81d5-0d301743c8ed","timestamp":"2026-10-21T02:03:31.002Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"d06e3fd4-16f0-47c0-81d5-0d301743c8ed","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEZSzQcxZ6SPXHoqVeNL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm working out the geometry: the overlay starts below the 36px window-controls band, with an 8px inset giving the stage top at 44 and bottom at 712, which roughly matches the screenshot's measurements. The top/bottom gap asymmetry seems intentional because of that control band, and the user's markup seems to be asking for the stage to extend upward into that band.\n\nNow I'm noticing the sidebar's collapse tab is partially hidden behind the overlay since the overlay's left edge aligns with the main content left edge, while the tab sits slightly further left -- this means the overlay's z-index is covering part of the tab. I also want to check the stage's left inset, which seems to be zero while the other three sides use an 8px inset, creating an inconsistency I should resolve by giving the stage uniform insets on all sides matching the toolbar row's vertical position.\n\nThe drag region at the top eats clicks near the toolbar, which explains that gap band. So I'll drop the separate band and just inset the stage to match the resting grid exactly: top at 37, bottom at 30, left at 14, so it lines up with the library-scroll rect at rest.\n\nThis also means in the browser preview without a titlebar, the same main-content padding should apply uniformly — so I'll derive frameRect by adding padding on all sides consistently across both runtimes, rather than special-casing the titlebar height.\n\nThen I want the stage itself to use an asymmetric inset (0 on top/bottom/left, 320px reserved on the right for the inspector), which lines up the stage top with the library scroll top and keeps everything visually consistent with the grid, including how the flight animation and overlay border-radius/background read against the sidebar edge.\n\nChecking for overlaps: the window controls, drag region, and the sidebar collapse tab all clear the new stage/overlay boundaries fine once the inspector starts at the right offset. Focus mode has its own styling path so it's unaffected, and I should make sure the resize handler and other destination-rect logic all consistently use frameRect.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1918,"cache_read_input_tokens":138818,"output_tokens":2063,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1902},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1918,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2063,"cache_read_input_tokens":138818,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1918,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1918},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":23297,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEZSz81HkEa9dKP7oECa","requestRef":"7886c978-c6bf-4fc3-8d1c-4953e746a5ad","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"145078c9-c346-436e-b7e2-fb8ae81cc187","timestamp":"2026-10-21T02:03:31.001Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
