{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"43bf657572444fb02118396ce59196576285f728caf179729c752fe6bdf981fd","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking the actual grid width — at 1280px with four columns the lanterns card is shorter, around 171px tall, so the 52px toolbar overlap is now 30%, which crosses the 25% threshold and counts as too much hidden content.\n\nThis explains the infinite loop with exactly this first item. My padding fix addresses the underlying geometry issue, but I should also add a safeguard: if the scroll position doesn't actually change after adjustment, just resolve with the current rects instead of looping forever.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017G9mbZo34pagUKue8hg232","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && python - <<'EOF'\np='src/App.tsx';s=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\nold='''            if (isCardTooFarOffscreen(rects.card, currentViewport)) {\n              scrollElement.scrollTop += rects.card.top - currentViewport.top - 16;\n              requestAnimationFrame(waitForCard);\n              return;\n            }'''\nnew='''            if (isCardTooFarOffscreen(rects.card, currentViewport)) {\n              // At either end of the list the scroll can't move, so take the card\n              // where it is rather than waiting forever (Back would never close).\n              const before = scrollElement.scrollTop;\n              scrollElement.scrollTop += rects.card.top - currentViewport.top - 16;\n              if (scrollElement.scrollTop !== before) {\n                requestAnimationFrame(waitForCard);\n                return;\n              }\n            }'''\nassert s.count(old)==1; s=s.replace(old,new); open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nEOF","description":"Stop the card-into-view loop when scroll is stuck"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
