{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"23f3559f9b696d6142b0a7943805f41760f3a9ebcd95aae2a9c5f18d9b904c2e","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm thinking about an archive handler that reuses the closing animation's shrink-toward-card-rect motion, but fades the item out instead of letting it return to its spot, then calls onForget once the fade completes.\n\nI need to be careful about the error case: if onForget fails, the overlay would be left invisible but still mounted since selectedItem wasn't cleared. So instead of firing onForget before the shrink animation, I should animate first, then await onForget, and only if the overlay is still mounted afterward (meaning an error occurred) restore its opacity and geometry back to normal. I'm writing the archiveFromView function that captures the dialog's starting rect, computes a shrunk destination centered on it, and guards against missing refs or reduced-motion preference by just calling onForget directly in those cases.\n\nI'm leaning toward reusing the existing flight/close state machine rather than a separate archiving flag, since the close flight already handles the \"is-flying\" visual treatment. I want to extend the close flight type with an optional fade flag so that when fading, opacity tweens to zero across the animation and onComplete calls onForget instead of onClose -- so I need to check the Flight type definition to add this field.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018Ntt5hzqHbf1vNTnhqrGFF","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && sed -n 88,112p src/components/ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx; grep -n \"onForget\" src/components/ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx; grep -n \"OVERLAY_FLIGHT_MS =\\|OVERLAY_EASE =\" -r src | head","description":"Read Flight type and onForget uses"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
