{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","prNumber":170,"prUrl":"https://github.com/Squidys-Tools/inkling/pull/170","prRepository":"Squidys-Tools/inkling","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:08:40.986Z"}
{"parentUuid":"31d71c8b-ca8b-414b-8788-6024c62750e7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a5d551ad-5e9e-431c-a603-b554797c9ccd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019b5HKmVepQVg5TdCRQPLCW","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"fluidglass glass shader edge light refraction webgpu\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Building an Infinite Liquid Glass Grid with Three.js, WebGPU, and TSL\",\"url\":\"https://tympanus.net/codrops/?p=120372\"},{\"title\":\"# liquidGL – Ultra-light glassmorphism for the web\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/liquid-gl@2.0.1/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"gogz_liquid 0.1.0 copy \\\"gogz_liquid: ^0.1.0\\\" to clipboard\",\"url\":\"https://pub.dev/packages/gogz_liquid\"},{\"title\":\"OneClient Liquid Glass\",\"url\":\"https://pub.dev/documentation/oc_liquid_glass/0.3.0/\"},{\"title\":\"Fluid Glass UI\",\"url\":\"https://godotshaders.com/shader/fluid-glass-ui/\"},{\"title\":\"Help this asset pack reach its goal\",\"url\":\"https://binbun3d.itch.io/fluid-glass-ui\"},{\"title\":\"oc_liquid_glass 0.3.0 copy \\\"oc_liquid_glass: ^0.3.0\\\" to clipboard\",\"url\":\"https://pub.dev/packages/oc_liquid_glass/versions/0.3.0\"},{\"title\":\"Glass Material\",\"url\":\"https://luma.gl/docs/api-reference/experimental/glass-material\"},{\"title\":\"Liquid Glass Studio\",\"url\":\"https://docsearch.algolia.com/mcp/docs/repo/iyinchao/liquid-glass-studio\"}]\n\nI didn't find a library called \"fluidglass\" for WebGPU. The closest matches were these:\n\n- **Codrops / Shader article (Three.js + WebGPU + TSL):** This is the most relevant hit. It describes a liquid glass grid built on flat, subdivided planes, with the rounded corners, beveled edges, and refraction all faked in the material. It also derives a normal from the slope between texture samples, which is the usual way to get edge refraction.\n- **Liquid Glass Studio (GitHub):** A web engine that utilizes WebGL2 and WebGPU to deliver realistic refraction, dispersion, and shape-merging effects via custom shaders and SDF-defined shapes.\n- **luma.gl glassMaterial:** An experimental, cross-backend shader module for refractive translucent surfaces. It combines transmission, Fresnel reflection, and dispersion.\n- **liquidGL:** A web library whose dispersion concentrates at the bevelled edge and vanishes at the flat centre. I didn't see a WebGPU mention for it.\n- **Fluid Glass UI (Godot):** Not WebGPU, but it shows the edge-curve approach: refraction based on the curve of the edge, plus a rim light option.\n\nIf you meant a specific package named \"fluidglass,\" tell me the source or maintainer and I can search for that directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8ed969f4-744e-4778-b225-1b3f7051f6e4","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:08:41.438Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"fluidglass glass shader edge light refraction webgpu","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01KuFVXttRV91hRdxKwK5Hyu","content":[{"title":"Building an Infinite Liquid Glass Grid with Three.js, WebGPU, and TSL","url":"https://tympanus.net/codrops/?p=120372"},{"title":"# liquidGL – Ultra-light glassmorphism for the web","url":"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/liquid-gl@2.0.1/README.md"},{"title":"gogz_liquid 0.1.0 copy \"gogz_liquid: ^0.1.0\" to clipboard","url":"https://pub.dev/packages/gogz_liquid"},{"title":"OneClient Liquid Glass","url":"https://pub.dev/documentation/oc_liquid_glass/0.3.0/"},{"title":"Fluid Glass UI","url":"https://godotshaders.com/shader/fluid-glass-ui/"},{"title":"Help this asset pack reach its goal","url":"https://binbun3d.itch.io/fluid-glass-ui"},{"title":"oc_liquid_glass 0.3.0 copy \"oc_liquid_glass: ^0.3.0\" to clipboard","url":"https://pub.dev/packages/oc_liquid_glass/versions/0.3.0"},{"title":"Glass Material","url":"https://luma.gl/docs/api-reference/experimental/glass-material"},{"title":"Liquid Glass Studio","url":"https://docsearch.algolia.com/mcp/docs/repo/iyinchao/liquid-glass-studio"}]},"I didn't find a library called \"fluidglass\" for WebGPU. The closest matches were these:\n\n- **Codrops / Shader article (Three.js + WebGPU + TSL):** This is the most relevant hit. It describes a liquid glass grid built on flat, subdivided planes, with the rounded corners, beveled edges, and refraction all faked in the material. It also derives a normal from the slope between texture samples, which is the usual way to get edge refraction.\n- **Liquid Glass Studio (GitHub):** A web engine that utilizes WebGL2 and WebGPU to deliver realistic refraction, dispersion, and shape-merging effects via custom shaders and SDF-defined shapes.\n- **luma.gl glassMaterial:** An experimental, cross-backend shader module for refractive translucent surfaces. It combines transmission, Fresnel reflection, and dispersion.\n- **liquidGL:** A web library whose dispersion concentrates at the bevelled edge and vanishes at the flat centre. I didn't see a WebGPU mention for it.\n- **Fluid Glass UI (Godot):** Not WebGPU, but it shows the edge-curve approach: refraction based on the curve of the edge, plus a rim light option.\n\nIf you meant a specific package named \"fluidglass,\" tell me the source or maintainer and I can search for that directly."],"durationSeconds":6.426008099999978,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"31d71c8b-ca8b-414b-8788-6024c62750e7","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
