{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"f3f0ff4c77bb81d08944140da0af8085721da2dd7c78b23c1d7e7ca12ddb5e69","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm wary of adding this much machinery just because it looks architecturally impressive, but the user explicitly requested it via the Paper note, so I need to think through how it would realistically work. The liquid-dom approach uses a canvas that captures live DOM content into GPU textures so glass elements can refract whatever's behind them, which means the content under the glass needs to be structured in a way that supports this.\n\nThe note mentions thumbnails working fine under glass while full-size images caused hitches, and flags the virtualized grid as untested -- it sounds like someone already experimented with this on a demo. I should check npm for the actual liquid-dom packages to see what's really available.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QLgknXvDE31VKxqMgFCCX9","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && timeout 60 npm view @liquid-dom/react name version dist.unpackedSize dependencies peerDependencies license 2>&1 | head -40; timeout 60 npm view @liquid-dom/core name version dist.unpackedSize dependencies license 2>&1 | head -30","description":"Look up liquid-dom packages on npm"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
