{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","prNumber":170,"prUrl":"https://github.com/Squidys-Tools/inkling/pull/170","prRepository":"Squidys-Tools/inkling","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:09:15.607Z"}
{"parentUuid":"de1b3d0d-9053-4045-8c13-16cb3836e347","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEj4tzEjmhXVoUzxzasc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a significant architectural shift — to use liquid-dom, the library grid would need to live inside the liquid scene's canvas as an Html node, since children there are only hit-tested and laid out but not directly painted, requiring explicit drawing via drawElementImage.\n\nThis raises real concerns: whether text selection and accessibility still work properly since hit-testing depends on synced transforms, and whether the virtualized grid's scroll behavior survives being nested inside canvas-managed content. There's apparently a prior experiment showing comparable frame times to CSS, but I'm now weighing whether there's a lighter-weight way to get the same visual effect without going all-in on HTML-in-Canvas.\n\nSince the glass elements themselves are small UI pieces, I'm considering using an SVG displacement filter through backdrop-filter instead — the known \"liquid glass\" CSS trick that works in Chromium, which is what Electron ships. This would combine a displacement map for edge refraction with a specular highlight, and since Skia can run feDisplacementMap on GPU, performance should hold up fine for elements this size.\n\nThe user wants liquid glass applied to all translucent buttons and made the default, which makes me wonder if there's already an experimental toggle or implementation elsewhere — maybe in another worktree where they tested this. I should search other worktrees for references to \"liquid-dom\" to see if this was already prototyped somewhere.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11931,"cache_read_input_tokens":83016,"output_tokens":1388,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1131},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11931,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1388,"cache_read_input_tokens":83016,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11931,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11931},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":13486,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEj4tiNGbTcP96XYSqXQ","requestRef":"2ad42971-ecd1-4ab1-afef-84025d0bd8ce","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"45a4b33f-84e4-4f21-b5bc-1edc11e9fb0a","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:09:29.703Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
