{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"7b17f335bfea1821729de72d2aeb40a5e71fb4d7c8e2d75de6fe6d12850830da","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I notice the canvas has the right APIs available, but navigator.gpu is undefined, which suggests WebGPU isn't accessible because the context isn't secure—likely because about:blank doesn't count as a secure context when opened this way. That makes me wonder whether the app is actually loading through file:// or a custom protocol instead.\n\nI should look at how the renderer is loaded in electron/main.mjs, then test by probing with a matching file:// or custom scheme URL to confirm.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N1ftDtURxwopkn5pgCx8Zv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && grep -n \"loadURL\\|loadFile\\|registerSchemesAsPrivileged\\|webPreferences\\|appendSwitch\\|enableBlinkFeatures\\|secure\" electron/main.mjs | head -30","description":"Check how the Electron app loads the renderer"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
