{"parentUuid":"b255e1fa-46fe-4744-a593-5a96c1cb890d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01Q7swrBt9Qw7hbcVx56weXM","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b991bf94-2143-444c-9dbd-e10ade86b400","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:16:00.740Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"b991bf94-2143-444c-9dbd-e10ade86b400","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEjYTgFpU7YqxMifiFLJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm reconsidering the structure: the toolbar floats above the library scroll area which has a negative margin so cards scroll underneath it, and I'm thinking about whether the liquid canvas should actually replace the library-scroll's rendering rather than sit behind it as a separate backdrop.\n\nNow I'm working out the layering more precisely—canvas sized to the library-scroll box with the toolbar controls drawn above it at z-index 2, glass surfaces positioned at the control rects relative to the canvas. I need to check the edge-tab positioning since it sits near the frame's padding edge, potentially straddling outside the canvas bounds, and also account for how the query-chip and capture-error status row shift the grid down when a pinned query is active.\n\nI'm realizing when a query is pinned, the filter row sits above the grid rather than over it, meaning the query-chip glass would end up outside the canvas and only see the flat frame background instead of grid content behind it—so I should consider expanding the canvas to cover the entire main-content box and reworking how the library-scroll content gets portaled into it.\n\nOne approach is to absolutely position the library-scroll inside the canvas host and manually replicate its padding and spacing, though that feels fragile. A cleaner option is to put the whole main-content (grid, toolbar, everything) inside the canvas, using the layering rule where Html below a container becomes its backdrop and Html above covers it—so I'd stack the grid as backdrop, the glass shapes as the container, and the toolbar as a layer on top, keeping the toolbar crisp instead of blurred.\n\nI'm now weighing whether the mascot eyes in the search field animate continuously, since that affects whether the toolbar host needs constant repaint and recapture. The alternative of keeping controls as native DOM above the canvas is simpler and cheaper, but then the glass panels need to be positioned by measuring those controls rather than rendering everything through the GPU.\n\nFor syncing the glass rects during the search field's transition, I think a rAF loop driven by transition start/end events would work better than a ResizeObserver, since position changes like translate or top aren't picked up by resize observation—only size changes are.\n\nI'll also account for framer-motion animations inside controls, like the view-selection pill sliding within view-controls, which doesn't affect the glass container's own rect. Then I need to work out the CSS toggling: the `.glass` class applies the border, background, shadow, and backdrop-filter by default, but when a liquid-glass mode is active on the root, those styles get stripped out so the glass effect is handled differently.\n\nOne tricky bit is per-control variation, like the search field's mascot state needing a deeper shadow — but since shadows are set at the liquid container level, not per glass element, I can't vary them individually without separate containers. I also need to worry about fusion: nearby glass elements within the same container merge into one blob if their spacing is under the fusion threshold, so I need to decide whether to group controls like history-nav and view-controls into separate containers to avoid unwanted gooey merging given their 8px gap.\n\nThen there's the question of how canvas and DOM layers interact — the canvas renders the grid and glass surfaces, while the actual control icons sit in a transparent DOM layer on top, so scrolling triggers a paint-copy-render cycle each frame while the controls stay static. I'm also working out where the glass rectangles are positioned in canvas space relative to the main content container, since the backdrop needs to track control positions correctly.\n\nI need to check whether the sidebar edge tab sits inside or outside the main container's bounds, since anything outside would get clipped by the canvas. I also need to verify what background color shows through the main-content area — it looks like it's transparent, so the app-shell's own background is what's visible beneath everything, and I should check whether rounded corners come from clipping at the canvas level.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2402,"cache_read_input_tokens":135141,"output_tokens":2914,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2821},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2402,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2914,"cache_read_input_tokens":135141,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2402,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2402},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":30620,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEjYTKvgJ6bESSsDiqxG","requestRef":"77409633-63ea-4772-8339-f807ce7f1136","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1ba73309-e83e-4328-b5d0-cdfb41eb5d5c","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:16:00.739Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
