{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"92c82721832ab76c3c28033922e4562bba7c5e33a81972b5d0da51122dad1816","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm thinking about how the edge tab's glass effect should track its bounding rect during the 3D flip animation when it closes, since the rotateY perspective narrows the rect as it rotates — I may need to hide the liquid glass during the flip and let plain CSS handle that transition instead.\n\nBut I also need to check positioning: the edge tab sits at the frame's left edge inside the padding area, while the canvas starts further in past the padding, so the canvas might not actually cover the tab's location. I should look at the edge-tab's base styles around lines 700-735 to confirm its exact placement.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014KHX54VQ5HQfFmLbtin9gp","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && sed -n 690,735p src/App.css && sed -n 85,140p src/App.css && grep -n \"GradualBlur\" src/*.tsx src/components/*.tsx | head","description":"Read edge tab base and app shell CSS"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
