{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"3a512fe08bb64db06ebdf8778c8642c8e05d4e77d8d7bf2108e7735c774e17fb","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm considering whether to add GPU types as a dependency or declare minimal types locally, then starting to write the LiquidGlass component importing the container, glass, and scene pieces I'll need.\n\nI'm deciding to dynamically import the core library so it stays out of the main bundle for web preview but loads quickly in Electron. Now I'm writing a memoized support-check function that verifies canvas subtree layout, WebGPU availability, and reduced-transparency media preferences before enabling liquid glass.\n\nEach stage should independently handle device loss by awaiting `device.lost` and falling back to CSS until the next reload rather than attempting automatic retries. I also want to check whether there's a user-facing setting for liquid glass -- I should look at the Settings General tab to see if an appearance section already exists where I could add a toggle.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AYJCN4Dt4ENsspViYSxZ9n","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && grep -n \"settingsTab ===\\|settings-section\\|localStorage\\.\\(get\\|set\\)Item\\|useLocalStorage\\|readPreference\\|PREF\" src/App.tsx | head -40","description":"Inspect settings tabs and preference storage"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
