{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","prNumber":170,"prUrl":"https://github.com/Squidys-Tools/inkling/pull/170","prRepository":"Squidys-Tools/inkling","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:21:24.437Z"}
{"parentUuid":"80bd71aa-2b0d-4eb4-9986-ba90f55bc0f7","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01WXTtmv1An4ne8Hc2bLxUpp","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"cb488308-e522-4ed8-bca5-26710d3cc9d1","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:21:40.568Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"cb488308-e522-4ed8-bca5-26710d3cc9d1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEjzd2oPFzXxU4Zax4mE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'll skip adding a settings toggle since it's unnecessary here—making liquid glass the default means it's on without a flag, rather than opt-in. The CSS fallback stays automatic, and I could mention a toggle as a future option, but I won't build one now.\n\nI'm also considering the `prefers-reduced-transparency` media query for accessibility, but that feels like scope creep, so I'll skip it and keep things minimal.\n\nNow I'm designing the LiquidGlassStage component structure, defining props for the backdrop content and target elements, then sketching out how it's used in both the library view and the zoom pill.\n\nFor the zoom lens, the pill itself acts as the target root, with the lens backdrop absolutely positioned behind the buttons using negative z-index, inheriting the pill's border radius and clipping overflow. The tricky part is positioning the image replica correctly relative to the pill, which requires measuring both the image and pill bounding rects via `getBoundingClientRect()` in an effect whenever zoom or pan changes, then applying that offset directly to the replica's style.\n\nI'm now wondering if it's cleaner to make the LiquidGlass component generically handle mirroring an image through a `mirror` prop, keeping an internal replica synced to the mirrored element's on-screen position. The challenge is detecting when the mirrored element moves, since pan/zoom updates its transform via style changes rather than React re-renders -- so I'd need either a callback from the zoomable image or a MutationObserver watching the style and src attributes.\n\nThinking it through more, I think the cleaner approach is for ExpandedItemOverlay's ZoomableImage to pass its image ref directly into the lens component as a prop. I want to check how ZoomableImage actually applies zoom and pan state to the element's style before deciding.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":760,"cache_read_input_tokens":196392,"output_tokens":1521,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1299},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":760,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1521,"cache_read_input_tokens":196392,"cache_creation_input_tokens":760,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":760},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":15387,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEjzcjSvqYG8XL3QxK5r","requestRef":"1fd63a34-ad86-421e-9769-ad53d41361c7","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"35b52f37-4339-4fb0-8118-4d44f4601cd6","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:21:40.568Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"35b52f37-4339-4fb0-8118-4d44f4601cd6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEjzd2oPFzXxU4Zax4mE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Next I'm reading the zoom code, so the pill's lens can track the image as it pans and zooms."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":760,"cache_read_input_tokens":196392,"output_tokens":1521,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1299},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":760,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1521,"cache_read_input_tokens":196392,"cache_creation_input_tokens":760,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":760},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgEjzcjSvqYG8XL3QxK5r","requestRef":"1fd63a34-ad86-421e-9769-ad53d41361c7","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"635701ba-814f-43da-8b8b-4728415078c6","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:21:40.572Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
