{"parentUuid":"13c0ed34-3dd2-475a-8226-c663b1137c09","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01Kbqx4ra5568ii3sh7Gh2as","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"77ef658a-e831-4a49-b803-592299b8e665","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:23:04.632Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"77ef658a-e831-4a49-b803-592299b8e665","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEk6ep8KqHmwgwXcXENJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm thinking the stage's dotted radial gradient background would get blurred into near-uniform color in the lens replica anyway, so I can just approximate it with a plain solid color close to #121110 rather than replicating the exact dot pattern and positioning math.\n\nI'm also checking the mobile media query padding at 780px breakpoint — Electron's 320px minWidth means narrow windows could trigger this layout, so I'm defining a CSS variable for the library-scroll top offset that differs between desktop (titlebar height plus 4px) and mobile (30px header padding plus 12px, totaling 42px). I'm leaning toward keeping the absolute positioning approach for the stage since it stays clean, accepting that the capture area will extend slightly beyond library-scroll's actual box into the rest of main's padding region.\n\nFor pointer events in liquid mode, I'm confirming that clicks on empty toolbar space (which has pointer-events disabled) should fall through to the canvas and correctly hit-test the underlying grid cards, since Chromium hit-tests subtree children using their CSS transforms per spec — so focus, keyboard nav, text selection, and context menus on cards should all keep working through the DOM as before. I'm flagging that drag-and-drop for images might break and needs checking later, and now I'm thinking through DPR handling for crisp grid text — using devicePixelRatio but capping it at 2 to avoid excessive cost on high-density displays.\n\nI want to size the canvas precisely to device pixels to avoid blur, ideally using ResizeObserver's devicePixelContentBoxSize when available for exactness. Now I'm planning to write the LiquidGlass module as a single component file containing a memoized support check and the main component, with tunable glass-look parameters like blur and spacing that I'll need to calibrate.\n\nStill writing config values... I should check whether spacing of zero is actually valid for preventing fusion by looking at how the shader uses that value.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7904,"cache_read_input_tokens":200744,"output_tokens":1644,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1448},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7904,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1644,"cache_read_input_tokens":200744,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7904,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7904},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":17792,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEk6eLMYGehBFg51v61N","requestRef":"7432b421-7ceb-4afd-8ed9-58762307641b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b056e5ff-d9ef-439e-a48b-4a196b70fcd8","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:23:04.631Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
