{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","prNumber":170,"prUrl":"https://github.com/Squidys-Tools/inkling/pull/170","prRepository":"Squidys-Tools/inkling","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:23:56.798Z"}
{"parentUuid":"55b5f5e3-63b4-46e8-af8a-d4fc3a22da4b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEkBrs4iFMpvpC91xhi2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm tracing how the content gets appended to the wrap element, then when GPU mode activates, LiquidSurface wraps it in an Html node whose host stays detached until sync() attaches it to the canvas during the paint cycle—triggered by the resize observer firing on initial mount.\n\nBut the host just got appended mid-paint, so there's no record to copy yet for that frame, causing a one-frame delay before the content actually renders. Calling sync() directly in the constructor should fix this by attaching the host synchronously, leaving at most a brief blank flash on initial load that's acceptable since it only happens at app startup.\n\nI'll gate \"shown\" status on checking that the backdrop's copied width is actually greater than zero, rather than just checking whether a draw happened, since the draw could occur before content is copied.\n\nFor the glass shape geometry, I'm working out the logic in a separate module: computing position, size, and radius from a box with per-corner radii, extending flat edges outward, and returning null when the shape doesn't intersect the canvas — handling the edge-tab case and the generic rule for flat-side detection and clamping the radius to half the smaller dimension.\n\nI'm also checking performance concerns around reading computed styles and bounding rects per frame during the settle loop, considering how opacity cascades from parent elements onto target pills, and confirming TypeScript's device pixel box size types. I need to add a custom type declaration for the canvas's requestPaint method since TypeScript doesn't recognize it natively.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5159,"cache_read_input_tokens":213666,"output_tokens":2720,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1372},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5159,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2720,"cache_read_input_tokens":213666,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5159,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5159},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":15142,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEkBrUjtx32KV4Am2skH","requestRef":"c64ec727-96a6-412d-9d2b-fa1819359019","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"23b783af-4a4e-474b-82f9-812716f36c67","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:24:12.753Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"23b783af-4a4e-474b-82f9-812716f36c67","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEkBrs4iFMpvpC91xhi2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I need two small pieces: a pure helper that turns an element's box into a glass shape, and its tests."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5159,"cache_read_input_tokens":213666,"output_tokens":2720,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1372},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5159,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2720,"cache_read_input_tokens":213666,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5159,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5159},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgEkBrUjtx32KV4Am2skH","requestRef":"c64ec727-96a6-412d-9d2b-fa1819359019","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a0670f06-a65e-4eb5-9a56-8e0a1ae6e657","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:24:12.755Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"a0670f06-a65e-4eb5-9a56-8e0a1ae6e657","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEkBrs4iFMpvpC91xhi2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GfEYDWCp6ZRaRLS6cc5qoh","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304\\src\\components\\liquidGlassShape.ts","content":"// An element's box, in the canvas's CSS pixels, with its border radii in CSS\n// order: top-left, top-right, bottom-right, bottom-left.\nexport type ShapeBox = {\n  x: number;\n  y: number;\n  width: number;\n  height: number;\n  radii: [number, number, number, number];\n};\n\nexport type GlassShape = { x: number; y: number; width: number; height: number; radius: number };\n\n// liquid-dom glass has one corner radius. A side whose corners are square (the\n// edge tab's flat side against the frame) is pushed out past the canvas by that\n// radius, so its rounded corners fall outside and get clipped.\nexport function glassShape(box: ShapeBox, canvasWidth: number, canvasHeight: number): GlassShape | null {\n  const [topLeft, topRight, bottomRight, bottomLeft] = box.radii;\n  const radius = Math.min(Math.max(...box.radii), box.width / 2, box.height / 2);\n  let { x, y, width, height } = box;\n  if (radius > 0) {\n    if (topLeft === 0 && bottomLeft === 0) {\n      x -= radius;\n      width += radius;\n    }\n    if (topRight === 0 && bottomRight === 0) width += radius;\n    if (topLeft === 0 && topRight === 0) {\n      y -= radius;\n      height += radius;\n    }\n    if (bottomLeft === 0 && bottomRight === 0) height += radius;\n  }\n  if (x >= canvasWidth || y >= canvasHeight || x + width <= 0 || y + height <= 0) return null;\n  return { x, y, width, height, radius };\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5159,"cache_read_input_tokens":213666,"output_tokens":2720,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1372},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5159,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2720,"cache_read_input_tokens":213666,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5159,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5159},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01GfEYDWCp6ZRaRLS6cc5qoh":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304\\src\\components\\liquidGlassShape.ts","content":"// An element's box, in the canvas's CSS pixels, with its border radii in CSS\n// order: top-left, top-right, bottom-right, bottom-left.\nexport type ShapeBox = {\n  x: number;\n  y: number;\n  width: number;\n  height: number;\n  radii: [number, number, number, number];\n};\n\nexport type GlassShape = { x: number; y: number; width: number; height: number; radius: number };\n\n// liquid-dom glass has one corner radius. A side whose corners are square (the\n// edge tab's flat side against the frame) is pushed out past the canvas by that\n// radius, so its rounded corners fall outside and get clipped.\nexport function glassShape(box: ShapeBox, canvasWidth: number, canvasHeight: number): GlassShape | null {\n  const [topLeft, topRight, bottomRight, bottomLeft] = box.radii;\n  const radius = Math.min(Math.max(...box.radii), box.width / 2, box.height / 2);\n  let { x, y, width, height } = box;\n  if (radius > 0) {\n    if (topLeft === 0 && bottomLeft === 0) {\n      x -= radius;\n      width += radius;\n    }\n    if (topRight === 0 && bottomRight === 0) width += radius;\n    if (topLeft === 0 && topRight === 0) {\n      y -= radius;\n      height += radius;\n    }\n    if (bottomLeft === 0 && bottomRight === 0) height += radius;\n  }\n  if (x >= canvasWidth || y >= canvasHeight || x + width <= 0 || y + height <= 0) return null;\n  return { x, y, width, height, radius };\n}\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgEkBrUjtx32KV4Am2skH","requestRef":"c64ec727-96a6-412d-9d2b-fa1819359019","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"536eed94-46ba-45e7-bf0d-9d3f702d5b11","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:24:16.435Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
