{"parentUuid":"8f4470d4-d6ce-43eb-b020-33a5f7ed7e22","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304\\src\\components\\liquidGlassShape.ts","snippet":"8\t  radii: [number, number, number, number];\n9\t};\n10\t\n11\texport type GlassShape = { x: number; y: number; width: number; height: number; radius: number };\n12\t\n13\t// liquid-dom glass has one corner radius. A side whose corners are square (the\n14\t// edge tab's flat side against the frame) is pushed out past the canvas by that\n15\t// radius, so its rounded corners fall outside and get clipped.\n16\texport function glassShape(\n17\t  box: ShapeBox,\n18\t  canvasWidth: number,\n19\t  canvasHeight: number,\n20\t): GlassShape | null {\n21\t  const [topLeft, topRight, bottomRight, bottomLeft] = box.radii;\n22\t  const radius = Math.min(Math.max(...box.radii), box.width / 2, box.height / 2);\n23\t  let { x, y, width, height } = box;\n24\t  if (radius > 0) {\n25\t    if (topLeft === 0 && bottomLeft === 0) {\n26\t      x -= radius;\n27\t      width += radius;\n28\t    }"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1775a905-e10b-44c5-85a1-b85b91e923de","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:24:51.714Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304\\src\\components\\liquidGlassShape.ts changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n8\t  radii: [number, number, number, number];\n9\t};\n10\t\n11\texport type GlassShape = { x: number; y: number; width: number; height: number; radius: number };\n12\t\n13\t// liquid-dom glass has one corner radius. A side whose corners are square (the\n14\t// edge tab's flat side against the frame) is pushed out past the canvas by that\n15\t// rad