{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"e02d1f89fd5c80c24fa3107be40f739a703e4d944fe89bea1a0bd6dde4c0b910","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Writing layout CSS...\n\nRight, so in the 780 breakpoint the toolbar sits at 42px (12+30), so I'll set `--library-top: 42px` there. Padding transitions still work fine since vars driving computed padding still animate, though the scroll position itself jumps at breakpoint changes which is acceptable. Writing library-scroll positioning styles...\n\nI also need to verify z-index layering: stage at 0, edge fade at 1, capture bar at 2, so the fade sits above the stage but under the bar, and the stage itself likely needs default pointer-events since it covers the padded main area beneath the capture bar.\n\nFor the liquid glass styling, I'm removing the border, background, shadow, and backdrop-filter so the surface renders through to the canvas layer below, while keeping an outer shadow specifically for the zoom pill lens case.\n\n`.glass` is defined at the end of App.css, so I'll add this block right after it.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I'll update the CSS: moving main's padding into variables, positioning the scroller absolutely for consistent layout, styling the stage and canvas, and disabling CSS glass once liquid glass renders its first frame.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BD62qHJyjAakV1B5cYzFiC","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && python - <<'EOF'\nimport io\np='src/App.css'\ns=io.open(p,encoding='utf-8',newline='').read()\ndef rep(old,new,count=1):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)==count, (old, s.count(old))\n    s=s.replace(old,new)\nrep('''.main-content {\n  width: auto;\n  height: 100vh;\n  min-width: 0;\n  min-height: 0;\n  flex: 1 1 auto;\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  padding: calc(4px + var(--titlebar-height)) 14px 30px;\n  position: relative;''','''.main-content {\n  --main-pad-top: calc(4px + var(--titlebar-height));\n  --main-pad-x: 14px;\n  --main-pad-bottom: 30px;\n  /* Where the toolbar row starts; the library scroller starts here too. */\n  --library-top: var(--main-pad-top);\n  --stage-background: var(--paper);\n  width: auto;\n  height: 100vh;\n  min-width: 0;\n  min-height: 0;\n  flex: 1 1 auto;\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  padding: var(--main-pad-top) var(--main-pad-x) var(--main-pad-bottom);\n  position: relative;''')\nrep('''  .main-content {\n    border: 1px solid var(--library-border);\n    border-right: 0;\n    border-radius: var(--frame-radius) 0 0 var(--frame-radius);\n    background: var(--library-frame);\n  }''','''  .main-content {\n    --stage-background: var(--library-frame);\n    border: 1px solid var(--library-border);\n    border-right: 0;\n    border-radius: var(--frame-radius) 0 0 var(--frame-radius);\n    background: var(--library-frame);\n  }''')\nrep('''  .main-content {\n    padding-inline: 14px;\n    width: calc(100vw - var(--sidebar-width));\n  }''','''  .main-content {\n    width: calc(100vw - var(--sidebar-width));\n  }''')\nrep('''  .main-content {\n    width: 100%;\n    padding: 12px 18px 24px;\n    transition: none;\n  }''','''  .main-content {\n    --main-pad-top: 12px;\n    --main-pad-x: 18px;\n    --main-pad-bottom: 24px;\n    /* Below the 30px library-header padding. */\n    --library-top: 42px;\n    width: 100%;\n    transition: none;\n  }''')\nrep('''.library-scroll {\n  flex: 1 1 auto;\n  min-height: 0;\n  overflow: hidden;\n  position: relative;\n  scrollbar-width: none;\n  -ms-overflow-style: none;\n  margin-top: -52px;\n}\n/* Paper 1.3: the 44px filter row and the grid's 4px top padding put the first\n   card 100px below the toolbar's top. The -52px pull-up above cancels the\n   52px toolbar, so the pinned offset is 100 - 52. */\n.library-scroll.has-pinned-query {\n  margin-top: 48px;\n}''','''/* The stage covers the frame under the toolbar. It holds the library scroller\n   and, with liquid glass, the canvas that draws it (LiquidGlass.tsx). The\n   scroller is placed absolutely so it lands in the same spot either way. */\n.library-stage,\n.library-stage > .liquid-glass-content {\n  position: absolute;\n  inset: 0;\n  z-index: 0;\n}\n.library-stage > .liquid-glass-content,\n.library-stage .liquid-glass-content {\n  background: var(--stage-background);\n}\n.library-scroll {\n  position: absolute;\n  top: var(--library-top);\n  right: var(--main-pad-x);\n  bottom: var(--main-pad-bottom);\n  left: var(--main-pad-x);\n  overflow: hidden;\n  scrollbar-width: none;\n  -ms-overflow-style: none;\n}\n/* Paper 1.3: the 44px filter row and the grid's 4px top padding put the first\n   card 100px below the toolbar's top. */\n.library-scroll.has-pinned-query {\n  top: calc(var(--library-top) + 100px);\n}''')\nrep('''  backdrop-filter: var(--glass-filter);\n}\n''','''  backdrop-filter: var(--glass-filter);\n}\n/* Liquid glass draws this surface on the canvas below, so the element itself\n   goes clear. Set once the canvas has drawn a frame (LiquidGlass.tsx). */\n.glass[data-liquid] {\n  border-color: transparent;\n  background: none;\n  box-shadow: none;\n  backdrop-filter: none;\n}\n.liquid-glass-canvas {\n  position: absolute;\n  inset: 0;\n  display: block;\n  width: 100%;\n  height: 100%;\n}\n.liquid-glass-content {\n  position: absolute;\n  inset: 0;\n}\n''')\nio.open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8',newline='').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"library-header {\" -A 4 src/App.css | head -20","description":"Apply stage and glass CSS changes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
