{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"c486064cc571f34fde1e6dbe33cc980bc52b20ddd738475085cf22bbe107746e","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to figure out the radius cap correctly for an extended edge: since the extension amount itself depends on the radius, I should use the raw max radius to compute the extension first, then cap the final radius against half the extended width and height.\n\nChecking examples: an edge tab with r0=14 gives width 26+14=40, so radius = min(14,20,17) = 14; a pill with r0=999 gives radius = min(999,60,17) = 17. But for unusual shapes with huge r0 and a flat side, extending by 999px would be excessive, so I should also cap the extension radius itself by the minimum of the original box's width and height before using it to extend — applying that to the edge tab case still gives 14, which checks out.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The failing test caught a real bug: the radius was capped before the flat side was pushed out. Fixing it:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018m9a8Qc3V6P199q39um4EA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && python - <<'EOF'\nimport io\np='src/components/liquidGlassShape.ts'\ns=io.open(p,encoding='utf-8',newline='').read()\nold_start=s.index('  const [topLeft, topRight, bottomRight, bottomLeft] = box.radii;')\nold_end=s.index('  if (x >= canvasWidth')\nnew='''  const [topLeft, topRight, bottomRight, bottomLeft] = box.radii;\n  const corner = Math.min(Math.max(...box.radii), box.width, box.height);\n  let { x, y, width, height } = box;\n  if (corner > 0) {\n    if (topLeft === 0 && bottomLeft === 0) {\n      x -= corner;\n      width += corner;\n    }\n    if (topRight === 0 && bottomRight === 0) width += corner;\n    if (topLeft === 0 && topRight === 0) {\n      y -= corner;\n      height += corner;\n    }\n    if (bottomLeft === 0 && bottomRight === 0) height += corner;\n  }\n  const radius = Math.min(corner, width / 2, height / 2);\n'''\ns=s[:old_start]+new+s[old_end:]\nio.open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8',newline='').write(s)\nEOF\nbun test src/components/liquidGlassShape.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Fix radius cap order and rerun tests"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
