{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"d3bf5227c78e0d39df1c8214c42d2be053971d9355d88f1d6ea8528429e60f25","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I notice the npm package hasn't been updated since the fix merged into master, so I'm weighing whether to pull the fix in via a git dependency pointing to the specific commit, though the monorepo/pnpm workspace structure complicates installing just the subpackage that way.\n\nA cleaner option is using `bun patch` against the published 0.1.1 package — I can create a patch that updates the texture copy call sites directly in the compiled dist/index.js to match the new signature, which is minimal, reviewable, and avoids build tooling issues. I just need to check the actual fix commit's diff so the patch mirrors it exactly, focusing only on the signature change rather than other unrelated changes merged since then.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'll look at the fix commit so I can apply it as a bun patch on the published 0.1.1 version, since liquid-dom fixed this on master but never released it to npm.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BrAjFs4jEZWA9rRBzkFEAK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && SHA=$(timeout 30 gh api \"repos/AndrewPrifer/liquid-dom/commits?per_page=12\" --jq '.[] | select(.commit.message | startswith(\"Fix HTML-in-Canvas texture copy signature\")) | .sha') && echo $SHA && timeout 30 gh api \"repos/AndrewPrifer/liquid-dom/commits/$SHA\" --jq '.files[] | \"=== \" + .filename + \"\\n\" + (.patch // \"\")' | head -150","description":"Show the upstream signature fix diff"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
