{"parentUuid":"843c36d2-1d04-4b42-a958-46b41af72596","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01ToX3iq5JSpwVQJY2i8DW1P","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ed11cf1d-b7e4-44b4-aea5-0700babf6eba","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:27:56.078Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"ed11cf1d-b7e4-44b4-aea5-0700babf6eba","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEkTinLZQ4W5t8K6wa6c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm also confirming the patches folder isn't needed at runtime since Vite bundles everything, and that CI's frozen-lockfile install applies patches correctly regardless of electron-builder's files config. For the feature check, verifying the new API signature exists should be sufficient, and I'm planning for future Electron API changes by catching InvalidStateError or TypeError appropriately.\n\nBut the bigger risk is a silent failure mode where the canvas stays black and the library content effectively disappears if the copy throws unexpectedly. I need a safety net: detecting when no successful frame copy has occurred after a threshold — either a paint-count limit or a timeout (say 1500ms) from mount — and falling back to CSS rendering, marking the feature as unsupported so it doesn't keep retrying. There's a brief visibility gap during that fallback window, but that's acceptable for a failure path. A cleaner approach might be probing the API at support-check time with a hidden canvas and a tiny texture copy to confirm it actually works before committing to the GPU path.\n\nI'm now trying to figure out how to make that probe reliable — the probed element needs to actually get painted by the browser for the snapshot to succeed, so hiding it via opacity or clip-path risks the browser skipping the paint as an optimization, which would make the probe falsely fail.\n\nI realize the DOM ordering is the problem: the canvas gets inserted after the content in the wrapper, so it sits on top and would cover the visible grid during probing, causing a black flash. I need to figure out whether making the canvas invisible until ready actually prevents this, or whether visibility changes affect what gets painted for the copy probe.\n\nSimplifying the approach: I'll create a dedicated hidden probe canvas fixed to the body, positioned off behind everything with negative z-index so it's covered by the app shell's background but still gets painted. Wait for that paint event, try copying into a 1x1 texture, and if it throws no exception, mark support as true — then remove the probe canvas. This only costs one extra frame at startup.\n\nOther failure modes like a mid-session device loss are already handled separately by device.lost, so I don't need to add a watchdog here — the probe just needs to check the API signature once.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2497,"cache_read_input_tokens":249824,"output_tokens":1932,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1796},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2497,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1932,"cache_read_input_tokens":249824,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2497,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2497},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":23391,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEkTiKZTj7WuaoVL5H7y","requestRef":"b2dc2066-b060-42be-868e-4afcae3f1b10","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"02034a0b-1948-4173-9da3-5db4e94f3a40","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:27:56.076Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-g